ge\">So the <a href=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/033/719/333/a611c9833e4c6bda581f50da71a75761_original.jpg?ixlib=rb-4.0.2&amp;w=700&amp;fit=max&amp;v=1622481827&amp;auto=format&amp;frame=1&amp;q=92&amp;s=13277b8008909ecb6f3c62a371e335b9\" target=\"_blank\">Summer Caste mark</a> sure looks like to be the astrological symbol of the asteroid Pallas. With that in mind, my money is on the other three being Juno (Spring), Vesta (Winter), and Ceres (Autumn).<br /> <br /> OBSERVE:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://78.media.tumblr.com/6567913d897408c3c2d27e7513bf42de/tumblr_owpsfcLq6n1w1119eo1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>According to Discord this is actually indeed the case. Though which symbol to which season hasn't been confirmed yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T16:58:41-07:00","id":1450519,"title":"","content":"So, I wasn't expecting Getimians to all be Bond villains with an endless supply of minions, but I don't know why I wasn't.<br /> <br /> Infected Fate is all kinds of great; it's both a fun mechanic and ties very well into the Getimian thematic as Fantasy SPECTRE/noble rebels against a crooked Heaven. And pretty much confirms my idea for an Immaculate Getimian I drafted works, I just need to decide if he is Spring or Summer.<br /> <br /> (In his world, he was the strongest mortal link in a Wyld Hunt that broke apart a corrupt god's pyramid scheme, only to wake up to discover that god ensured the Hunt never even discovered his scheme, let alone marched against it - and then Rakan Thulio told him the whole truth. He now wants to reform the Philosophy into one that is not slaved to the Realm, and more importantly scrubbed of Bronze Faction influence - and if we were still having Motivations, his initial one would be &quot;Punch Chejop Kejack in the face&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T18:25:48-07:00","id":1450526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450495#post1450495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today's sneak peek were the first pieces of mechanics I've seen on Getimians at all. It's interesting that they get bonuses from the current size of their mote pools. Given that other Exalts have been getting their Essence in bonuses, that suggests something about the relative size of mote pools in ExE, and gives some perspective on how difficult and risky it might be to activate an Iconic Anima effect.<br /> <br /> Very eager to see the base system and the full basic Exalt types tomorrow!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, this might just be the mechanics guy in me talking, but with regards to mote pools, you can have either Still or Flowing higher <i>and</i> be Balanced can\u2019t you? (Since Balanced is within 1)<br /> <br /> I.e. if you are jiggering it right, you can have the one success bonus on 2/3 of all possible rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T18:46:39-07:00","id":1450530,"title":"","content":"Liking the new preview. And thinking I can use it for an idea I've been trying to make work...&gt;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 06-01-2021, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T23:06:14-07:00","id":1450547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450526#post1450526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, this might just be the mechanics guy in me talking, but with regards to mote pools, you can have either Still or Flowing higher <i>and</i> be Balanced can\u2019t you? (Since Balanced is within 1)<br /> <br /> I.e. if you are jiggering it right, you can have the one success bonus on 2/3 of all possible rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see what you mean. I read &quot;higher&quot; to mean &quot;not balanced&quot;, but your reading is possible too. We'll see what the full text says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T01:34:10-07:00","id":1450551,"title":"","content":"So, apparently there is some amazing super city god (god of the very concept of cities, maybe?) who has enough strength they can afford to somewhat regularly give bits of it out to gods of lesser cities who want to raise up an exigent but are worried about being able to pay the cost. Thats an interesting dynamic I hadn't thought of, more powerful gods eating part of the cost without actually taking over control of the exaltation from a weaker god. Maybe I've been too harshly cynical in my estimations of the average asshole level of major gods in this setting if they can refrain themselves like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T01:48:26-07:00","id":1450552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450551#post1450551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, apparently there is some amazing super city god (god of the very concept of cities, maybe?) who has enough strength they can afford to somewhat regularly give bits of it out to gods of lesser cities who want to raise up an exigent but are worried about being able to pay the cost. Thats an interesting dynamic I hadn't thought of, more powerful gods eating part of the cost without actually taking over control of the exaltation from a weaker god. Maybe I've been too harshly cynical in my estimations of the average asshole level of major gods in this setting if they can refrain themselves like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Delegation is an essential (some would say the most essential) skill for the establishment of settlements of any considerable size, historically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T02:13:27-07:00","id":1450554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450551#post1450551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, apparently there is some amazing super city god (god of the very concept of cities, maybe?) who has enough strength they can afford to somewhat regularly give bits of it out to gods of lesser cities who want to raise up an exigent but are worried about being able to pay the cost. Thats an interesting dynamic I hadn't thought of, more powerful gods eating part of the cost without actually taking over control of the exaltation from a weaker god. Maybe I've been too harshly cynical in my estimations of the average asshole level of major gods in this setting if they can refrain themselves like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wun Ja has been the goddess of cities sicne 1e. But yeah, that's the gist going on basically. THey split the burden to make it you know, not melt the lower guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name"