put type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://78.media.tumblr.com/6567913d897408c3c2d27e7513bf42de/tumblr_owpsfcLq6n1w1119eo1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>God that works so well with how I\u2019ve been picturing Zen Mu...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T02:54:48-07:00","id":1450557,"title":"","content":"That manuscript preview came out early in the day! Yay!<br /> <br /> Some first reactions as I read.<br /> <br /> Moonsilver tattoos aren't listed as an Advantage, but just kind of mentioned in a sidebar. But they clearly are an advantage against Wyld influence. Seems inconsistent.<br /> <br /> I love how the Lunar Passive Anima effects are so god damn casual. No Moon's like, I live in your house, what you gonna do, you can't see me!<br /> <br /> Sidereals are really scary, just knowing shit about you for free. I love it.<br /> <br /> So, an Alchemical can choose a community to devote themselves to, but in order to not tie them down to a single place, that community can be stuff like &quot;orphaned children&quot;. I have issues with that idea of community, particularly as trust and personal relationships seem so important to the rest of the Alchemical kit. &quot;Orphaned children&quot; sounds more like a cause or ideological devotion to me, rather than a community. Hm.<br /> <br /> The new Infernals. I'm torn. On the one hand, the 2e structure was burdensome and sidestepped a lot of the basic design space the rest of the game used. On the other, they were one of the hypest things about 2e at the back end of the system's life. It's much too early to tell without Charms, of course, but I really hope they don't turn out into &quot;Solars, but ANGERY.&quot;<br /> <br /> A whole lot of <i>iconoclasts</i> among the Exalted. Mh, yes.<br /> <br /> Yo, Liminals, though? I'm very pleasantly surprised. Overall, I'm not a big Abyssal fan, and I was less than interested in another death themed Exalt. What I'm seeing here is really doing it for me, though. Love the grounded, emotion-based descriptions.<br /> <br /> Saving the rest for later. Overall, really cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 06-01-2021, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T03:23:12-07:00","id":1450558,"title":"","content":"I went into 3rd edition not really wanting a lot of new toys, but, man... Getimians is such a rad concept! Instead of just being antagonists you can use in that Sidereal game you will probably never run anyway, they add something rather novel to the game, really opening the door for a lot philosophical debates generally and the many-worlds interpretation specifically.<br /> <br /> But before we get to those debates, I have some more grounded questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Infected Fate: This is awesome, but could I designate a target to have the role of &quot;Victim&quot; in regards to myself?<br /> <br /> 2) If I was a major hero in a different world that never happened, could I have been, say, a Dragon-Blooded Exalt in that reality that never happened? Or would I have to have been a heroic human, you think?<br /> <br /> Now, I am going to close-read the Abyssals, because I have missed them so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T04:41:04-07:00","id":1450572,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of the decision to use the array system for Attributes, without a called-out option to assign dots freely. It's fine for Abilities, simply because there are more of those.<br /> If I run an XS game, I'm going to houserule the shit out of that.<br /> <br /> Also, the different Liminal milestones don't really seem like they have parity.<br /> <br /> Soil and Blood Aspects get unique, flavourful ones, while the Marrow Aspect gets a dry-but functional one. The Breath milestone, though, doesn't seem like it has anything to do with their fluff (contemplative, passive = punish the wicked?), and the Flesh milestone is just a more restrictive Dusk one (the Dusk Caste only has to engage in combat, while the Flesh has to <i>win</i>).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Decomposition reduces the Liminal to a shambling corpse or hungry ghost within one lunar month. They lose another Intimacy per week, and can no longer use Undying. They also decompose cosmetically, per the player\u2019s aesthetic choice. The Liminal can still anchor her Thread of Life to a mortal within this time. If she does, decomposition stops and she heals. Liminals of Essence 3+ may anchor themselves to an Exalt within their Circle, or to another powerful entity. </div> </div> </div> It's kind of unclear, but I <i>think</i> this says you can come back from decomposition even after one month has passed.<br /> Or, at least, I hope it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T09:09:30-07:00","id":1450591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450558#post1450558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) If I was a major hero in a different world that never happened, could I have been, say, a Dragon-Blooded Exalt in that reality that never happened? Or would I have to have been a heroic human, you think?<br /> <br /> Now, I am going to close-read the Abyssals, because I have missed them so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you are supposed to have been a mortal. But I don't see any big issues with saying you used to be a different Exalt type. It's just background (that exists only in your memories).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T09:16:54-07:00","id":1450592,"title":"","content":"I have to say, overall, I'm disappointed.<br /> Character Creation I am mostly very happy with, but I guess that's the easiest part to house-rule anyway.<br /> Some of the powers I like and some I don't, but that's kind of subjective. I can play something I like, others can play something they like.<br /> But for a system that's supposed to be simpler and more elegant, well tbh a lot of the anima powers don't seem much simpler than the ones in 3rd ed. Actually some are more complex.<br /> The Milestone system also ends up being more complex than a normal XP system. There's 4 types of milestones that you get at different, variable times, some are in a pool you fill up, two are swappable anyway. It feels more like an alternate system for standard Ex3 than a pared-down, simpler system.<br /> <br /> I thought Essence might be too simple for me, I didn't want something like FATE, but so far it doesn't really seem simpler or more elegant. It is in parts of course, but others are not.<br /> <br /> Hopefully the rules and charms will do the heavy lifting of simplification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T09:28:25-07:00","id":1450594,"title":"","content":"The Lunar passive powers are clever because it makes them narratively powerfull but doesn\u2019t give them an edge with other named characters. Like a rampaging Full Moon npc is unscathed by the the entire city state militia, but that invulnerability doesn\u2019t equate to an advantage against your named PC swordsman facing them (obviously their Charms still can). Very nice genre emulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-01-2021, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T11:24:26-07:00","id":1450616,"title":"","content":"This latest drop is the strongest argument I've seen yet for putting the system stuff BEFORE the character creation!<br /> <br /> You read this as a new player, and you have no clue what half the words mean. Soak? Milestones? Motes? Dice caps? None of this has been explained before you're blasted with a bunch of terms with little or no explanation in character creation. If this is supposed to be an easy-to-digest form of Exalted, then explaining what specialist terms mean before they're used in anger would be much more helpful.<br /> <br /> Also, has the way anima banners work changed? Each caste of each Exalt type seems to have a certain set of themes that they have in their banners, rather than being defined by the players, as they were before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Essence</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ten Sheave sacrificed himself to empower Janest. She is one of a kind, and cannot pass her power on \u2014 and, therefore, one of the Celestial Exalted. Had she been one of many Strawmaidens empowered by the harvest deity, she might be Terrestrial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that Dragon-blooded can pass their exaltation on to their children in a way Celestials can't, but the spark from other Celestials can pass on to others. There's either some poor wording here, or some other criteria that determine whether an Exigent is Terrestrial or Celestial. I like the notion of the Terrestrials expanding beyond the Dragon-blooded, but it needs to be far better-defined than this.<br /> <br /> Also, not sure if this is where we should be giving feedback on the content, so apologies if this is the wrong place. If I could be pointed in the correct way, that would be a great help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","user":"Xerxes","date":".  More added to avoid double-posting 06-01-2021, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T13:04:19-07:00","id":1450631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450616#post1450616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This latest drop is the strongest argument I've seen yet for putting the system stuff BEFORE the character creation!<br /> <br /> You read this as a new player, and you have no clue what half the words mean. Soak? Milestones? Motes? Dice caps? None of this has been explained before you're blasted with a bunch of terms with little or no explanation in character creation. If this is supposed to be an easy-to-digest form of Exalted, then explaining what specialist terms mean before they're used in anger would be much more helpful.<br /> <br /> Also, has the way anima banners work changed? Each caste of each Exalt type seems to have a certain set of themes that they have in their banners, rather than being defined by the players, as they were before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I get that Dragon-blooded can pass their exaltation on to their children in a way Celestials can't, but the spark from other Celestials can pass on to others. There's either some poor wording here, or some other criteria that determine whether an Exigent is Terrestrial or Celestial. I like the notion of the Terrestrials expanding beyond the Dragon-blooded, but it needs to be far better-defined than this.<br /> <br /> Also, not sure if this is where we should be giving feedback on the content, so apologies if this is the wrong place. If I could be pointed in the correct way, that would be a great help.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here's the essence feedback sheet <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc0r3huSSsYO1BYedG2QRBvHerxu6z3FOwETDvTt3MnNtpYMQ/viewform\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1F...tpYMQ/viewform</a><br /> <br /> I will mention that I did show off the manuscripts to my roommates and their response to both the first and second manuscript was a mixture of interest and curiosity and the only games they've played were D&amp;D 5E which also puts character classes and race first and a game called Double Cross, I tried to get them into Cofd but time constraints, especially in covid, is kind of a problem for us right now<br /> <br /> Also in regards to Milestones, the dev's already heard about the feedback in discord and plan to fix it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 06-01-2021, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T13:38:00-07:00","id":1450635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450631#post1450631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Here's the essence feedback sheet <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc0r3huSSsYO1BYedG2QRBvHerxu6z3FOwETDvTt3MnNtpYMQ/viewform&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1F...tpYMQ/viewform</a><br /> <br /> I will mention that I did show off the manuscripts to my roommates and their response to both the first and second manuscript was a mixture of interest and curiosity and the only games they've played were D&amp;D 5E which also puts character classes and race first and a game called Double Cross, I tried to get them into Cofd but time constraints, especially in covid, is kind of a problem for us right now<br /> <br /> Also in regards to Milestones, the dev's already heard about the feedback in discord and plan to fix it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The feedback sheet is for typos and &quot;I don't understand this&quot; as opposed to &quot;I don't like this.&quot; Just so people know.<br /> And, tbh, if I don't like stuff, I don't expect them to change it at this point. I don't expect them to go and rewrite the anima powers and milestones to be simpler because a couple of fans disliked it. <br /> <br /> Talking to the Devs, it seems the Milestones section is some kind of mix of a current and previous version. I hope that they will put it in the Week 5 complete pdf.<br /> <br /> So I guess I can't really say for sure that I don't like it as I don't understand how it works. From what I have heard, I think I will still feel that it's too complicated for a simple game, but it would be unfair to say it now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T13:41:10-07:00","id":1450636,"title":"","content":"I don't think putting character gen first is a big issue in a book because you can skip ahead. Though obviously you can't do that here.<br /> <br /> Milestones is in this section though. Well, a previous version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T14:22:54-07:00","id":1450640,"title":"","content":"Hello guys, I have been out of the loop when it comes to Exalted and the forums for quite a while now and just saw that Exalted Essence is in development. I tried to read up on the information available but still, some things seem unclear to me.<br /> <br /> What exactly is the degree of compatibility between 3rd and Essence?<br /> Can I take my 3rd edition characters and just use them with Essence rules or vice versa? Is some tweaking needed? If yes will there be a guide to import charms from one to the other like there was for Requiem and Masquerade back in the day? What about future supplements? Will they use Essence rules or 3rd edition rules?<br /> <br /> Can someone explain it to me like I am stupid? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T14:32:46-07:00","id":1450642,"title":"","content":"You'll probably need to do some changing, but it will probably be less than going between WoD and CofD. However, the conversion rules are in the appendix, and that will be released late in the Kickstarter campaign. We also haven't gotten the system chapter yet. So, it's hard to answer your question with any real authority.<br /> <br /> ETA: 3rd edition is still the main ruleset, and future Exalted supplements will support it. Essence is a one-off with a companion book or two generated from the Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T14:41:28-07:00","id":1450643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450640#post1450640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello guys, I have been out of the loop when it comes to Exalted and the forums for quite a while now and just saw that Exalted Essence is in development. I tried to read up on the information available but still, some things seem unclear to me.<br /> <br /> What exactly is the degree of compatibility between 3rd and Essence?<br /> Can I take my 3rd edition characters and just use them with Essence rules or vice versa? Is some tweaking needed? If yes will there be a guide to import charms from one to the other like there was for Requiem and Masquerade back in the day? What about future supplements? Will they use Essence rules or 3rd edition rules?<br /> <br /> Can someone explain it to me like I am stupid? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its a different ruleset, though it's the 3rd edition setting, so all 3rd edition books present and future will continue to be useful if you're running on the Essence rules. As far as we know there isn't currently a formal translation guide for characters, but it really shouldn't be hard to write up an equivalent character with the other ruleset.<br /> <br /> Currently we don't know about anything that will add more Essence rules beyond the Essence core, and the Companion that is being built with stretchgoals - hence it being good that we are getting all 10 canon Exalted types up front in Essence. The answer when it was asked about future cool charms in 3E books without Essence equivalents getting Essence translations was &quot;Essence Charms are so easy to write up, you'll be able to do it yourself&quot;. But it would not surprise me, if we see some future sidebars and such in later 3E books with &quot;here's this thing's Essence stats&quot; or &quot;Here's how to use it in Essence&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T17:12:32-07:00","id":1450651,"title":"","content":"I haven't actually thought about Exalted in years, not since the 3e Kickstarter basically ruined it, but I am taking the chance on Exalted Essence and so far it looks really cool. The chapter that was just posted today has a very interesting design for things. Character creation is also interesting, and I am glad for the various pool of points options for attributes, abilities, and merits. So yeah its looking good and I am eagerly awaiting more material about it. <br /> <br /> It also has me looking up some of my old material and some of it could easily be brought back and such. (Not everything, just somethings, hehe)<br /> <br /> So yeah, this whole project is very cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T18:50:54-07:00","id":1450656,"title":"","content":"Pretty stoked about this. I briefly tried running a 3rd edition game not long after the core book dropped, but the system was too crunchy and people didn't have fun keeping track of all the moving pieces. I think more basic systems like 5th edition D&amp;D really got them spoiled. So I'm looking forward to seeing how much less bookkeeping is required and if it's a decent amount less I'll be running my first Exalted campaign in close to a decade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T23:23:53-07:00","id":1450666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450616#post1450616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This latest drop is the strongest argument I've seen yet for putting the system stuff BEFORE the character creation!<br /> There's either some poor wording here, or some other criteria that determine whether an Exigent is Terrestrial or Celestial. I like the notion of the Terrestrials expanding beyond the Dragon-blooded, but it needs to be far better-defined than this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why it's not clearly defined is because Exigents are Build-an-Exalt. (Like Build-a-Bear but with awesome custom powers.) Some are going to be Terrestrial caliber and some are going to be Celestial caliber and some are going to be between those two somewhere. As I understand it, the Exigent is as powerful as the power the god was able to put into their Exalt. So I'm guessing the only real criteria is going to be &quot;what you and your ST hash out.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, our one example is Janest. How would you compare her to other Exalts? Terrestrial or Celestial? Ten Sheaves was a minor god of harvest and had to sacrifice themself to Exalt her. A lesser god compared to Ten Sheaves would have a less powerful Exalt. Edited to Add: But it could be that a more powerful god could put less effort into it and have a less powerful Exalt as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","name":"Ariketh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T00:59:08-07:00","id":1450673,"title":"","content":"So I'm noticing a pattern: Solar, Abyssal, and Infernal anima powers that mimic each other tend to be weaker or more restrictive in the hands of the latter two, for no good reason.<br /> I think most of these are due to certain developments and changes not being implemented properly, but it's a bad look.<br /> <br /> Let's go through them:<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Warrior</b>/<b>Death is Inevitable</b>/<b>Font of War: </b>Dawns and Azimuths kill (Essence) extras per turn without a roll, while Dusk Castes can only kill one. Additionally, while Dusks gain a guaranteed success on decisive damage, Dawns/Azimuths gain +(Essence) damage dice against battle groups and a +(Essence) difficulty increase to their rout checks. However, Supernal Warrior applies this increase automatically, while Font of War has to build it over time for each individual battle group by successfully damaging them.<br /> <br /> <b>Fearsome Visage</b>/<b>Terrifying Visage:</b> The Azimuth power is just weaker, lacking the gambit cost reduction of Fearsome Visage; unlikely to be anything but an oversight. The Abyssal <b>Fear Made Flesh</b> is similar in purpose but works entirely differently, so I'm not going to try to compare it the Fearsome Visage.<br /> <br /> <b>All Eyes Upon Me</b>/<b>Shake Off Your Chains: </b>As above, Shake Off Your Chains is just All Eyes Upon Me with the secondary benefit (a situational dice bonus) filed off. The Ascendant power doesn't specify it has to be &quot;reasonable,&quot; though. Also as above, the Abyssal equivalent is too different to compare.<br /> <br /> <b>Purity of Purpose</b>/<b>Apocalyptic Voice</b>/<b>Laws of Hell:</b> Zeniths get (Essence) automatic successes to Presence and Performance rolls, while the other two gain an equivalent bonus to social influence using any Ability, but each to a specific purpose. However, Zeniths also casually annihilate undead extras, and deal bonus damage to undead battle groups.<br /> <br /> <b>Joyous Pursuit</b>/<b>Knowledge at All Costs:</b> These are identical, but Twilights get a more significant difficulty reduction than Horizon Castes. Chalk this one up to a very understandable oversight.<br /> <br /> <b>Indefatigable Genius</b>/<b>Underworldly Lore</b>/<b>Principles of Hierarchy: </b>All three are identical, except that the Daybreak's Focus Will bonus only applies to necromancy where the other two get the (I assume) broader &quot;spellcasting.&quot; And that is wack.<br /> <br /> <b>No One Special</b>/<b>Walking in Daylight</b>/<b>Subtle Enemy:</b> These are all worded differently, but are essentially the same. Subtle Enemy can technically dampen iconic animas, which is clearly a typo, while Walking in Daylight gets an additional air-breathing mermaid bonus (which, honestly, Day Castes do need).<br /> <br /> <b>Cloak of Shadows</b>/<b>Grim Caul</b>/<b>Death\u2019s Shadow:</b> Grim Caul only provides its bonus to Stealth instead of both Stealth and Athletics. Meanwhile, Death's Shadow automatically hides from Extras, which the other two can't. Definitely typos/minor errors on both counts.<br /> <br /> <b>Universal Scholar</b>/<b>God of the Ashes</b>/<b>Fiend to All Nations:</b> All identical, except that the Penumbra Caste can't learn Charms from celestial gods. This is clearly deliberate for flavour reasons, though, so I won't complain.<br /> <br /> <b>Esteemed Guest</b>/<b>Speaker for the Dead</b>/<b>Dealbreaker:</b> The Eclipse and Moonshadow powers look like the same effect at different stages of development, with the former having a clear mechanical effect where the latter leaves it up to the ST. The Penumbra variant is also not grounded in the mechanics, but it has a unique social power to compensate.<br /> <br /> Now, having been negative for most of this post, here are some cool things I noticed while writing it:<br /> Towering Demon Emperor is rad (why ever play a non-Azimuth Infernal?). Corona of Fury pushes you to flagrant displays of your unlimited power, which is cool. Horizon Castes can steal the sorcery right out of your hands. Day Castes at iconic turn into cool ghosts. The Greater Sign of Mars is the best thing in the preview.<br /> <br /> I would have liked it if the Greater Sign of Saturn was more like <a href=\"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Gods_of_Peg%C4%81na#The_Deeds_of_Mung_(Lord_of_all_Deaths_between_Peg%C4%81na_and_the_Rim)\" target=\"_blank\">the sign of Mung</a>, but I'll take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-02-2021, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T02:42:35-07:00","id":1450674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450592#post1450592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, overall, I'm disappointed.<br /> Character Creation I am mostly very happy with, but I guess that's the easiest part to house-rule anyway.<br /> Some of the powers I like and some I don't, but that's kind of subjective. I can play something I like, others can play something they like.<br /> But for a system that's supposed to be simpler and more elegant, well tbh a lot of the anima powers don't seem much simpler than the ones in 3rd ed. Actually some are more complex.<br /> The Milestone system also ends up being more complex than a normal XP system. There's 4 types of milestones that you get at different, variable times, some are in a pool you fill up, two are swappable anyway. It feels more like an alternate system for standard Ex3 than a pared-down, simpler system.<br /> <br /> I thought Essence might be too simple for me, I didn't want something like FATE, but so far it doesn't really seem simpler or more elegant. It is in parts of course, but others are not.<br /> <br /> Hopefully the rules and charms will do the heavy lifting of simplification.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same impression with the Milestone, and apparently other people as well. <br /> <br /> I think most Anima powers are much better designed than in the Core, can you mention some than you find more complex ? (I haven't read them all to be honest)<br /> <br /> My personal thingy is I would have liked 1 or 2 more attributes (9 is too much, but I feel 3 is a bit short). The Abilities seem good to me.<br /> <br /> I'm very not clear on what is the deal with Infernals thematically, though. They seem agents of chaos and revolution, but for some kind of a &quot;better Creation&quot; (overthrowing tyrants, rebelling against unjust authority). I'm not sure on how this fits in &quot;I'm chosen by mad imprisonned Titans to avenge them&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T02:46:15-07:00","id":1450675,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar97_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"97\" data-vbnamecard=\"97\">The MG</a> Do you think the difference could possibly be explained by the &quot;Solars are always a slight bit ahead of everyone&quot; theme ? Most differences seem minor, or with restriction on non-Solar due to &quot;Fluff/thematic&quot; reasons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T03:01:39-07:00","id":1450677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450675#post1450675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar97_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"97\" data-vbnamecard=\"97\">The MG</a> Do you think the difference could possibly be explained by the &quot;Solars are always a slight bit ahead of everyone&quot; theme ? Most differences seem minor, or with restriction on non-Solar due to &quot;Fluff/thematic&quot; reasons</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean, sure, but that's <i>bad</i>. Being slightly ahead of everyone is already the totality of their Exalted Advantages: always winning ties, free excellencies, and universal Resonance; they don't need any more of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T03:15:26-07:00","id":1450678,"title":"","content":"I do love No Gods, No Masters giving Agg damage vs those loyal to heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T04:59:07-07:00","id":1450679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450674#post1450674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very not clear on what is the deal with Infernals thematically, though. They seem agents of chaos and revolution, but for some kind of a &quot;better Creation&quot; (overthrowing tyrants, rebelling against unjust authority). I'm not sure on how this fits in &quot;I'm chosen by mad imprisonned Titans to avenge them&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I read them as expressions of resentment, as agents intended to overthrow the status quo regardless of whether that\u2019s strategically viable. They\u2019re Lawgivers in the sense that they have the power to make and enforce laws, but stripped of the Heavenly veneer that humans associate with justice and legitimacy. And because the Infernal Exaltation always chooses people who feel oppressed or betrayed, it will always be a phenomenon that challenges the status quo, not for the sake of chaos, but because there will always be injustice.<br /> <br /> Put another way, the Solar Exaltation posits that justice is possible and should be sought. The Infernal Exaltation posits that injustice is real and must be fought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 06-02-2021, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T08:29:44-07:00","id":1450687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450642#post1450642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll probably need to do some changing, but it will probably be less than going between WoD and CofD. However, the conversion rules are in the appendix, and that will be released late in the Kickstarter campaign. We also haven't gotten the system chapter yet. So, it's hard to answer your question with any real authority.<br /> <br /> ETA: 3rd edition is still the main ruleset, and future Exalted supplements will support it. Essence is a one-off with a companion book or two generated from the Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450643#post1450643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Its a different ruleset, though it's the 3rd edition setting, so all 3rd edition books present and future will continue to be useful if you're running on the Essence rules. As far as we know there isn't currently a formal translation guide for characters, but it really shouldn't be hard to write up an equivalent character with the other ruleset.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Currently we don't know about anything that will add more Essence rules beyond the Essence core, and the Companion that is being built with stretchgoals - hence it being good that we are getting all 10 canon Exalted types up front in Essence. The answer when it was asked about future cool charms in 3E books without Essence equivalents getting Essence translations was &quot;Essence Charms are so easy to write up, you'll be able to do it yourself&quot;. But it would not surprise me, if we see some future sidebars and such in later 3E books with &quot;here's this thing's Essence stats&quot; or &quot;Here's how to use it in Essence&quot;.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Alright!! Thanks guys!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T12:08:34-07:00","id":1450712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450674#post1450674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm very not clear on what is the deal with Infernals thematically, though. They seem agents of chaos and revolution, but for some kind of a &amp;quot;better Creation&amp;quot; (overthrowing tyrants, rebelling against unjust authority). I'm not sure on how this fits in &amp;quot;I'm chosen by mad imprisonned Titans to avenge them&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I read this a bit, and I don't get it. Seems like this is one of the most obvious internal links to me.<br /> <br /> Soon-To-Be-Infernal: Oh Dragons, everything hurts. Is this all there is to life? Is this how the world should be?<br /> <br /> Malfeas: HELLO. I'M THE MUTILATED KING OF THE PEOPLE WHO ARE SUPPOSED TO BE IN CHARGE OF EVERYTHING, AND NO, IT REALLY ISN'T. THE GODS WHO ABANDONED YOU STABBED YOU IN THE BACK AND ARE EVIL URSURPERS WHO STOLE THE THRONE AWAY FROM THE RIGHTFUL RULERS, IE US, AND THE WORLD SUCKS BECAUSE OF IT. PUT US BACK IN CHARGE OR INHERIT THE THRONE, AND EVERYTHING WILL BE BETTER. HERE, HAVE THE POTENTIAL TO DO SO AND A GIANT KAIJU FORM.<br /> <br /> Green Sun Prince: Wow, sweet! Can I punch in the faces of everyone who helped make the world suck more?<br /> <br /> Malfeas: PROTIP: YOU DON'T NEED TO ASK MY PERMISSION FOR THAT. GO GET'EM, CHAMP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T12:29:33-07:00","id":1450716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450674#post1450674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very not clear on what is the deal with Infernals thematically, though. They seem agents of chaos and revolution, but for some kind of a &quot;better Creation&quot; (overthrowing tyrants, rebelling against unjust authority). I'm not sure on how this fits in &quot;I'm chosen by mad imprisonned Titans to avenge them&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You can move the dial from avenging legitimate grievances to smashing everything out of spite depending on how much you want any given Infernal to be influenced by the Yozis. At the most sympathetic end of the spectrum, the Yozis get an Exalted champion capable of empathizing with the betrayal they experienced at the hands of the gods. At the least sympathetic end, they get an Exalted champion who can exact their hate-fueled vengeance on the world and cast down the Heavens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T12:43:49-07:00","id":1450721,"title":"","content":"Also if they keep one thing from 2e Infernals I hope its the possibility to say &quot;beep that!&quot; to the Yozi's and go do your own quest for a better world. Which looks pretty likely given that &quot;Anarchist&quot; is an explicitly endorsed character idea and no anarchist would be interested in putting the Yozi's back in charge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T12:51:59-07:00","id":1450722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450712#post1450712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read this a bit, and I don't get it. Seems like this is one of the most obvious internal links to me.<br /> <br /> Soon-To-Be-Infernal: Oh Dragons, everything hurts. Is this all there is to life? Is this how the world should be?<br /> <br /> Malfeas: HELLO. I'M THE MUTILATED KING OF THE PEOPLE WHO ARE SUPPOSED TO BE IN CHARGE OF EVERYTHING, AND NO, IT REALLY ISN'T. THE GODS WHO ABANDONED YOU STABBED YOU IN THE BACK AND ARE EVIL URSURPERS WHO STOLE THE THRONE AWAY FROM THE RIGHTFUL RULERS, IE US, AND THE WORLD SUCKS BECAUSE OF IT. PUT US BACK IN CHARGE OR INHERIT THE THRONE, AND EVERYTHING WILL BE BETTER. HERE, HAVE THE POTENTIAL TO DO SO AND A GIANT KAIJU FORM.<br /> <br /> Green Sun Prince: Wow, sweet! Can I punch in the faces of everyone who helped make the world suck more?<br /> <br /> Malfeas: PROTIP: YOU DON'T NEED TO ASK MY PERMISSION FOR THAT. GO GET'EM, CHAMP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that creating a better world and exerting the order of the Yozis seem incompatible to me. I cant imagine a former slave, modeled by &quot;No one shall live in chains of masters&quot;, deciding to reinstaure the order of the Yozis, which was probably very oppressive","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T13:18:27-07:00","id":1450725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450722#post1450722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that creating a better world and exerting the order of the Yozis seem incompatible to me. I cant imagine a former slave, modeled by &quot;No one shall live in chains of masters&quot;, deciding to reinstaure the order of the Yozis, which was probably very oppressive</div> </div> </div> </div>The irony is intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T13:33:39-07:00","id":1450728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450722#post1450722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that creating a better world and exerting the order of the Yozis seem incompatible to me. I cant imagine a former slave, modeled by &amp;quot;No one shall live in chains of masters&amp;quot;, deciding to reinstaure the order of the Yozis, which was probably very oppressive</div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming the Infernal knows that.<br /> <br /> Hell, most demons probably don't know that, or at least, don't understand that.<br /> <br /> As noted, out of universe, it's an irony. In-universe, it's not just a good recruitment tactic, it's a really dangerous and effective lie, because both the hearer wants to believe it, and the teller honestly thinks it's true, just leaving out the specifics for later. It's the kind of thing a cult recruiter does; find broken people and give them something to rebuild around. Just showing sympathy and rewards is a good way to get the Infernal eating out of the Yozis' hands.<br /> <br /> This also has an inherent arc to it - the crushing realization that leaders they trusted were just as bad, and having to end up developing a healthier meaning on their own. This is not a bug. Hell, it reminds me of Megami Tensei 2 (no Shin), where the game ends up being a really good story because of how it gradually reveals your mentor is not trustworthy - and how your friend and teammate just shuts down rather than believe someone who gave him hope is this conniving treacherous ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T19:28:16-07:00","id":1450767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1449971#post1449971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you zoom in, it looks like a straight X layered over/under a four pointed star, too.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/7Vopxta.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I was right! He's an Azimuth Caste. &quot;Their Caste Marks are an unholy sunburst with eight rays, with the larger diagonal cross rays emphasizing a center without a circle.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T19:47:34-07:00","id":1450770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450712#post1450712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read this a bit, and I don't get it. Seems like this is one of the most obvious internal links to me.<br /> <br /> Soon-To-Be-Infernal: Oh Dragons, everything hurts. Is this all there is to life? Is this how the world should be?<br /> <br /> Malfeas: HELLO. I'M THE MUTILATED KING OF THE PEOPLE WHO ARE SUPPOSED TO BE IN CHARGE OF EVERYTHING, AND NO, IT REALLY ISN'T. THE GODS WHO ABANDONED YOU STABBED YOU IN THE BACK AND ARE EVIL URSURPERS WHO STOLE THE THRONE AWAY FROM THE RIGHTFUL RULERS, IE US, AND THE WORLD SUCKS BECAUSE OF IT. PUT US BACK IN CHARGE OR INHERIT THE THRONE, AND EVERYTHING WILL BE BETTER. HERE, HAVE THE POTENTIAL TO DO SO AND A GIANT KAIJU FORM.<br /> <br /> Green Sun Prince: Wow, sweet! Can I punch in the faces of everyone who helped make the world suck more?<br /> <br /> Malfeas: PROTIP: YOU DON'T NEED TO ASK MY PERMISSION FOR THAT. GO GET'EM, CHAMP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve always liked the angle of \u201cThe Yozis are never, ever going to escape, but they can sure as Malfeas make sure THEIR GUY/GAL is in charge, which is a decent second option.\u201d<br /> <br /> (The Inherit the Throne option mentioned above). Imagine what influence on the mortal plane an Empire run by a Malfeas friendly Infernal would give the Yozis.<br /> <br /> (That\u2019s an interesting Infernal goal, make a Kingdom where demons and Creation-born can live together in harmony and prosperity)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 06-02-2021, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T21:53:22-07:00","id":1450778,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, it's really superior to 2E where increasingly, as it became plain the Yozi's were probably going to get out, that more or less devoured every other storyline. <br /> <br /> On another question-- we get new chapters at the beginning of the week, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T23:40:26-07:00","id":1450785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450778#post1450778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I mean, it's really superior to 2E where increasingly, as it became plain the Yozi's were probably going to get out, that more or less devoured every other storyline.<br /> <br /> On another question-- we get new chapters at the beginning of the week, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually Tuesday, but the Charms chapter will be different, released in parts from June 13th (Sunday) to June 19th (Saturday).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T01:03:50-07:00","id":1450789,"title":"","content":"The thing to remember about 3e is that Reclamation isn't a thing in 3e the Yozis know that they aren't getting out of their king's body no matter what and have come to terms with that to them I think the worst betrayal is accepting the infernal exaltation and doing absolutely nothing with it something that many would hate and not just the titans that exalted you. To them, I think the infernals are the Yozis angry reminder that they are still there and they want heaven to know that they created this angry fireball cursing out the realm and its slavery as well as the heavens that allowed them to go hurting people for so long.<br /> <br /> Winning to the Yozis is basically when an Infernal change the world for better or worst cause it reminds everyone that they are still there able to influence people beyond just simple demon summoning. I think a win for the Yozis is destroying every slave den in an entire direction just as destroying house Mnemon counts as a victory because it was caused by their powers and no one else's.<br /> <br /> Also here's a dev quote that works really well to me when I think about creating infernal characters.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Yozis gave you this power in a moment of genuine sympathy AND because they want you to fuck over the people they hate, not because they love you and care deeply about your struggles. What do you do with that power? How are you seen by others? What comes next, when the prince has been torn down and your demon friends have driven the slavers from the streets? That\u2019s all part of it. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T03:12:56-07:00","id":1450793,"title":"","content":"The Yozi really just want you to make Creation look like a Heavy Metal Album cover, everything else is details and details never really interested them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T05:58:11-07:00","id":1450805,"title":"","content":"For me the beauty of the Infernals is that, regardless of the real intention of the one behind their exaltation, they are a living embodiment of the failures of creation, and that makes a lot of people very uncomfortable. Whoever takes the time to actually know their story can't say with a good conscience that they don't have a point or don't have a right to their anger, the world is a flawed place filled with a flawed system that hurts a lot of innocent people.<br /> Now, whether the infernals become heroic rebels that tear down the corruption of heaven and earth or creatures of destruction consumed by their resentment, that's entirely up to each infernal. In the end, being an infernal in its best aspect is about rebellion against injustice, while on it's worst is about pure destruction out of spite. That's why for me, Solars exist to build a new world while Infernals exist to tear down the old one, with the morality of their actions resting on each individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 06-03-2021, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T08:36:46-07:00","id":1450825,"title":"","content":"Well I didn't expect such good introspection from many different people but I'm glad that happened so thanks for your answers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T10:04:05-07:00","id":1450840,"title":"","content":"The descriptor that has been given to them on the podcasts at least was &quot;Shaken soda can&quot;. As in the sense that the Yozis shook the fucking hell out of that can and threw it as hard into the crowd as possible. What it does after that point is really neither under their control or to their interests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T11:04:28-07:00","id":1450854,"title":"","content":"What do we know about character creation? What are the attributes and abilities, and how do we a lot them? Has the character sheet been revealed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T11:17:10-07:00","id":1450855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wingnut2292</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450854#post1450854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do we know about character creation? What are the attributes and abilities, and how do we a lot them? Has the character sheet been revealed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The chargen chapter, including the list of pretty much all traits save Charms, is currently one of the sections in the Backer preview manuscript. So basically everything.<br /> <br /> Attributes: Finesse, Force, Fortitude<br /> Abilities: Atheletics, Awareness, Close Combat, Craft, Embassy, Integrity, Navigate, Performance, Physique, Presence, Ranged Combat, Sagacity, Stealth, War<br /> <br /> Attributes, Abilities, and Merits are assigned in arrays. Options to distribute Abilities and Merits via point-buy are given. A fan character sheet is floatinga round but isn't final.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T11:18:38-07:00","id":1450857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wingnut2292</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450854#post1450854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do we know about character creation? What are the attributes and abilities, and how do we a lot them? Has the character sheet been revealed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Three attributes, Force, Finesse and Fortitude, rated between 1 and 5. Assign a 4, a 3 and a 2 between them. Which one you use depends on your approach to an action, unless a specific one is specified.<br /> <br /> 14 abilities, Awareness, Athletics, Close Combat, Craft, Embassy, Integrity, Navigate, Performance, Physique, Presence, Ranged Combat, Sagacity, Stealth, and War, rated between 1 and 5. Assign one 5, one 4, three 3s, two 2s, and one 1 between them.<br /> <br /> For the social system, there's Intimacies and Virtues (Ambition, Compassion, Courage, Discipline, Justice, Loyalty, and Wonder).<br /> <br /> There's also Merits.<br /> <br /> Character sheets haven't been shown, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 06-03-2021, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T13:18:28-07:00","id":1450872,"title":"","content":"Infernals just got a lot more interesting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T13:54:00-07:00","id":1450881,"title":"","content":"Personally I was very drawn to the old (<i>old</i>) Kickstarter preview's &quot;decadent sorcerer-kings&quot; schtick for the Infernals, so I'm hoping this Angry Solars vibe XS has going is just the more accessible half of their pitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T15:42:03-07:00","id":1450887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450881#post1450881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I was very drawn to the old (<i>old</i>) Kickstarter preview's &quot;decadent sorcerer-kings&quot; schtick for the Infernals, so I'm hoping this Angry Solars vibe XS has going is just the more accessible half of their pitch.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels to me that the designers for 3E and Essance have really been going for &quot;there are no hard walls here&quot; kwhen you're coming up with your character. Which honestly is good, because the universe in which you can't get a Solar, Lunar, Dragonblood, Infernal and Sideral, stick them in a magic green van and have them go and solve mysteries with their intelligence and mystic kung-fu isn't a universe I want to live in . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T16:53:09-07:00","id":1450892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450857#post1450857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">14 abilities, Awareness, Athletics, Close Combat, Craft, Embassy, Integrity, Navigate, Performance, Physique, Presence, Ranged Combat, Sagacity, Stealth, and War, rated between 1 and 5. Assign one 5, one 4, three 3s, two 2s, and one 1 between them.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's three 2s, actually. The sidebar on spending dots freely accounts the total as 25, which would require another 2, and the quick summary on p. 57 says you get three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T23:22:22-07:00","id":1450918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450892#post1450892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it's three 2s, actually. The sidebar on spending dots freely accounts the total as 25, which would require another 2, and the quick summary on p. 57 says you get three.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I spotted that too, and flagged it as a typo in the form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T07:14:00-07:00","id":1450954,"title":"","content":"I've read that it's the sidebar and quick summary that are in error, but I'm not certain of that. Clarity later probably!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T11:12:50-07:00","id":1450971,"title":"","content":"I'm incredibly excited for Essence (and these more-detailed looks at Getimians and new!Infernals do not disappoint!), but I do have a few concerns at this (admittedly early) date, which aren't objective enough for for errata, but really don't seem right to me.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450594#post1450594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar passive powers are clever because it makes them narratively powerfull but doesn\u2019t give them an edge with other named characters. Like a rampaging Full Moon npc is unscathed by the the entire city state militia, but that invulnerability doesn\u2019t equate to an advantage against your named PC swordsman facing them (obviously their Charms still can). Very nice genre emulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little less thrilled about this.Full Moons only get a milestone for defeating a significant foe in single combat, then their anima is focused on tearing through weak trash. I'm not even sure whether it's good at that job, since the Solar/Azimuth passive implies that Battle Groups are not &quot;Extras,&quot; so a Full Moon might still take damage from that militia. But even if the ability is good for the one thing it does, it looks like Essence is following 3E's example of making Full Moons better at styling on trivial threats (which almost everyone is good at, by definition), then giving a different Lunar caste the defense buff which is far more valuable in serious fights - amusingly, it switched from No Moon to Changing, meaning that anyone has a better shot at optimal combat powers than the combat Lunars. That's silly.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the contradiction in Full Moon milestones, a lot of these milestone conditions seem like they'd be wildly different difficulties to get in play, which I really hope is not the actual goal. A Full Moon Lunar needs to win in a specific type of fight, but a Dawn only needs to fight at all? I've hardly ever had an RPG session where you couldn't argue that the PCs &quot;took an action toward<br /> furthering a long-term goal,&quot; (Air Aspect), but you need a much more specific setup to learn &quot;story-important&quot; secrets for your Marrow Aspect, and Breath/Soulsteel Milestones are almost literally &quot;you get one for picking an argument with the GM after the session.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lawyering rather than roleplaying is also my biggest worry with the Alchemicals' Community Spirit. Design any ability, then pick a &quot;group&quot; as broadly as possible, in the hopes that you always have it. It seem unnecessary to invite all of that trouble, when Living Artifact already does a great job of underscoring the Alchemical themes of community through logistics while still respecting the practicalities of many PC groups. A second trait aimed at representing their unusual bodies and souls could avoid the whole thing without hurting their core identity.<br /> <br /> It's Exalted, so we obviously can't get through a round of mechanics without super seduction powers. Since it's inevitable, I do appreciate that they gave them to <i>horrifying Frankenstein Japanese Ghosts</i>, to at least keep things surreal.<br /> <br /> Sidereal Anima powers buffing your allies feels like an even stronger statement of purpose here than usual, given the multi-splat focus, and I love it. However, I do wish they all felt like buffs which multiple party members would actually want. Journeys (movement), Secrets (stealth, though only for scouting/spying), and Endings (noticing danger <i>and</i> trying to talk people down) are all good examples of this, but Battles and Serenity need help. War and Craft are some of the canonical examples of Abilities that one person is using while everyone else sits on their hands, and I'd love to see those Chosen get to provide the same kind of support to their whole playgroup that the other three enjoy.<br /> <br /> Also, I really hope that when we see the system mechanics, I can piece together some kind of theory for why 4/5 Sidereals &quot;transform her Essence in dice to automatic successes&quot; on relevant rolls, but Journeys lets people &quot;add the Sidereal\u2019s Essence in dice any time they would need to roll&quot;. I know just enough from teasers to see a few slight differences, but the effects are so similar that I'm mystified by the choice to not simply choose a template and stick to it. Though that's obviously nothing new to Exalted.<br /> <br /> There are also a few abilities where I am genuinely not sure what they do. Can Laws Of A New Creation remove people's belief in object permanence? Can an Untouchable Changing Moon do things like tear people in half or say &quot;I am the Devil Empress&quot; in perfect Seatongue, and still have significant characters be incapable or responding to them as anything save a normal squirrel? Does the Sidereal choose the location Greater Sign of Mercury teleports people to, and the &quot;safe location of the Storyteller's choice&quot; just keeps people from telefragging, or does the Sidereal just decide &quot;teleport these people somewhere,&quot; and the destination is up to the ST? Inevitably, those are some of my favorite abilities in the entire preview, but past experience tells me that a lot of people will have their own intuition on those questions without even questioning it, and if those people reach different answers and then play together, it could get awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T16:36:58-07:00","id":1450994,"title":"","content":"Minor quibble - why is the Navigate Ability titled as a verb when all the other Abilities are nouns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T20:26:22-07:00","id":1451008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450971#post1450971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lawyering rather than roleplaying is also my biggest worry with the Alchemicals' Community Spirit. Design any ability, then pick a &quot;group&quot; as broadly as possible, in the hopes that you always have it. It seem unnecessary to invite all of that trouble, when Living Artifact already does a great job of underscoring the Alchemical themes of community through logistics while still respecting the practicalities of many PC groups. A second trait aimed at representing their unusual bodies and souls could avoid the whole thing without hurting their core identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I was surprised that the Alchemicals didn't get a trait like the Abyssals, all of the good things about being a robot with (almost) none of the bad. Allowing them to not have to breath or eat would be a good &quot;advantage&quot; to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T21:15:24-07:00","id":1451011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450971#post1450971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I really hope that when we see the system mechanics, I can piece together some kind of theory for why 4/5 Sidereals &quot;transform her Essence in dice to automatic successes&quot; on relevant rolls, but Journeys lets people &quot;add the Sidereal\u2019s Essence in dice any time they would need to roll&quot;. I know just enough from teasers to see a few slight differences, but the effects are so similar that I'm mystified by the choice to not simply choose a template and stick to it. Though that's obviously nothing new to Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I feel like it's probably for the same reason that Chosen of Secrets have a Greater Sign of Secrets instead of a Greater Sign of Jupiter - this isn't the final revision, and sometimes things just slip through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T06:32:55-07:00","id":1451046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElOhTeeBee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451011#post1451011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I feel like it's probably for the same reason that Chosen of Secrets have a Greater Sign of Secrets instead of a Greater Sign of Jupiter - this isn't the final revision, and sometimes things just slip through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you're right!<br /> <br /> A large part of my confusion here is that I don't have a good handle on how to distinguish a mistake (which I'd report to them) from a choice I don't understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T08:46:32-07:00","id":1451054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450971#post1450971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also a few abilities where I am genuinely not sure what they do. Can Laws Of A New Creation remove people's belief in object permanence? Can an Untouchable Changing Moon do things like tear people in half or say &quot;I am the Devil Empress&quot; in perfect Seatongue, and still have significant characters be incapable or responding to them as anything save a normal squirrel? Does the Sidereal choose the location Greater Sign of Mercury teleports people to, and the &quot;safe location of the Storyteller's choice&quot; just keeps people from telefragging, or does the Sidereal just decide &quot;teleport these people somewhere,&quot; and the destination is up to the ST? Inevitably, those are some of my favorite abilities in the entire preview, but past experience tells me that a lot of people will have their own intuition on those questions without even questioning it, and if those people reach different answers and then play together, it could get awkward.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Laws of A New Creation at least, I think you can change peoples belief into thinking object permancence is a taboo topic. That does not make object permance not real or factual, so all that will do is give them some penalties as they try to work around not mentioning the taboo topic while still reacting to how the real world actually functions. Sounds like a fun RP challenge, but not really very useful beside that. In addition, there are still rules for unacceptable influence and things like that which will stop the worst potential problems.<br /> <br /> I think some of these potential problems will just be up to the table to decide.Trying to prevent rules lawyering in roleplaying games is a futile endevour, especially in a game with lighter rules. Any charm or power more complicated than adding or subtracting dice will get rules laywered by a certain kind of player, and limiting design to account for that would be a mistake.<br /> I have had games with people that are willfully obtous if it can get them an advantage, to the degree that they argue that they can fly and phase to walls because the rules for a movement actions said &quot;move at Speed in any direction&quot;. Those kind of players or STs either have to be reigned in at the table or just not included in the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1228-jhiriit","name":"Jhiriit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T09:09:56-07:00","id":1451057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jhiriit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451054#post1451054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Laws of A New Creation at least, I think you can change peoples belief into thinking object permancence is a taboo topic. That does not make object permance not real or factual, so all that will do is give them some penalties as they try to work around not mentioning the taboo topic while still reacting to how the real world actually functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would really appreciate a rule book giving me at least a hint of what &quot;some penalties&quot; might entail.<br /> <br /> I'm a pretty cynical person, so in the short term, I don't think any one's belief has a lot of impact on what people actually do - once a lynch mob is formed, no longer believing in the arguments for its creation doesn't matter, because people also don't want to look bad, or to have others turn on them. (Or, for a more relatable example, nobody has to honestly <i>believe</i> that &quot;the customer is always right&quot; to keep acting like it's true due to social pressure.) So in my mind, eliminating a belief in a small area for a single scene does roughly nothing, because beliefs only matter over the long term of shaping behaviors. But this is an Iconic ability, and I assume the writers have different intuition than my own, if they would only share it with the class.<br /> <br /> Conversely, you can also make a <i>behavior</i> taboo, but I don't even know what qualifies. &quot;Hitting people&quot; is definitely a behavior, as is &quot;talking,&quot; but this ability &quot;cannot force characters to stop making attacks or social influence actions,&quot; so those don't count. What about holding weapons? Breathing? Probably not.<br /> <br /> When I look at this ability and consider using it against, say, &quot;a soldier's duty is to obey the chain of command,&quot; that might: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Automatically disperse any organized army which can see the Winter.</li> <li>Grant a minor bonus on social influence actions to change the views of soldiers within fifty feet or so.</li> <li>Do anything in between.</li> </ol><br /> I know people will think I'm being willfully obtuse, but I am not. I do not know the authorial intent. I do not have a strong guess. I do not think that all of the people who think the meaning is &quot;obvious&quot; actually agree with each other. I do not think it's unreasonable to expect rules, which exist to give us some shared expectations in a game of make believe, to provide some context for these questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T09:44:28-07:00","id":1451062,"title":"","content":"On a more positive note, I was highly skeptical of pre-defined Virtues returning, but today's preview looks really smart. The virtues are broad enough that very few gameable characters won't be able to find a pair that fit them, they encourage players to find larger drives for their PCs than selfishness or apathy (a trap I've seen a lot of really good roleplayers fall into accidentally), and the need to link Intimacies to virtues looks like a deliberate attempt to fix one of the biggest critiques of 3E social influence.<br /> <br /> Building up a suite of shallow Intimacies to justify them as supporting each other (&quot;you like oranges, and my pet monkey can bring you oranges&quot;) doesn't make a lot of sense when the only Intimacies the game tracks are ones tied to a character's primary drives. We'll need to see the social system to know how that all shakes out, but I like what I see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 06-05-2021, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T11:03:16-07:00","id":1451068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Up-to-Eleven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450721#post1450721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if they keep one thing from 2e Infernals I hope its the possibility to say &quot;beep that!&quot; to the Yozi's and go do your own quest for a better world. Which looks pretty likely given that &quot;Anarchist&quot; is an explicitly endorsed character idea and no anarchist would be interested in putting the Yozi's back in charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, they're Exalted. Nobody can command the Exalted. That's why they were created.<br /> <br /> You can pretend you can command them, you can trick them into thinking they can be commanded, but nobody can actually bend the Exalted to their will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:32:51-07:00","id":1451137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElOhTeeBee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1450994#post1450994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor quibble - why is the Navigate Ability titled as a verb when all the other Abilities are nouns?</div> </div> </div> </div>People asked, it's just coincidence. There wasn't any particular aim to make them all nouns or verbs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:37:01-07:00","id":1451138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451008#post1451008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I was surprised that the Alchemicals didn't get a trait like the Abyssals, all of the good things about being a robot with (almost) none of the bad. Allowing them to not have to breath or eat would be a good &amp;quot;advantage&amp;quot; to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will be honest, the Alchemicals had my least-liked Advantages, I would have preferred that. Plus I think it makes even more sense for golems than the living dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T19:06:36-07:00","id":1451175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451046#post1451046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope you're right!<br /> <br /> A large part of my confusion here is that I don't have a good handle on how to distinguish a mistake (which I'd report to them) from a choice I don't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who knows a whole heck of a lot about Exalted, a choice *you* don't understand is still a mistake, just one of clarity rather than content. I'd report them just the same and let the writers sort it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T20:03:17-07:00","id":1451176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451057#post1451057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a pretty cynical person, so in the short term, I don't think any one's belief has a lot of impact on what people actually do - once a lynch mob is formed, no longer believing in the arguments for its creation doesn't matter, because people also don't want to look bad, or to have others turn on them. (Or, for a more relatable example, nobody has to honestly <i>believe</i> that &amp;quot;the customer is always right&amp;quot; to keep acting like it's true due to social pressure.) So in my mind, eliminating a belief in a small area for a single scene does roughly nothing, because beliefs only matter over the long term of shaping behaviors. But this is an Iconic ability, and I assume the writers have different intuition than my own, if they would only share it with the class.<br /> <br /> Conversely, you can also make a <i>behavior</i> taboo, but I don't even know what qualifies. &amp;quot;Hitting people&amp;quot; is definitely a behavior, as is &amp;quot;talking,&amp;quot; but this ability &amp;quot;cannot force characters to stop making attacks or social influence actions,&amp;quot; so those don't count. What about holding weapons? Breathing? Probably not.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I may well have comparable levels of cynicism; maybe the difference is how much a *taboo* can impact behavior?<br /> <br /> Like, if &quot;breathing&quot; were taboo, people wouldn't stop breathing, but they might wear scarves or masks so no one sees them doing it? And maybe they generally avoid heavy exertion in public because that would mean *heavy* breathing, which is harder to conceal?It's not like bodily functions being taboo is anything new.<br /> <br /> Attacking someone may be taboo, but if I'm in the middle of a fight I'm not going to not do it? I'm just going to be a bit more reluctant, probably somewhat embarassed about doing it, maybe talk to my priest about it later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T21:58:01-07:00","id":1451179,"title":"","content":"I have to say, seeing that the default ability allocation is 5/4/3/3/3/2/2/2/1 and then no bonus points is good. No more every twilight crafter having melee 5 just because why not it's so easy.<br /> <br /> I also think that taking Supernal out of the game was a good idea, especially combined with not just reintroducing buying Essence 5 from chargen. Now you can actually have the kind of progression where you don't have the ability to start out suplexing incarna unless you specifically want to start the game higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 06-07-2021, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T06:32:06-07:00","id":1451199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451179#post1451179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, seeing that the default ability allocation is 5/4/3/3/3/2/2/2/1 and then no bonus points is good. No more every twilight crafter having melee 5 just because why not it's so easy.<br /> <br /> I also think that taking Supernal out of the game was a good idea, especially combined with not just reintroducing buying Essence 5 from chargen. Now you can actually have the kind of progression where you don't have the ability to start out suplexing incarna unless you specifically want to start the game higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly think Supernal should be removed from the Core, the only thing it does is make the game a nightmare for ST's","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T06:43:30-07:00","id":1451201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451175#post1451175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who knows a whole heck of a lot about Exalted, a choice *you* don't understand is still a mistake, just one of clarity rather than content. I'd report them just the same and let the writers sort it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really nice of you to say!<br /> <br /> Still the Discord has some pretty strongly-worded posts discouraging just sending in feedback reports willy-nilly. I'll at least wait until I've read the full text to send in anything more borderline like that. See also: whether the Alchemical dice adders (and Lesser Sign of Mercury) mean that all the other bonus dice effects count against &quot;the cap,&quot; whether Shifting Moon's Reserve can provide a bonus to attacks rolls (a final insult to poor Full Moon abilities), and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451176#post1451176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and I may well have comparable levels of cynicism; maybe the difference is how much a *taboo* can impact behavior?<br /> <br /> Like, if &quot;breathing&quot; were taboo, people wouldn't stop breathing, but they might wear scarves or masks so no one sees them doing it? And maybe they generally avoid heavy exertion in public because that would mean *heavy* breathing, which is harder to conceal?It's not like bodily functions being taboo is anything new.<br /> <br /> Attacking someone may be taboo, but if I'm in the middle of a fight I'm not going to not do it? I'm just going to be a bit more reluctant, probably somewhat embarassed about doing it, maybe talk to my priest about it later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plausible! I'd still appreciate actual guidelines for the penalties in question, though. In fact, as an example of how vaguely LoaNC is written, it hadn't previously occurred to me that it might &quot;just&quot; make people awkward about doing the thing, rather than mentally or physically incapable (unless they make the hardest roll in the preview).<br /> <br /> It makes sense. That is what a taboo means in real life. But when the actual text says that something <i>cannot</i> be done, italics in the original, my impulse was to read it as an absolute prohibition. Which just gets to the core of my issue with vagueness here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451179#post1451179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that taking Supernal out of the game was a good idea, especially combined with not just reintroducing buying Essence 5 from chargen. Now you can actually have the kind of progression where you don't have the ability to start out suplexing incarna unless you specifically want to start the game higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal abilities were a powerful statement about the setting, and really the only form of niche protection that Solars got, so I think they were a good idea. But I, also, am encouraged by the thought that Essence may not need them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T09:19:33-07:00","id":1451219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451201#post1451201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal abilities were a powerful statement about the setting, and really the only form of niche protection that Solars got, so I think they were a good idea. But I, also, am encouraged by the thought that Essence may not need them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly succeeded at that, and it fixed the Dawn problem to boot, but in retrospect I'm not sure if it was necessary. It's not like Solars aren't both more powerful and faster progressing than the other exalt types without Supernal. Because you could buy Essence with bonus points in 2e, and especially once the Scroll of Heroes added gaining bonus BP with flaws, Exalted hasn't really had a progression since 1e, unless you intentionally held yourself back really hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T09:52:50-07:00","id":1451228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451179#post1451179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, seeing that the default ability allocation is 5/4/3/3/3/2/2/2/1 and then no bonus points is good. No more every twilight crafter having melee 5 just because why not it's so easy.<br /> <br /> I also think that taking Supernal out of the game was a good idea, especially combined with not just reintroducing buying Essence 5 from chargen. Now you can actually have the kind of progression where you don't have the ability to start out suplexing incarna unless you specifically want to start the game higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure it\u2019s 5/4/3/3/3/2/2/1.<br /> <br /> I asked on the Discord and Monica seemed to be saying that 25 points was a typo and it\u2019s supposed to be 23.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T10:25:47-07:00","id":1451233,"title":"","content":"That would also track with the note that there will be six Abilities left at 0 dots.<br /> <br /> &quot;Abilities.&quot; Not to be mistaken for Exalt Advantages and/or Anima Effects, both called &quot;special abilities&quot; multiple times, whilst the first sentence of the Abilities heading calls <i>them </i>&quot;skills&quot;. Sometimes, the strange nomenclature someone chose three decades ago works out, and sometimes this happens.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451219#post1451219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It certainly succeeded at that, and it fixed the Dawn problem to boot, but in retrospect I'm not sure if it was necessary. It's not like Solars aren't both more powerful and faster progressing than the other exalt types without Supernal. Because you could buy Essence with bonus points in 2e, and especially once the Scroll of Heroes added gaining bonus BP with flaws, Exalted hasn't really had a progression since 1e, unless you intentionally held yourself back really hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, buying up Essence at chargen was bad for BP/XP economy back in 2E, so I mostly saw people try to start with all the Essence 1-2 Charms they wanted, then immediately mainline Essence to unlock the fancy toys. But I take your point. 3E deliberately locked Essence progression to overall character power, then immediately unlocked that same link for the game's flagship (and, for a long time, only) splat, and that does feel odd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T23:42:19-07:00","id":1451285,"title":"","content":"There is something I'm not sure yet and this is how &quot;First Among Equals&quot; is good ? I'm pretty sure in my 3 years of playing Exalted 3e, I've rad very rare occurence of equality on opposed tests. This seems to be not too bad for Defense (I guess if you are playing a Solar, someone must surpass your Defense and not only match it), but I feel this looks like something good on paper but not very useful in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T01:43:19-07:00","id":1451291,"title":"","content":"I see it occasionally, but the main thing is that there's then arguments about who is the defender, who had the best stunt, etc.<br /> <br /> But it depends on the system: how many opposed rolls are there? In ex3 combat, there's control rolls, clashes and stealth rolls and that's it. In social influence there's hardly any. Does ExEss use more? Less?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T01:44:46-07:00","id":1451292,"title":"","content":"I will say Chausse, if it means you have to overcome a Solar's defence instead of equaling it that's amazing. But I doubt that it applies to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T01:47:54-07:00","id":1451293,"title":"","content":"Then I'm curious to see how it goes, from my experience in 3e it doesn't sound very useful but maybe the soon-to-be-previewed system will show something interesting for ExEss.<br /> <br /> I'd be surprised if it doesn't apply to Defense, the text doesn't suggest any kind of roll, but only a &quot;tie&quot;, which seems appropriate in an attack vs. defense scenario","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T01:48:09-07:00","id":1451294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451179#post1451179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, seeing that the default ability allocation is 5/4/3/3/3/2/2/2/1 and then no bonus points is good. No more every twilight crafter having melee 5 just because why not it's so easy.<br /> <br /> I also think that taking Supernal out of the game was a good idea, especially combined with not just reintroducing buying Essence 5 from chargen. Now you can actually have the kind of progression where you don't have the ability to start out suplexing incarna unless you specifically want to start the game higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of things I didn't like in these sections, but character gen looks great. The array should lead to much more sensible characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T03:48:06-07:00","id":1451298,"title":"","content":"I, also, am curious about how much First Among Equals will come up, but I think it might be like Passionate Ideals: a deliberately-mediocre advantage because the other one (whether shapeshifting or unlimited free Excellencies) is so good.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Supremacy of Ability, am I the only one here entertained by how the mechanical expression of Solar &quot;masters of skill&quot; has completely inverted? In 3E, a skilled Solar can generally buy victory in any opposed context, because they have high caps and powerful dice tricks, but they have to be careful about how often they go all-out with those things, since when you pour that many motes into a single roll, your pools evaporate and you end up without enough motes to ensure victory later. In Essence, we don't even know if they have higher caps than DBs, but they do get all the Excellencies they want for free - whether or not they have the most raw power, they can use it all day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T05:56:39-07:00","id":1451301,"title":"","content":"New update! Finally, some payoff for all those Build Power memes.<br /> <br /> What I'm really stuck on is the social influence rules. Those are always tricky, and I really never know at first whether I like a new set. I'm still musing on the implications: Major Virtues/Intimacies are a more powerful thing to work on than Minor, so they cost more to learn, but is that worth the oddness that it's harder to figure something out when a person acts on it more? Or that Read Intentions appears to not even pay lip service to the idea of learning things based on what the target is actually doing at the time? And it looks like, against significant foes, Persuade/Dissuade is really more of a fancy &quot;Aim&quot; action than a social tool: &quot;Leviathan, I demand that you NOT attack this Realm navy! No? Ah, well, at least I get +3 dice on an action of my choice during the fight.&quot; That's might be a good thing - social stuff can often struggle with having no middle ground between &quot;useless&quot; and &quot;utterly dominating&quot; - but it's definitely an <i>odd</i> one, which is why I need a little time to process it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I think it's really odd that if you succeed at a Persuade/Dissuade action with no extra successes, the target can go along with it if they want, or can refuse at no cost. How this is different from failing at the same roll is a mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 06-08-2021, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T06:37:53-07:00","id":1451303,"title":"","content":"I'm still at the beginning of the read, and I must rant about something : <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Sometimes, a success bonus is noted as \u201cautomatic successes.\u201d These are the same thing</span><br /> <br /> <br /> </span> </div> </div> </div>Then just write success bonus. I'm not saying this only for Exalted, but this is very common among OPP and WhiteWolf Games : Why make things clear when you can make them unclear ? This is present in Vampire, Mage, Exalted, etc ... I understand the need to have a pleasant reading prose with varied sentences, but I feel they always come at the cost of clarity of mechanical effects.<br /> <br /> End of rant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T06:43:04-07:00","id":1451304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451298#post1451298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, also, am curious about how much First Among Equals will come up, but I think it might be like Passionate Ideals: a deliberately-mediocre advantage because the other one (whether shapeshifting or unlimited free Excellencies) is so good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually trade First Among Equals for something more narratively driven like &quot;Passionate Ideals&quot; (the first part at least) because it's way more flavourful, and if it's designed to not be awesome mechanically, at least I want it to be cool or say something about the Exalted narratively.<br /> <br /> After reading the rules about ties, which favours PC characters anyway, I'm even more confused by First Among Equals. Am I missing something ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T07:13:05-07:00","id":1451307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451304#post1451304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the rules about ties, which favours PC characters anyway, I'm even more confused by First Among Equals. Am I missing something ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, that did make things more confusing. Especially since Essence is implicitly not designed for PVP.<br /> <br /> In this case, maybe just replace FAE with having a flashlight and a pocketwatch, like Solars do in other editions. Sure, that's not much, but I at least know what it's for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T07:19:09-07:00","id":1451308,"title":"","content":"So I think actually Solars Win, then Defenders Win, and then PCs win. So that's why it's useful for a Solar PC.<br /> <br /> But I think in one place it says Defenders Win and another PCs win? Defenders win I think is correct. Not 100% sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T07:28:17-07:00","id":1451309,"title":"","content":"That is my reading as well, but it still seems pretty narrow for that to actually happen - a tie, and the other party must <i>unambiguously</i> be the &quot;defender,&quot; since if there were any doubt you'd win regardless?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T07:29:13-07:00","id":1451310,"title":"","content":"So I'm about halfway through the rules. And I think they're good?<br /> <br /> Social Influence seems pretty similar but a bit simpler, though I think the way you ignore influence might lead to some arguments. It may be more interesting than &quot;spend 1wp and ignore, except when you can't&quot;. I can see people giving out extra dice to the person trying to convince them a lot because in an entirely social scene, does it matter if they get other dice?<br /> <br /> I think combat will be quicker. The basic idea of how Withering works seems good, and much quicker.<br /> <br /> But honestly, there's a lot of things I just don't quite understand because they're not well explained. And when I hear the writers explain them, it makes other things not make sense. I have been told some of this is versioning issues, but that does make it hard to judge, and without seeing the real version<br /> There's also some things that have been &quot;simplified&quot; but not in a way that I think actually makes things simpler. A lot of the static values for example. That's pretty minor.<br /> <br /> For example, a Lunar, Kovan the Librarian, swipes a demon with his mighty bear paw (Overwhelm 1). The demon has Defence 4. Kovan rolls 5 successes to hit. Does he get 1 power or 2? I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> His ally Fulgens Cruciatus, Dawn Caste warlord, swings his mighty artefact weapon (Overwhelm 3) at the demon. He rolls 5 successes, 1 more than Defence. Does he get 3 power or 4?<br /> <br /> The demon attacks Kovan (Defence 3). It rolls 3. Does he get 1 power or 0?<br /> <br /> Next round, Fulgens attacks again with his artefact weapon but rolls terribly and only get 1 success, missing. Does he get 0 Power? 1 Power? 3?<br /> <br /> I would really like to see the real, current version, because I don't know if that makes everything clear or not.<br /> <br /> Edit: I found the answer to my Decisive question, it seems Decisive attacks are explained in two different places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-08-2021, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T07:30:17-07:00","id":1451311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451309#post1451309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is my reading as well, but it still seems pretty narrow for that to actually happen - a tie, and the other party must <i>unambiguously</i> be the &quot;defender,&quot; since if there were any doubt you'd win regardless?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's definitely the weaker of the two powers.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that's a big issue if Solars are balanced by having better Modes, etc, though. And those free excellencies, which seems very good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T07:44:53-07:00","id":1451313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451311#post1451311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it's definitely the weaker of the two powers.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that's a big issue if Solars are balanced by having better Modes, etc, though. And those free excellencies, which seems very good.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that much a power question to me than a simplicity question. Adding another logical gate to a &quot;Who wins ?&quot; flowchart which already takes 2 entire paragraphs does not seem clear design from my reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T07:47:34-07:00","id":1451314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451310#post1451310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see people giving out extra dice to the person trying to convince them a lot because in an entirely social scene, does it matter if they get other dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly. Persuade and Dissuade are only really meaningful in action scenes, which is what I meant about them being fancy Aim actions.<br /> <br /> Sure, the ST can just have NPCs not refuse very much, but isn't that true <i>without</i> social rules? I share the impulse to merge Essence and WP, but in a case like this, it feels like something ought to take WP's place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, a Lunar, Kovan the Librarian, swipes a demon with his mighty bear paw (Overwhelm 1). The demon has Defence 4. Kovan rolls 5 successes to hit. Does he get 1 power or 2? I'm not sure. </div> </div> </div>I think this is clear: &quot;If the character makes a withering attack, she gains 1 Power for meeting the target\u2019s Defense, and the extra successes are converted directly to Power.&quot; So, 2 Power here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His ally Fulgens Cruciatus, Dawn Caste warlord, swings his mighty artefact weapon (Overwhelm 3) at the demon. He rolls 5 successes, 1 more than Defence. Does he get 3 power or 4? </div> </div> </div>Less clear, since the book suddenly switches from &quot;extra successes&quot; to &quot;attack's successes,&quot; apparently for the same value. As written, I see 4 - I have no idea of the intention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The demon attacks Kovan (Defence 3). It rolls 3. Does he get 1 power or 0? </div> </div> </div>The really big problem. &quot;If she has any left-over successes, then she hits&quot; seems to mean that an attack MISSES if it rolls success equal to the target's Defense. That's... surprising if true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Next round, Fulgens attacks again with his artefact weapon but rolls terribly and only get 1 success, missing. Does he get 0 Power? 1 Power? 3? </div> </div> </div>See above about inconsistent terminology. Are Witherings with a high enough Overwhelming incapable of missing? Probably not the goal, but it would be nice to know for sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: I found the answer to my Decisive question, it seems Decisive attacks are explained in two different places. </div> </div> </div>And so are Withering attacks! I, uh, I really hope that the layout of information in this sections is changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:08:26-07:00","id":1451317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451303#post1451303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why make things clear when you can make them unclear ? This is present in Vampire, Mage, Exalted, etc ... I understand the need to have a pleasant reading prose with varied sentences, but I feel they always come at the cost of clarity of mechanical effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll do you one better:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExEss Preview Manuscript 3, p.35</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each Health Level also has a name: Bruised (0), Injured (-1), and Critical (-2). When an effect refers to \u201cCritical Health level\u201d you know that it<br /> means her -2 Health Levels, and vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>When something says &quot;Critical Health Level,&quot; <i>singular</i>, it could mean any of your -2 Health Levels, <i>plural</i>. Because why make that obvious to anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:10:58-07:00","id":1451318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451314#post1451314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, the ST can just have NPCs not refuse very much, but isn't that true <i>without</i> social rules? I share the impulse to merge Essence and WP, but in a case like this, it feels like something ought to take WP's place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think this is clear: &quot;If the character makes a withering attack, she gains 1 Power for meeting the target\u2019s Defense, and the extra successes are converted directly to Power.&quot; So, 2 Power here. </div> </div> </div> Yes. But... in the example, a character hits a Defence 4 person with 6 successes, so gets 2 Power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The really big problem. &quot;If she has any left-over successes, then she hits&quot; seems to mean that an attack MISSES if it rolls success equal to the target's Defense. That's... surprising if true. </div> </div> </div>And also doesn't fit with &quot;you get 1 Power for equaling the Defence.&quot; I think this is just a mistake.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See above about inconsistent terminology. Are Witherings with a high enough Overwhelming incapable of missing? Probably not the goal, but it would be nice to know for sure.<br /> </div> </div> </div>I think, from what writers said on the Discord, that when you miss you still get your Overwhelming rating. Also all Weapons have at least Overwhelm 1. But then does that mean you can actually get more Power than your successes? (If you roll 0 successes with a normal Overwhelm 1 weapon, for example.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhow. I basically feel that the chapters I have read so far need a good hard editing, but after that will probably be mostly an essentially good Exalted 3.5.<br /> <br /> Which works. I'm not sure it was actually what they were aiming to create though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-08-2021, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:14:33-07:00","id":1451320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451303#post1451303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still at the beginning of the read, and I must rant about something :<br /> <br /> Then just write success bonus. I'm not saying this only for Exalted, but this is very common among OPP and WhiteWolf Games : Why make things clear when you can make them unclear ? This is present in Vampire, Mage, Exalted, etc ... I understand the need to have a pleasant reading prose with varied sentences, but I feel they always come at the cost of clarity of mechanical effects.<br /> <br /> End of rant</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good point.<br /> <br /> Also, I've noted a few times when it's not entirely clear what's mechanics and what's rules, mostly in the Anima banners, which was a big complaint about 3rd ed Core.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:21:31-07:00","id":1451321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451314#post1451314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts exactly. Persuade and Dissuade are only really meaningful in action scenes, which is what I meant about them being fancy Aim actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd nuanced that bit by saying that your statement is true for Dissuade, but nor for Persuade. Persuade seems very akin to the Persuade in 3e, so they have an effect that can last for the entire life of someone, not only for a short scene, contrary to Dissuade who seems more designed for Action Scene","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:40:37-07:00","id":1451322,"title":"","content":"I'm really not sure about the whole three attribute thing. It seems to be reducing things for the sake of reducing things in an area that is not really that complicated. Beyond that the rest of the rules seem cool. I especially like Ventures and the nature of how crafting and social encounters work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:44:21-07:00","id":1451323,"title":"","content":"So is a Trivial Character the same thing as an Extra? The text doesn't really make it clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25545-jollycooperative","name":"jollycooperative","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:49:19-07:00","id":1451324,"title":"","content":"I don't like these teamwork rules, that are the same in a lot of teamwork rules, it just multiplies the number of rolls, and creates some weird times where the aiding character rolls better than the character doing the task (happens even more often in d20 systems), resulting in a strange case where the character doing the task was actually unnecessary. I'd have much preferred a simple static bonus (like +1 or +2 if the aiding has a good score in his ability) rather than the process of rolling a full roll","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:50:38-07:00","id":1451325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451321#post1451321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd nuanced that bit by saying that your statement is true for Dissuade, but nor for Persuade. Persuade seems very akin to the Persuade in 3e, so they have an effect that can last for the entire life of someone, not only for a short scene, contrary to Dissuade who seems more designed for Action Scene</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, assuming that anyone ever follows your influence (or even takes a Hard Bargain). For that matter, a Dissuade with 4 extra successes lasts for a story, which could be pretty significant (&quot;Satrap, you will issue no decrees this season!&quot;) if it worked. But the issue is, that will only happen on the honor system, because outside of an action scene, giving someone else some bonus dice on another roll within the same scene doesn't mean much. I guess they can psychically learn all your Virtues and Intimacies, but Essence seems pretty unfriendly to keeping secrets long-term, anyway.<br /> <br /> And once social influence rolls only matter on the honor system... why have those rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:54:39-07:00","id":1451326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jollycooperative</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451323#post1451323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is a Trivial Character the same thing as an Extra? The text doesn't really make it clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but the difference is explained in the Antagonists chapter which isn't out yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:56:41-07:00","id":1451327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451322#post1451322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really not sure about the whole three attribute thing. It seems to be reducing things for the sake of reducing things in an area that is not really that complicated. Beyond that the rest of the rules seem cool. I especially like Ventures and the nature of how crafting and social encounters work.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, having less attributes (and attributes) only makes things a bit simpler. On the other hand, it's a very easy change to make.<br /> <br /> The way they've done the attributes (Force, Finesse and Fortitude) I think actually doesn't make things simpler. I mean, I don't dislike it, I think you get quite iconic characters, but it feels more like an edition change than a simplification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T08:58:05-07:00","id":1451328,"title":"","content":"Whereas if, say, it was Physical/Social/Mental, that wouldn't be as interesting really, but it would be simpler. (I'm not advocating for that, just making the point that I think Essence isn't really a lot simpler than Exalted Core in many ways.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T09:00:19-07:00","id":1451329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451309#post1451309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is my reading as well, but it still seems pretty narrow for that to actually happen - a tie, and the other party must <i>unambiguously</i> be the &quot;defender,&quot; since if there were any doubt you'd win regardless?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are a few Charms in the current Solar Charmset this in effect replicates note. I know it at least does one of the Dodge ones, and I think some of the success-buyer Charms have dice tricks that look like it. Which is why it seems weak, but at the smae time is covering a notable amount of ground in the main 3e set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T09:05:28-07:00","id":1451332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451325#post1451325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's true, assuming that anyone ever follows your influence (or even takes a Hard Bargain). For that matter, a Dissuade with 4 extra successes lasts for a story, which could be pretty significant (&quot;Satrap, you will issue no decrees this season!&quot;) if it worked. But the issue is, that will only happen on the honor system, because outside of an action scene, giving someone else some bonus dice on another roll within the same scene doesn't mean much. I guess they can psychically learn all your Virtues and Intimacies, but Essence seems pretty unfriendly to keeping secrets long-term, anyway.<br /> <br /> And once social influence rolls only matter on the honor system... why have those rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to argue against your statement, but re-reading this passage of the rules I agree that it's not honestly clear. It feels like straightforward ignoring the influence roll should only fall under the Unacceptable Influence and not have an option to say &quot;Well to some extent yes but actually no, get some dices as a consolation prize&quot;, and the Hard Bargain seems interesting but I feel this is not fully-fledged out and could lead to many frustrations, even used in good faith.<br /> <br /> I clearly like the idea of the system, but I feel like some things are still incomplete.<br /> <br /> For personal use, I'd probably expect any character that was properly persuaded to take some course of action to actually take it, except if the circumstances change drastically. One of my worst frustration ever in Exalted 3e was a player whose character was convinced to take a course of action to say &quot;Well yes but actually no&quot;. I don't want it to happen here, and even less to be supported by the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T09:16:17-07:00","id":1451337,"title":"","content":"I guess that this ultimately comes down to the meaning of &quot;if she feels it is too far out of her character's nature&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's pretty subjective stuff (I would argue moreso than the Decision Points which you mention having a problem with previously), but if there's some kind of table agreement that going &quot;I find this totally unacceptable&quot; is the nuclear option to be used only in the most extreme circumstances (which I suspect was the case for the playtesters), then the system appears to work.<br /> <br /> But if that's the intention, why does the example end with a character doing exactly that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T09:30:20-07:00","id":1451338,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;falling damage&quot; rule have a problem, because it seems to imply than a medium fall (which is equivalent to &quot;conversation must be shouted to be heard&quot;, so probably something along the lines of 15-20 meters or something) is a Difficulty 2 test, which is &quot;below the Exalt station&quot; for rolls. I guess it should be 3 + range bands fall for the difficulty ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T09:54:08-07:00","id":1451341,"title":"","content":"Why are the rules for feats of strength sandwiched between the combat rules and the special-case combat rules (grappling, clashes, difficult terrain)? Why do they refer to a &quot;success requirement,&quot; which apparently isn't Difficulty, but goes unexplained otherwise?<br /> <br /> Why do the naval combat rules go before the action that allows you to transfer Power to another character? Shouldn't that be in the Building Power section?<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a character would take enough damage to bring her to Incapacitated, the player may choose to ignore that damage and take a <b>dramatic injury</b> instead. A dramatic injury introduces a different setback for the character other than injury. </div> </div> </div> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b9/MagrittePipe.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T09:57:42-07:00","id":1451342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451338#post1451338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the &amp;quot;falling damage&amp;quot; rule have a problem, because it seems to imply than a medium fall (which is equivalent to &amp;quot;conversation must be shouted to be heard&amp;quot;, so probably something along the lines of 15-20 meters or something) is a Difficulty 2 test, which is &amp;quot;below the Exalt station&amp;quot; for rolls. I guess it should be 3 + range bands fall for the difficulty ?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the core rules are the rules by which everyone plays and the Exaltes get to break those. So it being a difficulty 2 thing makes sense from a mortal standpoint and then an Exalt gets to look badass. Look at the media that inspires Exalted. &quot;Normal&quot; people will drop a story or two and break a leg or something but the superheroes can fall rather absurd distances and look either badass or mildly inconvenienced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:16:05-07:00","id":1451346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451342#post1451342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the core rules are the rules by which everyone plays and the Exaltes get to break those. So it being a difficulty 2 thing makes sense from a mortal standpoint and then an Exalt gets to look badass. Look at the media that inspires Exalted. &quot;Normal&quot; people will drop a story or two and break a leg or something but the superheroes can fall rather absurd distances and look either badass or mildly inconvenienced.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not an unfair point, but I feel like a Difficulty 3 roll for a &quot;Long fall&quot; (probably 40 or 50 meters) does not feel adequate. <br /> <br /> On a side note, I'm wondering why they decided to keep Withering Attacks. It seems build Power is perfectly suited for Withering Attacks with combat abilities, and would make for a good framework for Combat Charms that use any kind of abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:18:28-07:00","id":1451347,"title":"","content":"That's true, and I VASTLY prefer lowballing fall damage to 3E's highballing of it, but it is kind of a quirk that the roll to negate falling outright, without Charms, will never exceed Difficulty 4. I'm honestly not sure whether that's intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:44:04-07:00","id":1451354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451347#post1451347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true, and I VASTLY prefer lowballing fall damage to 3E's highballing of it, but it is kind of a quirk that the roll to negate falling outright, without Charms, will never exceed Difficulty 4. I'm honestly not sure whether that's intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, in the Old Age the air pressure was greater, so the terminal velocity was lower... yeah, I got nothing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:47:43-07:00","id":1451355,"title":"","content":"&quot;A target\u2019s Defense may never reduce a withering attack\u2019s successes below the character\u2019s Overwhelm value on her weapon.&quot;<br /> <br /> This part confused me alot.<br /> <br /> Does this mean, if i have Overwhelm(3) on my weapon, i can never miss and get 3 power from the attack? That doesn't feel right.<br /> <br /> I really liked the idea of <b>[(attack successes) - (target's defense) +1] power</b>. Seemed easy and fast way to resolve withering attacks. <br /> <br /> I think what they are trying to express is; when you attack first check if you meet that target's defense. If you do; gain power equal to 1+ extra successes on that attack , but you gain minimum of [1+ Overwhelm value]. Which makes the rules unnecessarily complicated.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of keeping withering attacks simple is a great one. Overwhelm should just apply in some form to decisive attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:50:23-07:00","id":1451356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451354#post1451354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You see, in the Old Age the air pressure was greater, so the terminal velocity was lower... yeah, I got nothing!</div> </div> </div> </div>They have access to the superhero/exalt three-point landing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T10:54:00-07:00","id":1451358,"title":"","content":"The social rules do feel pretty toothless.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am Gazban, Merchant of Hearts, Fourth soul of Orabilis, End of all Wisdom, Sixth soul of Cecelyne. A somewhat pathetic creature for a second circle demon I admit, but I have this....oh yes, the Pictarious Rex, the badge of kingship for your home, the item you've sought as its rightful heir for these past 90 years. It's yours, but only in trade, in return you must tell me the location of your uncle's hidden manse. A warning though, in case you were thinking of simply taking it from me, the instant we join battle away it goes to my vault in Malfeas, never to be seen again.&quot;<br /> <br /> *Gazban then proceeds to roll 14 successes with his stupid good persuasion pool*<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm good actually, I'll get it from you some other way later, maybe from that vault of yours.&quot;<br /> <br /> *Gazban gets 3 dice to use if a fight now breaks out, otherwise they're lost at the end of the scene*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451342#post1451342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the core rules are the rules by which everyone plays and the Exaltes get to break those. So it being a difficulty 2 thing makes sense from a mortal standpoint and then an Exalt gets to look badass. Look at the media that inspires Exalted. &quot;Normal&quot; people will drop a story or two and break a leg or something but the superheroes can fall rather absurd distances and look either badass or mildly inconvenienced.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, but they usually use charms to do so. Mortals can not walk on water, but the Exalted can...if they both have and choose to activate Feather Foot Style, otherwise their feet sink into it just like anyone else. They can fire a single arrow into the sky and rain down a storm of thousands of essence duplicates, but only if they've got Arrow Rain Tempest. They can pump up their muscles to the point of being able to lift an elephant over their head, but only with Ten Ox Meditation.<br /> <br /> The only things Exalted all get by default are increased lifespan, the inability to fully die just from mundane disease, and increased injury healing. Everything else is charms, and thus specific to individual exalted, as well as possibly dependent on essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T11:13:27-07:00","id":1451359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451355#post1451355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A target\u2019s Defense may never reduce a withering attack\u2019s successes below the character\u2019s Overwhelm value on her weapon.&quot;<br /> <br /> This part confused me alot.<br /> <br /> Does this mean, if i have Overwhelm(3) on my weapon, i can never miss and get 3 power from the attack? That doesn't feel right.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't feel right, and I thought it must be an error, but this actually seems to be correct. The Clash rules on p.40 say &quot;Instead of utilizing Defense, these rolls subtract from each other. In the case of a withering attack, this could mean both characters add to their Power pool based on their weapons\u2019 Overwhelm ratings.&quot; This suggests that an attack with 0 successes still builds Power equal to its Overwhelm rating.<br /> <br /> I guess that's one way to make heavy weapons viable, but it feels very odd to me.<br /> <br /> (Also, I'm already having anxiety about these Clash rules. If you face a Melee-oriented Solar, make sure to Reflexively move away from them after each attack - they'll get +3 dice on their attacks against you from the subsequent Rush, but at least they won't get an Excellency to boost both attack and defense every turn, for free, while they spend The Breath of War on additional threats.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451358#post1451358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The social rules do feel pretty toothless.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am Gazban, Merchant of Hearts, Fourth soul of Orabilis, End of all Wisdom, Sixth soul of Cecelyne...</div> </div> </div> </div>Gazban at least has the advantage of actual leverage - if getting into that vault seems hard enough, the <i>player</i> may actually be persuaded. Imagine if they fell back on a total chump move, like making you experience all the suffering you had inflicted upon others in your life of violence. &quot;Dang. Well, I don't want any new Intimacies or anything, so Invincible Sword Princess powers through the trauma.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only things Exalted all get by default are increased lifespan, the inability to fully die just from mundane disease, and increased injury healing. Everything else is charms, and thus specific to individual exalted, as well as possibly dependent on essence. </div> </div> </div>Given how Essence Edition says things like &quot;If an Exalt has at least one dot in Physique, she can [lift a full-grown warhorse or bend an iron bar] without a roll,&quot; I'm not sure it follows that philosophy. Maybe I'll be more certain once I reach the Storytelling chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T12:18:48-07:00","id":1451366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451359#post1451359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't feel right, and I thought it must be an error, but this actually seems to be correct. The Clash rules on p.40 say &quot;Instead of utilizing Defense, these rolls subtract from each other. In the case of a withering attack, this could mean both characters add to their Power pool based on their weapons\u2019 Overwhelm ratings.&quot; This suggests that an attack with 0 successes still builds Power equal to its Overwhelm rating.<br /> <br /> I guess that's one way to make heavy weapons viable, but it feels very odd to me.<br /> <br /> (Also, I'm already having anxiety about these Clash rules. If you face a Melee-oriented Solar, make sure to Reflexively move away from them after each attack - they'll get +3 dice on their attacks against you from the subsequent Rush, but at least they won't get an Excellency to boost both attack and defense every turn, for free, while they spend The Breath of War on additional threats..</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the rule is a good idea, it avoids someone playing a turn and ending it thinking &quot;Wow I achieved nothing.&quot; As long as you don't gain as much as a fully successful attack/turn I think these rules for Overwhelming are great. (I compare this to Reliable in Lancer which is also pretty great to not feel bad about missing an attack)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T12:43:14-07:00","id":1451368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451366#post1451366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the rule is a good idea, it avoids someone playing a turn and ending it thinking &quot;Wow I achieved nothing.&quot; As long as you don't gain as much as a fully successful attack/turn I think these rules for Overwhelming are great. (I compare this to Reliable in Lancer which is also pretty great to not feel bad about missing an attack)</div> </div> </div> </div>It tracks pretty well from a narrative standpoint, too. Unless they're getting in the killing blow, even a failed attack can be used to a skilled fighter's advantage. For the heavy weapon wielder, even though the opponent avoided the blow having to change their plans to avoid an oncoming car swung at their head counts for SOMETHING.<br /> <br /> While I haven't read the exact passage yet, it would also seem to only count for failed Clash attacks. Wiffing on an &quot;unopposed&quot; attack seems to net you nothing. Gives you a reason to go for clashes beyond charm set-up","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 06-08-2021, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T13:09:27-07:00","id":1451373,"title":"","content":"I must underline a point I like a lot.<br /> <br /> I think we've all lived through this experience where one player in a level 8 D&amp;D group wants to do something like making a stalactite fall on an enemy instead of doing his normal attack or spell or whatever, takes up 20 mns of play because the DM have no idea of what to do, and the thing ends in an anti-climactic result because anyway stalactite does like 1d6 damage because it's scaling is bad and the whole experience was boring and frustrating for everyone.<br /> <br /> Well now it's just a &quot;Build Power&quot; action and it's as effective as anything else, which is time-saving and way more satisfactory, and I really like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T13:32:40-07:00","id":1451375,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Build Power actions are revelatory, really unlocking the potential of the Withering/Decisive system, which I already thought was clever.<br /> <br /> I am in Critical Mode right now, not because Essence looks bad, but because it looks good... and this is the window of time in which the wording and unintended rules can be tightened to make this an Exalted I can actually play, out of the box, with groups who haven't gotten sold on the same obscure house rules I have, for years.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that the Essence Storyteller chapter is actually really good advice for anyone setting out to run their first game in almost any RPG. It's a shame there wasn't the word count to have both that and a little more discussion of how to reliably supply challenges for being as powerful as Exalts, but if you only get one or the other, they definitely chose the right stuff to keep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451366#post1451366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the rule is a good idea, it avoids someone playing a turn and ending it thinking &quot;Wow I achieved nothing.&quot; As long as you don't gain as much as a fully successful attack/turn I think these rules for Overwhelming are great. (I compare this to Reliable in Lancer which is also pretty great to not feel bad about missing an attack)</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who takes a perverse enjoyment from the long-term logistics and push-your-luck strategy of 15+ round 3E fights, I can't really judge that.<br /> <br /> However, I am curious to see, when we get actual weapon stats, how often it is, in fact, as good as hitting. I do think it's only really a problem if you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 06-08-2021, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T13:42:16-07:00","id":1451377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451359#post1451359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gazban at least has the advantage of actual leverage - if getting into that vault seems hard enough, the <i>player</i> may actually be persuaded. Imagine if they fell back on a total chump move, like making you experience all the suffering you had inflicted upon others in your life of violence. &quot;Dang. Well, I don't want any new Intimacies or anything, so Invincible Sword Princess powers through the trauma.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. In Exalted aren't talky people supposed to be pretty dangerous? I don't want a return to 2e style mental combat where a Solar just conjures a thundercloud in the shape of their face and perfectly convinces the entire kingdom that they are now, and have forever been, their king. That's dumb as all heck and the ruiner of fun. I just think at some point, like how at some point getting hit hard enough in combat loses you an arm, in social ventures you just need to accept your character got convinced/tricked by the trickster god and now you can go get your revenge or whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451359#post1451359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how Essence Edition says things like &quot;If an Exalt has at least one dot in Physique, she can [lift a full-grown warhorse or bend an iron bar] without a roll,&quot; I'm not sure it follows that philosophy. Maybe I'll be more certain once I reach the Storytelling chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, okay I need to think on this some more then. I'm a pretty big fan of the duality of Exalted. I really like the idea that you can grab the throttle, pull HARD and punch up to strike a telling blow against powerful foes, or resist irresistible influence, but still have very mortal vulnerabilities because their strength is almost limitless but the scope of their power isn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure how to feel about this. I like a lot of the cool stuff that comes from Exalted having a lot of unique crunchy charms, so Essence is really going to make-or-break on the charms chapter for me, and I feel like it's ultimately going to be a break, but there's so much other stuff here I like. Maybe I can hack some of it into Ex3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T13:59:14-07:00","id":1451380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451359#post1451359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given how Essence Edition says things like &amp;quot;If an Exalt has at least one dot in Physique, she can [lift a full-grown warhorse or bend an iron bar] without a roll,&amp;quot; I'm not sure it follows that philosophy. Maybe I'll be more certain once I reach the Storytelling chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't go as far as saying this is a mistake or unintended, but I think the advice is supposed to make people understand &quot;lesser easy feats of strength like lifting someone are easy, dont make a roll&quot; and not &quot;the harder end of the lesser feats of strength should never be rolled&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T14:06:44-07:00","id":1451382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451377#post1451377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, okay I need to think on this some more then. I'm a pretty big fan of the duality of Exalted. I really like the idea that you can grab the throttle, pull HARD and punch up to strike a telling blow against powerful foes, or resist irresistible influence, but still have very mortal vulnerabilities because their strength is almost limitless but the scope of their power isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that it's a change of tone. That was part of my earlier point, about how the Solar theme of excellence has flipped from &quot;they can burn the candle twice as fast and thrice as bright as others&quot; to &quot;their candle never burns out&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T14:48:20-07:00","id":1451392,"title":"","content":"Hey... Am I the only one noticing a pattern in these names in the examples? Being from a <i>certain <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">splort?</div></div> </div> </div></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2444-lindhrive","name":"Lindhrive","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T15:20:52-07:00","id":1451396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451359#post1451359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, I'm already having anxiety about these Clash rules. If you face a Melee-oriented Solar, make sure to Reflexively move away from them after each attack - they'll get +3 dice on their attacks against you from the subsequent Rush, but at least they won't get an Excellency to boost both attack and defense every turn, for free, while they spend The Breath of War on additional threats.)</div> </div> </div> </div>How does having to Rush you affect their Excellency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T15:30:06-07:00","id":1451399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451396#post1451396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does having to Rush you affect their Excellency?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. But you're manipulating the timing rules such that they don't get to Clash you, and thereby use that Excellency on both attack and defense. So you might at least get your own shots in.<br /> <br /> I mean, they still can Clash you, but then they'd skip their next turn, so they don't get to move, so you can just Sprint away and be at Long Range (including the one band you moved on the turn with the Clash), at which point they can no longer close the gap to attack. So they probably won't do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T15:35:09-07:00","id":1451400,"title":"","content":"The dramatic injury rules don't even mention losing limbs or senses, which feels like an oversight in a game with Liminals, who can explicitly and casually replace lost limbs. I suppose you're supposed to infer that from the vague, Attribute-reducing injuries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T18:42:25-07:00","id":1451409,"title":"","content":"So the social system, yes it basically relies a lot on player and ST immersion. It is toothless yet personally i'm still very intrigued with playing with it unlike with the social system in 3e proper. I and my groups tend to forget about social systems a lot, since it very much just adds busywork to things that can be done by roleplay. Essence social however provides I feel way more in the way of incentives then 3e does, with its many stacking effects and difficulties. It incentives while not being forceful and I can honestly say that part appeals to me. I believe Hard Bargain exists to just ignoring influence though I do wish it was explained more thoroughly, i didn't really get it in my first read. <br /> <br /> Also I'm kinda confused with how the Air Iconic will interact with the social system, given that you will likely be causing collateral damage at Anima 10 for DBs I don't really get what it's supposed to be incentiving for my Air Aspect. Convincing people in the middle of a fight is evocative yet feels very limited in a way i don't think Air Aspects are supposed to. Also I kinda dislike that its a Add Essence in Success effect as an Iconic given that most other castes/aspects gets that type of ability for Actives. That's just my thought anyhow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T23:52:53-07:00","id":1451418,"title":"","content":"I find interesting that the only Unacceptable Influence directly tied to the mechanical character is the Major Virtue and not the Major Intimacies<br /> <br /> Also I'm not too worried about the &quot;ignore influence for bonus dices&quot; rule as it seems be here mostly for things anthetical to the character, with a great chance of being an Unacceptable Influence. However it's true I think the Hard Bargain should be the go to option for that, not &quot;I deny 15 minutes of roleplay and mechanical play for nothing because I dont feel like it&quot; with no narrative progression. <br /> <br /> If the player doesnt feel good about the Influence then it's a line or an X card, not a specific sub system rule","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 06-09-2021, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T05:14:19-07:00","id":1451432,"title":"","content":"I just realized something about ExEss combat system.<br /> <br /> There is now an opportunity cost baked into making a withering attack due to introduction of Build power action. (I really like the build power idea btw).<br /> <br /> We will understand more once charms are available, but as it stands now assuming you can use the same dice pools for both, it is more beneficial use build power than attack with your weapon the harder / skilled your opponent is.<br /> <br /> For Example; As the Dawn of the circle lets say you have 10 dice to attack with your sword and 10 dice to move athletically.<br /> <br /> If you are fighting Crimson Dusk of the better days to bury, who has a defense of 7. It is much easier to beat the default difficulty of 3 for the build power (which your opponent cant do anything about) than try to hit him with your sword like a good little sword princess. So choosing to make a withering attack is almost certainly is a bad decision in combat, or a trap choice if you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T05:57:54-07:00","id":1451434,"title":"","content":"First, a small nitpick: there's no Build Power action for Athletics. But I see your overall point. A lot of people are having this concern, including earlier in this very thread.<br /> <br /> Over on the Discord, the writers were very adamant that they'd payed a lot of aIttention to making both options good during their playtest, so we at least know this has been looked at. We can't really compare them yet ourselves, since we don't have weapon stats (the ship weapons on p.43 do indicate that accuracy bonuses still exist, which can change the math), but we have worked out one important piece of context: Withering always gets you a minimum of your Overwhelm value in power (probably assuming that you roll that many successes in the first place, but that still means you're looking for a smaller number than a jacked-up Defense).<br /> <br /> That's not at all clear in the preview manuscript, and I didn't believe it at first myself, but it gets referenced more directly under the Clash rules, and has been confirmed by devs over on Discord.<br /> <br /> I am still quite curious about the comparisons between Withering and Build Power, and will do some real analysis once we have a complete picture. And, between Overwhelm and BP having a fixed difficulty, I'm honestly a little thrown by how power generation in general seems pretty uninteractive - that will be a big adjustment for me, after impeding your enemy's Initiative economy was the arguable <i>main</i> focus of big 3E fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T08:05:04-07:00","id":1451442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451432#post1451432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something about ExEss combat system.<br /> <br /> There is now an opportunity cost baked into making a withering attack due to introduction of Build power action. (I really like the build power idea btw).<br /> <br /> We will understand more once charms are available, but as it stands now assuming you can use the same dice pools for both, it is more beneficial use build power than attack with your weapon the harder / skilled your opponent is.<br /> <br /> For Example; As the Dawn of the circle lets say you have 10 dice to attack with your sword and 10 dice to move athletically.<br /> <br /> If you are fighting Crimson Dusk of the better days to bury, who has a defense of 7. It is much easier to beat the default difficulty of 3 for the build power (which your opponent cant do anything about) than try to hit him with your sword like a good little sword princess. So choosing to make a withering attack is almost certainly is a bad decision in combat, or a trap choice if you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are still some points to consider though. Having 10 power is useless if you can't hit your opponent, and using withering to use Concentrated Attacks (formerly onslaught) is a way to hit the opponent more easily. The point about Overwhelming has already been made. Atracking the ennemy can also force him to consume motes, while BP doesnt cost the enemy anything at all from a resource perspective. <br /> <br /> I think if necessary it shouldntm't be too difficult to slightly twist Build Power actions to increase Base Diffiuclty : if 3 is too low, just getring it to 4 or 5 should be enough for most purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T08:37:32-07:00","id":1451444,"title":"","content":"Man, Concentrated Attacks. What an odd rule. TTRPGs in general, and Exalted in particular, often get the complaint that traditional &quot;boss fights&quot; are hard to do, thanks to the action economy of ganging up on one enemy. So why have an implementation of Onslaught Penalties which only matters against high-Hardness targets, of which the example we have is a Deathlord?<br /> <br /> That's another thing I'm really hoping to understand better as we see equipment and antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T08:50:29-07:00","id":1451446,"title":"","content":"My main issue is less that Withering attacks are always weaker than Build Power, as that which is more powerful is a boring calculation to make.<br /> I can, given knowledge of my pools, my weapon, and the enemy's defense, calculate pretty easily what the optimal action to gain power is.<br /> In fact, I can when building a character calculate the value of defense where the average switches over. There's a bit of depth in gaining for yourself/giving to others, and in amount of randomness, but it's generally easy.<br /> Withering attacks should always be directed at the lowest-defense enemy on the field, there's nothing but defense that affects this.<br /> I worry that at the start of the fight you can determine the one or two actions you'll be taking (something to gain power, and decisive attacks if you aren't feeding it to an ally), and calculate when you'll use either based your power and nothing else<br /> <br /> In contrast, in 3e you need to think about whether to try to reduce an enemy's initiative to prevent a decisive, whether to try to crash someone, how to avoid being crashed yourself, etc. Your decisions are based the interactions of the initiative of everyone on the field.<br /> <br /> I get that it's simpler, but it lost all of the depth that 3e combat had, and still isn't exactly simple.<br /> <br /> Charms and gambits and whatever might add something, but I'd be a lot more confident in the ability of charms to be interesting if I was more confident in the base.<br /> <br /> I think I've probably let pessimism take hold here, and tomorrow I'll probably be optimistic. I also haven't actually played any fights, so take it with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> I do really like that you can build power for allies, but I worry that you'll always just build power for the person who's best at hitting with decisive attacks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T09:10:01-07:00","id":1451449,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23597\" data-vbnamecard=\"23597\">autXautY</a> that seems like a fair concern. If everuone ignores the deathlord until they have 10 power its annoying.<br /> <br /> May someone rephrase to me the war rules on page 44 ? The 5 step process? I dont get how this works","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T09:32:03-07:00","id":1451451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451449#post1451449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23597\" data-vbnamecard=\"23597\">autXautY</a> that seems like a fair concern. If everuone ignores the deathlord until they have 10 power its annoying.<br /> <br /> May someone rephrase to me the war rules on page 44 ? The 5 step process? I dont get how this works</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of what I'm worried about is what it means to &quot;ignore&quot; the Deathlord. What else can you do? You can try to kill them with decisive attacks, but if you could do that you'd do that. You can try to get a wound penalty on them, or hit them with gambits, but a) those are slow, and b) those feel much less dynamic to me than withering attacks. There's no change over time in how effective they are, gambits you either have enough power or not.<br /> <br /> I think that the war rules are confusing partially because they are an extension of the venture rules, but before where it explains venture rules.<br /> <br /> How I understand it:<br /> A war is a sequence of opposed rolls, separated by time and potentially by dramatic scenes.<br /> The number of opposed rolls is (highest War among all leaders)+1<br /> Each opposed roll is (some attribute based on stunt)+War+modifiers<br /> After each opposed roll, the winner counts their extra successes<br /> At the end, the person with the most total extra successes wins<br /> <br /> Dramatic scenes are like, the highlight reel of the war.<br /> About 1/main opposed roll, you have a Dramatic Scene<br /> Both people pick what they want this scene to be, then the leader of each side rolls (some attribute+ability appropriate to the scene they picked), and the winner's scene happens<br /> Then you run that scene, possibly modified by the scene-picking roll, and whoever wins the scene gets bonus dice on their next opposed roll","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T09:32:24-07:00","id":1451452,"title":"","content":"Another thing on Build Power vs Combat is that a lot of the assumptions rely on white room. If your Building Power, your not in combat. The Build Power actions are very much narrative hooks, and outside a white room if its just you and the opponent, that will not be pretty. As everyone pointed out we are missing the Charms which have always been a big part of the game but its not only for the PCs but the Antagonists as well. I very much like Build Power but seeing how most of them relate to skills and the restrictions on who gets power when done they are definitely not supposed to exist in a vacuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T09:56:00-07:00","id":1451453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451451#post1451451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the war rules are confusing partially because they are an extension of the venture rules, but before where it explains venture rules.<br /> <br /> How I understand it:<br /> A war is a sequence of opposed rolls, separated by time and potentially by dramatic scenes.<br /> The number of opposed rolls is (highest War among all leaders)+1<br /> Each opposed roll is (some attribute based on stunt)+War+modifiers<br /> After each opposed roll, the winner counts their extra successes<br /> At the end, the person with the most total extra successes wins</div> </div> </div> </div>The part I don't get is why is the number of Opposed rolls for everyone depending on the ability among the war leader ? It feel very strange : The better the people are, the longer the war goes on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T10:14:35-07:00","id":1451454,"title":"","content":"I just noticed there is no Build Power action to insult/intimidate opponent or something like that. Am I missing something ? I think it would make a fair addition to the Build Power possible actions (the closest would be Inspire, I guess ?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T10:30:37-07:00","id":1451456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451454#post1451454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just noticed there is no Build Power action to insult/intimidate opponent or something like that. Am I missing something ? I think it would make a fair addition to the Build Power possible actions (the closest would be Inspire, I guess ?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't really think there's anything for that that isn't covered by the Inspire build or Distract gambit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T10:50:13-07:00","id":1451459,"title":"","content":"New preview, showing the first glances into Charms.<br /> <br /> The most surprising thing here is the Unique Modes. I knew that Getimian charms would have Still and Flowing Modes but was surprised on the return of Aura though it does makes sense in hindsight. Also that Liminals will have Nature's tied to their charms, now that is interesting. I think it will probably be similar to DB's Aura but having their charms be multifaceted just feels nice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T11:15:38-07:00","id":1451461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451459#post1451459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New preview, showing the first glances into Charms.<br /> <br /> The most surprising thing here is the Unique Modes. I knew that Getimian charms would have Still and Flowing Modes but was surprised on the return of Aura though it does makes sense in hindsight. Also that Liminals will have Nature's tied to their charms, now that is interesting. I think it will probably be similar to DB's Aura but having their charms be multifaceted just feels nice</div> </div> </div> </div>Most surprising thing for me is that DB, Solars, Lunars, Sidereals, Alchemical and Getimian seem to have only Universal Charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T11:49:03-07:00","id":1451464,"title":"","content":"They're doing it from Abyssals to Infernals, then Liminals to Janest, including the others along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T11:54:01-07:00","id":1451465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451461#post1451461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most surprising thing for me is that DB, Solars, Lunars, Sidereals, Alchemical and Getimian seem to have only Universal Charms</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure where you got that. According to the devs so far, every Exalt gets unique Charms and the amount is pretty even between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T12:10:18-07:00","id":1451466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451464#post1451464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're doing it from Abyssals to Infernals, then Liminals to Janest, including the others along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I assume it's alphabetical: Abyssals, Alchemicals, Dragon-Blooded, Getimians, Infernals || Liminals, Lunars, Sidereals, Solars, the Strawmaiden.<br /> <br /> Not sure why it's in a different order from the Chapter Two list, it's weird that the three original uncorrupted Celestials go last, but I guess it's for the ability to find which section is where more quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T12:14:18-07:00","id":1451468,"title":"","content":"I wish it wasn't alphabetical and instead by power - Solar, Abyssal, Infernal, Lunar, Sidereal, Alchemical, Terrestrial, and then the others that came after that. I also hope that Solars get enough love since everything I have seen seems to be pushing them down a bit. <br /> <br /> I will say I am looking forward to seeing how Wyld Shaping Technique works for Solars and also the whole world within the soul element of Infernals, which I hope remain in the game. <br /> <br /> Also it seems, from the example, the term Charm is not a thing known in-setting while an indiivdual Charm might be - the example says Solars won't say 'I am using a Close Combat Charm' in character but might say 'Hey all, I'm activating Whirlwind Brush Technique'. While I will have the word Charm be an in-game in-character thing this actual idea works for me. In some ways its better than the whole 'since chames are based on abilities and thus are a concrete thing we know the universe is 25 abilities' element.<br /> <br /> I will say from a mechanical standpoint I am not against the whole Universal Charms, Exalt Modes, Unique Charms element of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T12:16:07-07:00","id":1451469,"title":"","content":"As an aside I also wouldn't mind Solar, Lunar, Sidereal, Terrestrial, Alchemical, Abyssal, Infernal, and then the others either. I just think having Solars go near the last due to S being later in the alphabet seems thematically out of place. And while I know they won't I wish they would rethink this structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T12:30:19-07:00","id":1451471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451453#post1451453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The part I don't get is why is the number of Opposed rolls for everyone depending on the ability among the war leader ? It feel very strange : The better the people are, the longer the war goes on</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is pretty arbitrary.<br /> <br /> The reason they give is: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">This represents the leader\u2019s ability to push her combatants into clashes.&quot;<br /> Which doesn't really make sense to me.<br /> I could see an argument that more skilled leaders are able to have more complex plans remain functional?<br /> <br /> I think possibly the truest reason is that if a character has a really high War pool, they probably care a lot about war and want a war to be an important thing when it happens, and the most war-invested character is only moderately invested they probably want War scenes to be less of a big deal</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T12:37:25-07:00","id":1451472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451452#post1451452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing on Build Power vs Combat is that a lot of the assumptions rely on white room. If your Building Power, your not in combat. The Build Power actions are very much narrative hooks, and outside a white room if its just you and the opponent, that will not be pretty. As everyone pointed out we are missing the Charms which have always been a big part of the game but its not only for the PCs but the Antagonists as well. I very much like Build Power but seeing how most of them relate to skills and the restrictions on who gets power when done they are definitely not supposed to exist in a vacuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am confused by your second sentence.<br /> My impression is that Power is only used for combat actions (gambits, decisive attacks), and that you'd only every gain Power in a combat scene. Some ways of gaining Power (most Build Power Actions) aren't combatty actions, but they are in combat.<br /> <br /> If I were to describe my complaint, it would be that fights don't have rhythm, that you can at the start of the fight figure out the optimal thing to do on each turn based on very simple metrics. Interesting terrain or goals other than &quot;kill them before they kill you&quot; don't really change this - it can change what's optimal, but any terrain that's present or goal you have is probably equally present throughout the fight. The only way to address my concern would be for the scenario to change in some novel way most turns, which could make for a cool fight, but probably shouldn't happen every fight with no grounding in the text of the rules.<br /> <br /> Build Power seems like it allows for a lot of cool stunts, and I appreciate that, but if my character has performance 5 and no combat skill and every fight, every turn I take an Inspire-type Build Power because it's the best way to generate Power I will get bored by like, the second fight.<br /> <br /> In 3e, the fight changes over time, you have momentary opportunities and threats you have to deal with, you can plan the next 3 turns and maybe have it turn out brilliantly or maybe 2 turns in something happens that disrupts your plans and you need new ones. I'm not sure that'll happen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T12:43:07-07:00","id":1451473,"title":"","content":"Huh. Were committed motes always supposed to immediately return to your pool instead of counting as spent after you release the commitment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T12:46:48-07:00","id":1451474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451472#post1451472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am confused by your second sentence.<br /> My impression is that Power is only used for combat actions (gambits, decisive attacks), and that you'd only every gain Power in a combat scene. Some ways of gaining Power (most Build Power Actions) aren't combatty actions, but they are in combat.<br /> <br /> If I were to describe my complaint, it would be that fights don't have rhythm, that you can at the start of the fight figure out the optimal thing to do on each turn based on very simple metrics. Interesting terrain or goals other than &quot;kill them before they kill you&quot; don't really change this - it can change what's optimal, but any terrain that's present or goal you have is probably equally present throughout the fight. The only way to address my concern would be for the scenario to change in some novel way most turns, which could make for a cool fight, but probably shouldn't happen every fight with no grounding in the text of the rules.<br /> <br /> Build Power seems like it allows for a lot of cool stunts, and I appreciate that, but if my character has performance 5 and no combat skill and every fight, every turn I take an Inspire-type Build Power because it's the best way to generate Power I will get bored by like, the second fight.<br /> <br /> In 3e, the fight changes over time, you have momentary opportunities and threats you have to deal with, you can plan the next 3 turns and maybe have it turn out brilliantly or maybe 2 turns in something happens that disrupts your plans and you need new ones. I'm not sure that'll happen</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe people shouldn't be able to use these actions repetitively ? Like, insulting your enemy might give you an edge the first time because he's angered by this, but by the 10th time he shouldn't really care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T13:06:05-07:00","id":1451477,"title":"","content":"They might cover this in the Charm section, but how do you think familiar are handled ? Through Build Power action, and they don't have actions of their own ? Through an entire separate character ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T13:21:39-07:00","id":1451480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451474#post1451474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe people shouldn't be able to use these actions repetitively ? Like, insulting your enemy might give you an edge the first time because he's angered by this, but by the 10th time he shouldn't really care.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might help?<br /> I wouldn't want a strict once/scene restriction, since then it just becomes &quot;I will spend my first few turns taking the good 1/scene actions, then take the best re-usable action&quot;, something more gradual would make identifying the turnover point more interesting<br /> In general I think decay is worse than up-and-down variance - I want to insult my enemy one turn, then stab them, then do a cool flip off of a nearby wall, then insult them, and each turn have the decision of which of those to use be novel, but if insults just get worse, or turn off entirely, there isn't as much interest in seeing what new situation each turn will bring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T13:44:25-07:00","id":1451483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451477#post1451477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might cover this in the Charm section, but how do you think familiar are handled ? Through Build Power action, and they don't have actions of their own ? Through an entire separate character ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know the answer, but given the visible mechanical influence and writer overlap with the Storypath games (Exalted Essence is definitely not a Storypath game, but it has some clearly inspired tweaks), my expectations are based on how the Storypath games (or at least Scion 2e) handle it. Scion's equivalent, the Creature Birthright, gives you an allied animal character built using the stripped-down NPC rules, with a dice pool for appropriate actions directly determined by its dot rating, and special qualities or abilities which are &quot;purchased&quot; in exchange for a lower dice pool. So a five-dot Basilisk Creature might have 9 dice for basilisky actions, the Miasmic Presence and Natural Weapon qualities, the Petrifying Gaze ability, and then its numerical Health, Defense, and Initiative ratings, and that's about its entire sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T13:58:01-07:00","id":1451485,"title":"","content":"Do we have any canon yet on WHEN Getimians were freed and started appearing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T14:01:31-07:00","id":1451486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451485#post1451485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any canon yet on WHEN Getimians were freed and started appearing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember hearing ~50 years ago, so roughly RY 718.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T14:41:00-07:00","id":1451490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451483#post1451483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know the answer, but given the visible mechanical influence and writer overlap with the Storypath games (Exalted Essence is definitely not a Storypath game, but it has some clearly inspired tweaks), my expectations are based on how the Storypath games (or at least Scion 2e) handle it. Scion's equivalent, the Creature Birthright, gives you an allied animal character built using the stripped-down NPC rules, with a dice pool for appropriate actions directly determined by its dot rating, and special qualities or abilities which are &amp;quot;purchased&amp;quot; in exchange for a lower dice pool. So a five-dot Basilisk Creature might have 9 dice for basilisky actions, the Miasmic Presence and Natural Weapon qualities, the Petrifying Gaze ability, and then its numerical Health, Defense, and Initiative ratings, and that's about its entire sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. I'm a bit annoyed by the fact that it takes an entire turn in game, but at least if there are rules to design it in game it can only be better than 3e on this aspect","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T14:42:12-07:00","id":1451491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElOhTeeBee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451473#post1451473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Were committed motes always supposed to immediately return to your pool instead of counting as spent after you release the commitment?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always run/understood it as &quot;spent after releasing the commitment.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T15:02:54-07:00","id":1451499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451491#post1451491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always run/understood it as &quot;spent after releasing the commitment.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. I'm pretty sure this was an intentional change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T15:02:59-07:00","id":1451500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dragon-Blooded Charms have Aura[...] </div> </div> </div> oh god damn it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElOhTeeBee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451473#post1451473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Were committed motes always supposed to immediately return to your pool instead of counting as spent after you release the commitment?</div> </div> </div> </div> No, that's just an Essence thing, likely lifted from Godbound's Effort and/or Scion's Legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T15:24:43-07:00","id":1451505,"title":"","content":"What on earth is a VTT token pack? I was looking at the rewards and can't really figure it out. Is it just small images in a generic format or is it some specific 3rd party digital thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/me