v> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Images of various size and design intended to be used as tokens, miniatures, and the like for virtual table tops like Roll20, Astral, etc<br /> <br /> Like these.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/338120\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/img/dtrpg/m_icon_menu_cab.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/338120\" target=\"_blank\"> DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/338120\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/338120 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Your one-stop online shop for new and vintage RPG products from the top publishers, delivered fresh to your desktop in electronic format. </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/309127\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/309127</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This reminds me how much I hate it when people use anacronyms for things without first defining what it is at least once (I'm looking at you [V]irtual [T]able [T]op).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T19:15:12-07:00","id":1451517,"title":"","content":"Are we allowed to share the preview PDFs at all? I have some friends I've been trying to get into Exalted and am trying to talk them into this KS an was going to show them some of it to give them an idea of what the game is like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T19:58:22-07:00","id":1451520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451517#post1451517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we allowed to share the preview PDFs at all? I have some friends I've been trying to get into Exalted and am trying to talk them into this KS an was going to show them some of it to give them an idea of what the game is like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if sharing the PDFs themselves is alright, they're one of the incentives for joining the Kickstarter in the first place. Distributing how the rules work shouldn't be too much of an issue however, we've known a lot of this stuff months prior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T03:46:09-07:00","id":1451534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451468#post1451468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish it wasn't alphabetical and instead by power - Solar, Abyssal, Infernal, Lunar, Sidereal, Alchemical, Terrestrial, and then the others that came after that..</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Hard stop disagree. The Charms chapter is a reference chapter. It\u2019s not a place where statements about the setting are being made. The Exalts chapter I\u2019m fine with not being in strict alphabetical order, because a) each exalt entry is short; and b) it tell you what order they\u2019re in at the beginning. Mostly, Exigents is pushed all the way to the back, but it\u2019s by far the longest. <br /> If I\u2019m looking for Infernal Charms, it\u2019s a lot easier to remember that \u201cInfernal\u201d comes after \u201cGetimian\u201d but before \u201cLiminal\u201d than it is to try and remember where they are in the power scale, something that officially has 2 levels, Terrestrial and Celestial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T07:44:13-07:00","id":1451540,"title":"","content":"Some Charms preview.<br /> <span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mongoose-and-Cobra Escape</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> <i>Finesse 2</i> or Athletics 2</span></span></span><br /> Yeah right they might want to rethink this one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T09:00:13-07:00","id":1451543,"title":"","content":"For today's Charm preview:<br /> <br /> <br /> Ox-body gives a -1 HL, and for the modes:<ul><li><b>Abyssal, Infernal and Solar Mode:</b> The Exalt gains their choice of an additional 0 or two -1 Health levels.</li> </ul><br /> So, if I got this right, Solaroids get 3 x -1 HLs per ox-body?! That's one hell of a lot!<br /> Even more so when Sids get 1 x 0, and the poor Alchemicals only get 1 x -1. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T09:15:36-07:00","id":1451545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451543#post1451543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For today's Charm preview:<br /> <br /> <br /> Ox-body gives a -1 HL, and for the modes:<ul><li><b>Abyssal, Infernal and Solar Mode:</b> The Exalt gains their choice of an additional 0 or two -1 Health levels.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> So, if I got this right, Solaroids get 3 x -1 HLs per ox-body?! That's one hell of a lot!<br /> Even more so when Sids get 1 x 0, and the poor Alchemicals only get 1 x -1. </div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I read it. Shakes out roughly like this, assuming max repurchases <br /> <br /> Lunars: -1x10, -2x5<br /> Liminal: -0x5, -1x5<br /> Solaroid: -0x5, -1x5 OR -1x15<br /> DB: -1x5, -2x5<br /> Fate Bois: -0x5<br /> Alchemicals: -1x5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T10:13:10-07:00","id":1451549,"title":"","content":"I assumed the mode replaced the -1 with a choice of -0 or 2x-1. That might be clarified in the full charms chapter when they discuss how modes work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T10:18:37-07:00","id":1451550,"title":"","content":"I read it as you get the Base + the Mode unless the mode for the particular exalt says its an exception. <br /> <br /> So Sidereals for example replace the base for just the mode while Solars get the Base and the Mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T10:19:19-07:00","id":1451551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451549#post1451549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed the mode replaced the -1 with a choice of -0 or 2x-1. That might be clarified in the full charms chapter when they discuss how modes work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinct language is conspicuous in that the Liminal Mode says &quot;The Exalt gains an additional 0 Health level&quot; whereas the Sidereal and Getimian Mode says &quot;The Exalt replaces the default -1 Health level with a 0 Health level.&quot; Unless they specify otherwise, Modes <i>add</i> to the base Charm effect, they don't normally replace it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T10:30:51-07:00","id":1451552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451545#post1451545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how I read it. Shakes out roughly like this, assuming max repurchases<br /> <br /> Lunars: -1x10, -2x5<br /> Liminal: -0x5, -1x5<br /> Solaroid: -0x5, -1x5 OR -1x15<br /> DB: -1x5, -2x5<br /> Fate Bois: -0x5<br /> Alchemicals: -1x5</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the first time Lunars don't have the advantage of quantity with this charm. But maybe they have other sources or something. Hard to judge for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>Inevitable Meerkat Style</b></i><br /> <i>The Student Sutra of Spotlight Hoging: Once, there was a maiden, but who cares about those? Let's talk about Lunars.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8863-slulura","name":"Slulura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T10:36:50-07:00","id":1451553,"title":"","content":"Man, poor Alchemicals. I wasn't expecting them to get the worst of the batch for Ox Body, I thought the Sidereals or the DBs would have been the ones on the chopping block.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T11:45:04-07:00","id":1451558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451553#post1451553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, poor Alchemicals. I wasn't expecting them to get the worst of the batch for Ox Body, I thought the Sidereals or the DBs would have been the ones on the chopping block.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather agree with this. That was the most unexpected thing I've seen so far. Perhaps Alchemicals will get a specific Charm to gain more Health levels? I can just say that 'Magical Material Robot' doesn't sound like something that should be so... flimsy.<br /> <br /> The other point is that a lot of the Infernal ability 'turns on' when they get to -2 Health Levels. I'm surprised that they don't get the ability like the Lunars to get a lot of -2s, thus extending the amount of time they are at Critical Health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T13:50:51-07:00","id":1451571,"title":"","content":"In 2nd ed the Alchemicals had a pretty decent Ox Body and had free extra health levels with their Essence levels, the difference is enormous!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T16:18:50-07:00","id":1451590,"title":"","content":"Word from the Discord is the Alchemical Ox-Body is a confirmed error and the whole breakdown is getting an overhaul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T19:03:26-07:00","id":1451600,"title":"","content":"As an aside one of the elements I really like about this edition is the whole &quot;some things that used to be Essence 6+ are now lower essence since they represent the excellence of an Exalt&quot;. This includes the whole Infernal soul-world element because seriously while I love Solars the most (and Sidereals from a personal real life 'which exalt would I be as me') the whole element of having my own world in my soul is just really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T20:41:51-07:00","id":1451608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451600#post1451600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside one of the elements I really like about this edition is the whole &amp;quot;some things that used to be Essence 6+ are now lower essence since they represent the excellence of an Exalt&amp;quot;. This includes the whole Infernal soul-world element because seriously while I love Solars the most (and Sidereals from a personal real life 'which exalt would I be as me') the whole element of having my own world in my soul is just really cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, not walling off the cool stuff to higher tier play is part of 3e\u2019s ethos. Elder Exalted just pick up one or two unique tricks that make them more distinct opponents, but don\u2019t keep building power at the same rate as entirely separate tier of play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T21:02:56-07:00","id":1451610,"title":"","content":"One thing that I'm really enjoying when I go through the charms showcased thus far is the Getimian interpretation of things. With Mongoose-and-Cobra Escape, we have a fairly simple effect: Pay 1 mote after dodging an attack, dash for 1 range band. All of the other modes are fairly unique and evocative, but the Getimian mode, Water-and-Ice Understanding, takes the cake: Not only can you teleport yourself by &quot;dodging&quot; or &quot;dashing,&quot; you can <i>impose</i> a &quot;dash&quot; onto your opponent. It's like some kind of Stand power, the Getimian causes something, &quot;a dash,&quot; to happen, but then imposes the effect, &quot;moving in the target direction,&quot; onto the target. This is the kind of conceptual BS that I love and hope to see more with the Gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T06:32:47-07:00","id":1451649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451610#post1451610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I'm really enjoying when I go through the charms showcased thus far is the Getimian interpretation of things. With Mongoose-and-Cobra Escape, we have a fairly simple effect: Pay 1 mote after dodging an attack, dash for 1 range band. All of the other modes are fairly unique and evocative, but the Getimian mode, Water-and-Ice Understanding, takes the cake: Not only can you teleport yourself by &quot;dodging&quot; or &quot;dashing,&quot; you can <i>impose</i> a &quot;dash&quot; onto your opponent. It's like some kind of Stand power, the Getimian causes something, &quot;a dash,&quot; to happen, but then imposes the effect, &quot;moving in the target direction,&quot; onto the target. This is the kind of conceptual BS that I love and hope to see more with the Gets.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I found this interesting, but also the Liminal one. If I read it right, you can maintain a Grapple at range with them. That's... interesting, to say the least.<br /> <br /> I'd also point out for the people concerned that Solars aren't 'good enough', their mode on that Charm seems to be a bit boring, but undeniably powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T07:01:30-07:00","id":1451654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451649#post1451649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I found this interesting, but also the Liminal one. If I read it right, you can maintain a Grapple at range with them. That's... interesting, to say the least.<br /> <br /> I'd also point out for the people concerned that Solars aren't 'good enough', their mode on that Charm seems to be a bit boring, but undeniably powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the vibe I'm getting from a lot of Solar stuff in ExEss. Less intricate, flavorful, and trippy but when you look at it mechanically the Solar is undeniably Better Than You.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T07:53:24-07:00","id":1451663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451654#post1451654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the vibe I'm getting from a lot of Solar stuff in ExEss. Less intricate, flavorful, and trippy but when you look at it mechanically the Solar is undeniably Better Than You.</div> </div> </div> </div>The approach to Solar Modes was what Monica calls the &quot;broadest applicability&quot; approach - they have Modes that are the most useful in every single circumstance, whereas a Dragon-Blooded's Mode might be &quot;equally strong&quot; but only useable in a specific instance. What we did want to do is preserve that other Exalts may have areas of niche or specialty where they can do things Solars flat-out can't, or where they might even be a little stronger, but Solars remain the Mario or the Lugh - they have immensely strong performance in <i>everything</i>, they're the best at several of them, and if they're not first they are a <i>very </i>close second. The Dusk Caste might be a better single opponent killer than the Dawn, but the Dawn will smash the hell out of a whole army.<br /> <br /> Solars get:<ul><li>Arguably the best Advantages - Supremacy of Ability is <i>very </i>strong, Divine Resonance is a nice cherry, and First Among Equals is definitely better than folks think at first glance;</li> <li>The most broadly applicable Modes, as described above;</li> <li>Arguably the strongest Exalt-specific Charms;</li> <li>The best ability to build anima (contained within their Charms);</li> <li>Greatest strategic power in terms of access to all Evocations, SMA, and upper-tier sorcery and mid-tier necromancy;</li> <li>Setting-wise, you may notice that Solars have the lowest &quot;zero to hero&quot; time period of reaching starting character level - DBs take several years or a decade, Celestials 2-5 years, but Solars are less than a year.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T09:49:15-07:00","id":1451682,"title":"","content":"Previews for Solar Charms just got up. Unconquered Sun's Sight, Glorious Solar Arsenal, and Dazzling Flare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T10:36:29-07:00","id":1451687,"title":"","content":"Anti-CoDs and equipment made of soul-light is just what I want to see from Solar unique charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T10:49:48-07:00","id":1451692,"title":"","content":"These are pretty cool!<br /> <br /> After reading Golden Champion Glory, I had to go back and check the rules for Committed motes. As far as I can tell, you really can un-Commit them with no action at any time, but I was happy to see that someone had thought of the obvious abuse case there, since if you do that, you &quot;may not reactivate the same Charm the following turn.&quot; Well-played! I do still wonder whether it would be worthwhile for Solar who already has one weapon to use Golden Champion Glory every other turn for the free Build Power...<br /> <br /> Conversely, Refracted Light Analysis is something I'll have to return to once we have the full text - to consider whether it really is the worst use of a Charm slot in the whole edition. So, as I understand this, I'm spending a Charm slot (already worth 2-3 times as much as in previous editions) to pick one ally, which I cannot ever change, who can also detect lies related to their intimacies... when I've got this Charm active anyway. I don't think I would spend a Charm slot on that in any edition, but it gets better: someone lying to your friend will also automatically flare your Anima, potentially outing you as a Solar at awkward times. Maybe just take some new Intimacies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:36:33-07:00","id":1451708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451692#post1451692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, Refracted Light Analysis is something I'll have to return to once we have the full text - to consider whether it really is the worst use of a Charm slot in the whole edition. So, as I understand this, I'm spending a Charm slot (already worth 2-3 times as much as in previous editions) to pick one ally, which I cannot ever change, who can also detect lies related to their intimacies... when I've got this Charm active anyway. I don't think I would spend a Charm slot on that in any edition, but it gets better: someone lying to your friend will also automatically flare your Anima, potentially outing you as a Solar at awkward times. Maybe just take some new Intimacies?</div> </div> </div> </div>New Charms and repurchases come from different milestones, so they shouldn't overlap. And I'd expect personal milestones to be pretty frequent, so picking up a repurchase or a new mode is not going to be a big deal. (This is also where I expect most of your Excellencies to come from.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T12:11:13-07:00","id":1451718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451708#post1451708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Charms and repurchases come from different milestones, so they shouldn't overlap. And I'd expect personal milestones to be pretty frequent, so picking up a repurchase or a new mode is not going to be a big deal. (This is also where I expect most of your Excellencies to come from.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If I have to choose between +1 Excellency and Refracted Light Analysis, I think I know which one benefits me more. See also: Ox-Body. And that's just what we've seen already.<br /> <br /> Maybe more to the point, look at the awesome upgrades that Glorious Solar Arsenal gets for free! Those abilities rule, and then I could turn around and buy something which I might be looking for ways to opt out of. It's puzzling.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm not saying this is some huge problem. Any set of discrete, exception-based powers will have some which are above or below average. This only really bugged me in 3E when it was a prerequisite for something cool, and as a repurchase, that seems unlikely here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T14:43:48-07:00","id":1451756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451708#post1451708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> New Charms and repurchases come from different milestones, so they shouldn't overlap. And I'd expect personal milestones to be pretty frequent, so picking up a repurchase or a new mode is not going to be a big deal. (This is also where I expect most of your Excellencies to come from.)</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Is</i> an Excellency a repurchase? The different Ability Excellencies have different names, so aren't they different Charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T17:44:37-07:00","id":1451779,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's something I can use some clarification on. Can Glorious Solar Arsenal be used multiple times while still having Motes committed? Like, can I use it to summon SunSword in turn 1, and then SunArmor in turn 2?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Perfected Shining Summons makes the charm reflexive. Does that mean I can use Glorious Solar Arsenal as many times in a single turn as I have motes to commit? Does that proc Golden Champion Glory every time? Could I theoretically dump half my motes in one turn into Glorious Solar Heavy Mob Cemetery and gather more power than god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25545-jollycooperative","name":"jollycooperative","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T17:58:35-07:00","id":1451781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jollycooperative</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451779#post1451779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here's something I can use some clarification on. Can Glorious Solar Arsenal be used multiple times while still having Motes committed? Like, can I use it to summon SunSword in turn 1, and then SunArmor in turn 2?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Perfected Shining Summons makes the charm reflexive. Does that mean I can use Glorious Solar Arsenal as many times in a single turn as I have motes to commit? Does that proc Golden Champion Glory every time? Could I theoretically dump half my motes in one turn into Glorious Solar Heavy Mob Cemetery and gather more power than god?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for charms say that unless otherwise stated they must be activated in step 1 of a turn, and only one charm can be used per step, so you cannot activate it multiple times in one turn. And if you activate it at all then you aren't using an excellency or any other step 1 charm.<br /> <br /> However, my understanding is that yes you can have it activated more than once to have both a weapon and armor, for example, but you commit essence both times and it takes 2 turns (and uses your step 1 charm activation in both). Best to do it before starting the fight, if you can...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T19:08:43-07:00","id":1451791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindharin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451781#post1451781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for charms say that unless otherwise stated they must be activated in step 1 of a turn, and only one charm can be used per step, so you cannot activate it multiple times in one turn. And if you activate it at all then you aren't using an excellency or any other step 1 charm.<br /> <br /> However, my understanding is that yes you can have it activated more than once to have both a weapon and armor, for example, but you commit essence both times and it takes 2 turns (and uses your step 1 charm activation in both). Best to do it before starting the fight, if you can...</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is that actions have steps, not turns. So it would be step 1 of an attack, or of a social roll, or another action.<br /> But Glorious Solar Arsenal isn't linked to any action - it's reflexive, which in previous versions meant it creates its own action. Which it's presumably step 1 of?<br /> <br /> Even if it doesn't create it's own action, my impression is you can activate a charm during a step of someone else's action - you have to, or you wouldn't be able to use charms to defense - so you could possibly activate it every time some took an action you didn't have another charm to use during, which should be fairly often (every action an ally takes, every time an enemy attacks someone other than you, etc)<br /> <br /> Also, If you can do this, it doesn't even use up all your motes - you can reflexively de-commit them all to regain the motes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T22:17:32-07:00","id":1451803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451791#post1451791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression is that actions have steps, not turns. So it would be step 1 of an attack, or of a social roll, or another action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Normally you only act once per turn, but you're right; if I flurry or otherwise make 2 attacks then each action will have a step 1 where I can activate a charm. Although the rules do say: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chapter 4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter what, a character can only take two actions per turn. This includes actions taken in response to things, like counterattacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That explicitly says actions taken in response to something, like counterattacks, are limited that way too. I think that means if you want to do a standard attack and use this charm on step 1, and that gives you the Build Power action, those are your two actions for the turn. So my reading is that we couldn't flurry the original action and also get the bonus action from this charm in the same turn, because then we would be having 3 total actions in the turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451791#post1451791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Glorious Solar Arsenal isn't linked to any action - it's reflexive, which in previous versions meant it creates its own action. Which it's presumably step 1 of?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for reflexive charms in update 18 say &quot;If it creates an action, it will specify.&quot; So, the use of a reflexive Glorious Solar Arsenal doesn't say it creates an action for its main effect of creating the weapon/armor, but it does say (at higher prereqs) that it creates an action for Build Power or the other choices. I think that action would have a Step 1, and you could then use a charm for it's step 1, but even if you used Glorious Solar Arsenal again at that point you couldn't get another Build Power in the same turn because you are limited to a max of 2 actions per turn anyway. But it would be a way to get both armor and a weapon in one turn, if you wanted to commit 2 motes. <span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451791#post1451791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Even if it doesn't create it's own action, my impression is you can activate a charm during a step of someone else's action - you have to, or you wouldn't be able to use charms to defense - so you could possibly activate it every time some took an action you didn't have another charm to use during, which should be fairly often (every action an ally takes, every time an enemy attacks someone other than you, etc)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451791#post1451791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, If you can do this, it doesn't even use up all your motes - you can reflexively de-commit them all to regain the motes</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you can activate charms on specific steps of someone else's action, so to use a defensive charm you need a charm that works on step 2 of their combat action (and probably 4, 7 and 8 too). But I don't think you can activate a charm on step 1 of someone else's action, that is their declaration phase, not yours. The defender gets to declare their response in step 2. Could be wrong, but letting every character act on every step of every other character's turn seems against the intent to me. I think you act on your turn, and you react on other turns only on specific steps of their action if you are their target. <br /> <br /> The rules for un-committing motes say that you can't use that same charm through the next turn, there is a cooldown before you can use it again. This was discussed with the devs on discord today, and they confirmed that you could only use this tactic to try to build power once every other turn. You'd be able to use the weapon or armor only half the rounds, and couldn't use excellencies or other step 1 charms on those turns either, but you could get an attack and a build power every other round as a way around the rule against flurrying them together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T03:11:56-07:00","id":1451823,"title":"","content":"I'm loving the Infernal Modes so far. And Hard Bargains are a neat Sophie's Choice kinda thing (though I would ignore the rule you can just nope a social influence action in exchange for giving your enemy extra dice; it should always be a Hard Bargain).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T06:57:12-07:00","id":1451838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451823#post1451823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm loving the Infernal Modes so far. And Hard Bargains are a neat Sophie's Choice kinda thing (though I would ignore the rule you can just nope a social influence action in exchange for giving your enemy extra dice; it should always be a Hard Bargain).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the idea of denying social influence but then giving your enemies an advantage over you in theory, but there should be a limit to the amount of times you can do that or the conditions needed to do it. Hard Bargains are great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T07:14:46-07:00","id":1451846,"title":"","content":"Hard Bargains are definitely a cool idea, but I'm reserving judgement until I see them in play. I like to think I'm a reasonably creative person, but I'm just not sure whether I'll regularly be able to thinki of something on the spot which seems to be (1) in the spirit of the original influence, (2) not quite as bad, and (3) not totally toothless. I would argue that, in the example, Heather's metafictional Storyteller failed at the second point: &quot;sell out the other real-life people I'm playing with&quot; is usually a much harder sell than &quot;sell out this minor NPC&quot;. Would I have done better?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451358#post1451358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I am Gazban, Merchant of Hearts, Fourth soul of Orabilis, End of all Wisdom, Sixth soul of Cecelyne. A somewhat pathetic creature for a second circle demon I admit, but I have this....oh yes, the Pictarious Rex, the badge of kingship for your home, the item you've sought as its rightful heir for these past 90 years. It's yours, but only in trade, in return you must tell me the location of your uncle's hidden manse. A warning though, in case you were thinking of simply taking it from me, the instant we join battle away it goes to my vault in Malfeas, never to be seen again.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exalt takes a Hard Bargain. Now what?<br /> <br /> Offering up something else in exchange for the Pictarious Rex isn't a Hard Bargain, because it would be literal bargaining in-character. That's no different from refusing outright. I suppose that I could offer to let them refuse this offer only by personally deciding that opposing Gazban matters more than being the rightful heir, renouncing that Intimacy, but &quot;radically alter your character concept&quot; isn't a much better ask than &quot;betray the PCs.&quot; Reducing an Intimacy from Major to Minor (as the book seems to suggest) has the opposite problem: it just doesn't seem to change very much, even assuming I'm insistent on them not increasing it again the next time they do something king-ey.<br /> <br /> Maybe in actual play, really ambiguous cases like that don't come up often. Maybe I'll quickly start presenting nastier social rolls with fallback positions already in mind. I don't know. I hope so, because as I said, they're a cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T07:57:08-07:00","id":1451853,"title":"","content":"Things we know about steps:<br /> <br /> Each attack has steps 1 through 8.<br /> <br /> Each social influence has steps 1 through 4.<br /> <br /> You can only activate Charms once per step.<br /> <br /> Questions I have about steps:<br /> <br /> Do non-attack non-social influence actions have steps? Is it just Step 1? (My guess: yes and yes, or maybe Step 1 to declare and Step 3 to roll if it has a roll.)<br /> <br /> Do reflexive Charms take a step? Can it be Step 1 of any action, even another player's? (My guess: yes and maybe?)<br /> <br /> What if a Charm creates an action - can I activate more Charms in that action's steps? (My guess: maybe?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T08:07:36-07:00","id":1451856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451853#post1451853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do non-attack non-social influence actions have steps? Is it just Step 1? (My guess: yes and yes, or maybe Step 1 to declare and Step 3 to roll if it has a roll.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a biggie. If you cannot use Perfected Shining Summons after declaring, say, a Full Defense action, that changes a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T08:23:15-07:00","id":1451857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindharin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451803#post1451803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. Normally you only act once per turn, but you're right; if I flurry or otherwise make 2 attacks then each action will have a step 1 where I can activate a charm. Although the rules do say:<br /> That explicitly says actions taken in response to something, like counterattacks, are limited that way too. I think that means if you want to do a standard attack and use this charm on step 1, and that gives you the Build Power action, those are your two actions for the turn. So my reading is that we couldn't flurry the original action and also get the bonus action from this charm in the same turn, because then we would be having 3 total actions in the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know if that's intended to be per turn, or per round?<br /> It says turn, which sounds to me like you can take only 2 actions on your turn, and then up to 2 actions on each other players turn.<br /> But that is a very light limit, and also doesn't fit with the emphasis on it including counterattacks. It doesn't contradict that, they could be saying no more than two counterattacks/similar reaction per person's turn, but that line makes more sense if it's per round.<br /> <br /> If it's per round, we're potentially back to activating Glorious Solar Arsenal on other people's turn. Depending on how charms that don't modify an action interact with the rule on 1 charm/step.<br /> <br /> I had missed the action limit. It makes the Dawn and Dusk iconic limit a bit weaker, since they'll be competing with other free action effects. Dusk especially, since they'll want to be flurrying attacks and intimidation a lot. If Glorious Solar Rave is never edited to not work, but the action limit is per round, it makes the Dawn effect a lot weaker, since any solar can hit their action limit every other turn with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindharin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451803#post1451803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you can activate charms on specific steps of someone else's action, so to use a defensive charm you need a charm that works on step 2 of their combat action (and probably 4, 7 and 8 too). But I don't think you can activate a charm on step 1 of someone else's action, that is their declaration phase, not yours. The defender gets to declare their response in step 2. Could be wrong, but letting every character act on every step of every other character's turn seems against the intent to me. I think you act on your turn, and you react on other turns only on specific steps of their action if you are their target. </div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that follows? All charms explicitly intended to work on other people's actions will almost certainly operate in those steps, but that's because those are the steps for interacting with other people's actions, but I don't think there's a rule saying those are the only times you can activate a charm on someone else's action.<br /> <br /> There shouldn't have to be, really. There shouldn't be any charms that could activate on step 1 of someone else's action, since that's not when the defender does stuff. It's only because it's ambiguous how the step rule applies to charms which don't interact with any action that &quot;can you activate charms on step 1 of other people's actions&quot; comes up.<br /> &quot;Charms can activate on step 1 of an arbitrary action, without regards to what that action is, and do not interact at all with that action&quot; is a logical reading of the rules, which mostly doesn't break anything, but which creates lots of little bits of friction.<br /> <br /> Actually, working as intended, if you summon a weapon to parry an attack or armor to block it, that almost could interact with an enemy attack. But still couldn't happen on step 2 of the attack, since the charm doesn't say it happens on step 2. (It's not what the Glorious Solar Raver would do, since they want to already be wearing armor and carrying a weapon)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","user":"autXautY","date":". 06-12-2021, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T09:10:41-07:00","id":1451865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451857#post1451857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had missed the action limit. It makes the Dawn and Dusk iconic limit a bit weaker, since they'll be competing with other free action effects. Dusk especially, since they'll want to be flurrying attacks and intimidation a lot. If Glorious Solar Rave is never edited to not work, but the action limit is per round, it makes the Dawn effect a lot weaker, since any solar can hit their action limit every other turn with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had also missed the action limit, and it does raise a lot of questions. I'd really like something like that to get its own paragraph, rather than being buried at the end of the description of Flurries (though, in the writers' defense, they did bold it). A ton of things depend on the details there! The most immediate implication which jumps out at me is: you cannot Reflexively move and use a Flurry in the same turn (though you can Flurry an action with a Rush). That's an odd quirk.<br /> <br /> It does say &quot;turn,&quot; so until the writers say otherwise, I'm going to assume that the odd note about Counterattacks is saying you could not somehow use Charms to take 3+ Reflexive actions on other people's turns. Otherwise, things get very strange very quickly.<br /> <br /> Either way, though, I don't think this impacts the Dawn (and Azimuth) Anima power, since Supernal Warrior doesn't call itself an action, Reflexive or otherwise. The Abyssal one suffers like the lame knockoff it is, though, and I am more anxious as ever to have some clarity on some of the vague Action timing stuff in the Anima effects - I hope that the section on Anima from the Charms chapter clears things up, because otherwise that'll be a bunch of erratas to submit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T07:04:13-07:00","id":1451988,"title":"","content":"Universal Charms Manuscript is up","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T07:43:27-07:00","id":1451996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451988#post1451988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Universal Charms Manuscript is up</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting: per Neall on RPGnet, they'll be writing a lot more Modes for the finished version.<br /> <br /> Also, some of the massive disparity in Modes between Solars and Liminals is versioning differences, so that'll factor in too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T09:01:06-07:00","id":1452001,"title":"","content":"I'm not super active on RPGnet or the discord, but I'm seeing a lot of mentions of versioning and things being in the &quot;finished version&quot; and it has me kinda concerned. Has it been clarified exactly how different things are? Will we have the actual current version when the KS ends? I really want to start diving into Essence and had assumed based on back KS that wouldn't be a problem with the KS manuscript but everything I'm hearing gives me pause. Any idea if the compiled version after the KS ends will have all these updates or are there potentially substantial changes we just won't even see until the backer PDF?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T09:28:44-07:00","id":1452003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452001#post1452001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not super active on RPGnet or the discord, but I'm seeing a lot of mentions of versioning and things being in the &quot;finished version&quot; and it has me kinda concerned. Has it been clarified exactly how different things are? Will we have the actual current version when the KS ends? I really want to start diving into Essence and had assumed based on back KS that wouldn't be a problem with the KS manuscript but everything I'm hearing gives me pause. Any idea if the compiled version after the KS ends will have all these updates or are there potentially substantial changes we just won't even see until the backer PDF?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My understanding is that there will be substantial changes we won't see until the backer PDF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T09:45:38-07:00","id":1452007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452001#post1452001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not super active on RPGnet or the discord, but I'm seeing a lot of mentions of versioning and things being in the &quot;finished version&quot; and it has me kinda concerned. Has it been clarified exactly how different things are? Will we have the actual current version when the KS ends? I really want to start diving into Essence and had assumed based on back KS that wouldn't be a problem with the KS manuscript but everything I'm hearing gives me pause. Any idea if the compiled version after the KS ends will have all these updates or are there potentially substantial changes we just won't even see until the backer PDF?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there will be some changes we won't see until some time, but I believe the Charms themselves are solid enough that you can play any Exalt you want without much problem","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T10:15:28-07:00","id":1452009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452001#post1452001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not super active on RPGnet or the discord, but I'm seeing a lot of mentions of versioning and things being in the &quot;finished version&quot; and it has me kinda concerned. Has it been clarified exactly how different things are? Will we have the actual current version when the KS ends?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think there is a &quot;current version&quot; in writing besides the backer previews. The writers have been playing and revising these rules for a long time, and like any play group, they know their own intentions to the point that a lot of things don't get written down as they change. I think the most important aspect of the errata period is for them to learn where the writing doesn't quite line up with their intentions.<br /> <br /> The Charms are great, but the biggest news related to ongoing discussions here was before they started, in the section on Counterattacks. It looks like I was wrong, and the intention really is &quot;two actions per round,&quot; including any reflexive stuff on other people's turns. That's a really big deal, doubly so if it counts the reflexive move you get every turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:03:18-07:00","id":1452015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452009#post1452009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not think there is a &quot;current version&quot; in writing besides the backer previews.</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs claim to have already fixed a few stuff in their draft that people pointed out upon seeing the previews.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Charms are great, but the biggest news related to ongoing discussions here was before they started, in the section on Counterattacks. It looks like I was wrong, and the intention really is &quot;two actions per round,&quot; including any reflexive stuff on other people's turns. That's a really big deal, doubly so if it counts the reflexive move you get every turn. </div> </div> </div>Reflexive actions don't count toward the limit. (It says this where reflexive actions are defined). But counterattacks aren't reflexive unless they say so (e.g in the Ready in Eight Directions mode).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T11:09:48-07:00","id":1452017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452015#post1452015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reflexive actions don't count toward the limit. (It says this where reflexive actions are defined).</div> </div> </div> </div>I had to check this. What it says is &quot;Reflexive actions do not count towards the total number of things a character can do during her turn,&quot; which is a textbook example of natural language making rules confusing. In hindsight, it probably does mean what you say, but at the time, I just thought it meant you don't need a Flurry to take one in addition to a Simple action.<br /> <br /> And, of course, read literally, these rules mean that a character can take any number of Reflexive actions (plus up to two other actions) on <i>her own turn</i>, and up to two actions (Reflexive or otherwise) on the turn of any given other character, assuming she has abilities allowing her to do so.<br /> <br /> I have no particular reason to assume that's the intention, but then again, that's my entire point.<br /> <br /> Either way, I really hope that there's some way for the writers to articulate their meaning which doesn't involve Reflexively creating a non-Reflexive action, because that kind of makes my head spin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 06-13-2021, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T12:41:06-07:00","id":1452034,"title":"","content":"One question about anima level : it is said that \u00ab Every two points of Anima increases the level of display from Dim to Iconic \u00bb Then it is mentionned Dim (1-2)<br /> Does it mean Dim has 2 level or the 1-2 is for the 1 or 2 motes spent ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T13:38:32-07:00","id":1452048,"title":"","content":"Anima powers are definitively supposed to be covered by the no more than two actions limit. The devs have expcititly said that that 2 actions is a hard limit for things you can do between when you take your turn and the next time it is your turn. This is to stop the ridiclous stuff happening in other editions. Solar Anima banner is supposed to stop you from doing any more actions until you get back to your initiative. Sadly, they have already printed exceptions in the charms, but at least they call out the fact that they are breaking this rule. Otherwise it should be pretty clear that 2 actions is a hard limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1228-jhiriit","name":"Jhiriit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T13:54:02-07:00","id":1452051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452003#post1452003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that there will be substantial changes we won't see until the backer PDF.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is... disappointing, given how many versioning errors are in the preview manuscript.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T13:59:54-07:00","id":1452056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jhiriit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452048#post1452048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anima powers are definitively supposed to be covered by the no more than two actions limit... Solar Anima banner is supposed to stop you from doing any more actions until you get back to your initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, which Solar Anima effect? This doesn't seem to refer to First Among Equals or Supremacy of Ability.<br /> <br /> More generally, now that we know everything the text is going to say about Anima powers and timing, I have a TON of questions. Far moreso than Charms, I don't feel like I know the writers' intention on whether things are Simple, Reflexive, or not-an-action stuff. And that last category absolutely exists! The most obvious example right now is uncommiting a mote, which you're p[retty clearly meant to be able to do on a Step when you're about to use a Charm, to get resources. But there's also Anima stuff: I don't think the writers expect you to do anything (beyond flaring Anima) to &quot;turn on&quot; Pasiap Still Stands, for example. But then, what about Laws of New Creation or No Gods, No Masters, which use the very active-sounding verbs &quot;establishes,&quot; and &quot;desecrates&quot;? Those... probably don't take any action? But then, what about using Thousand Elixir Tears or a Greater Sign?<br /> <br /> I feel like a lot of the Anima stuff comes from a version before the details of actions got hammered out, and I hope it gets revised to add a ton of context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452034#post1452034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question about anima level : it is said that \u00ab Every two points of Anima increases the level of display from Dim to Iconic \u00bb Then it is mentionned Dim (1-2)<br /> Does it mean Dim has 2 level or the 1-2 is for the 1 or 2 motes spent ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would ignore the &quot;every two&quot; sentence, since it's also contradicted by Bonfire covering 7, 8, <i>and</i> 9.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T14:11:40-07:00","id":1452062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452017#post1452017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had to check this. What it says is &quot;Reflexive actions do not count towards the total number of things a character can do during her turn,&quot; which is a textbook example of natural language making rules confusing. In hindsight, it probably does mean what you say, but at the time, I just thought it meant you don't need a Flurry to take one in addition to a Simple action.<br /> <br /> And, of course, read literally, these rules mean that a character can take any number of Reflexive actions (plus up to two other actions) on <i>her own turn</i>, and up to two actions (Reflexive or otherwise) on the turn of any given other character, assuming she has abilities allowing her to do so.<br /> <br /> I have no particular reason to assume that's the intention, but then again, that's my entire point.<br /> <br /> Either way, I really hope that there's some way for the writers to articulate their meaning which doesn't involve Reflexively creating a non-Reflexive action, because that kind of makes my head spin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Their answer is even though counter attack may be created as a reflexive action, it counts as an action.<br /> <br /> My personnal understanding is that you can do any combination of 2 actions, whatever they may be labelled, except reflexives, of which you get an unlimited number ? But you are restrained that you can only do them either on your turn, or at a specific step of another character action, so it's also restricted anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T14:12:43-07:00","id":1452063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452009#post1452009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not think there is a &quot;current version&quot; in writing besides the backer previews. The writers have been playing and revising these rules for a long time, and like any play group, they know their own intentions to the point that a lot of things don't get written down as they change. I think the most important aspect of the errata period is for them to learn where the writing doesn't quite line up with their intentions.<br /> <br /> The Charms are great, but the biggest news related to ongoing discussions here was before they started, in the section on Counterattacks. It looks like I was wrong, and the intention really is &quot;two actions per round,&quot; including any reflexive stuff on other people's turns. That's a really big deal, doubly so if it counts the reflexive move you get every turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also, Monica said that the intention is really &quot;2 actions per round&quot;, and she expects it will be edited properly at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T14:58:37-07:00","id":1452074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452062#post1452062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their answer is even though counter attack may be created as a reflexive action, it counts as an action.<br /> ...<br /> Also, Monica said that the intention is really &quot;2 actions per round&quot;, and she expects it will be edited properly at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Thanks for relaying that.<br /> <br /> I have a very hard time getting my head around reflexive charms creating not-reflexive (but, apparently, not called &quot;simple,&quot; either, because straightforward terminology is for cowards) actions. And now I don't even know what to guess about any other reflexive way to create something which would normally be an action. Glorious Solar Arsenal's Golden Champion Glory does specify a <i>reflexive</i> Build Power action (in other news, we're back to me not seeing anything to prevent massive abuse of GCG), so maybe anything which doesn't specify does eat up an action slot? But then, on p.3, if a Charm creates an action, it will specify. Swift Counterattack <i>doesn't</i> specify, which seems like a problem, until I realized that p.5 establishes a new general rule that counterattacks always count as an action. What an odd thing to have a general rule for - are there lots of counterattacks in this edition? Well, not in Universal Charms, where there are exactly two: Swift Counterattack, and Captivating Battlefield Display.<br /> <br /> Captivating Battlefield Display's counterattack explicitly does not count as an action.<br /> <br /> Essence, please. I'm not too proud to beg. Please please please please just pick whether reflexive Charms create reflexive or &quot;real&quot; actions, and specify every exception. Alternately, specify every time. I really want to love this game, and to know whether I do, you need to tell me the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T21:56:51-07:00","id":1452111,"title":"","content":"To be more fair, she didnt tell it should be written &quot;2 actions per round&quot; but that this is the intent and this whole thing should be clarified in the final text, but she didnt specify how the clarification should be done<br /> <br /> It's true that the counter attack rule seems a bit specific for so few charms. I will ask on the discord if the charms which allows you to Build Power reflexively (like GCG or the abyssal mode of the dodgkng Charm to greate a phantom double) do count as your action for the turn or not","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T23:50:32-07:00","id":1452121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1451846#post1451846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard Bargains are definitely a cool idea, but I'm reserving judgement until I see them in play. I like to think I'm a reasonably creative person, but I'm just not sure whether I'll regularly be able to thinki of something on the spot which seems to be (1) in the spirit of the original influence, (2) not quite as bad, and (3) not totally toothless. I would argue that, in the example, Heather's metafictional Storyteller failed at the second point: &quot;sell out the other real-life people I'm playing with&quot; is usually a much harder sell than &quot;sell out this minor NPC&quot;. Would I have done better?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Exalt takes a Hard Bargain. Now what?<br /> <br /> Offering up something else in exchange for the Pictarious Rex isn't a Hard Bargain, because it would be literal bargaining in-character. That's no different from refusing outright. I suppose that I could offer to let them refuse this offer only by personally deciding that opposing Gazban matters more than being the rightful heir, renouncing that Intimacy, but &quot;radically alter your character concept&quot; isn't a much better ask than &quot;betray the PCs.&quot; Reducing an Intimacy from Major to Minor (as the book seems to suggest) has the opposite problem: it just doesn't seem to change very much, even assuming I'm insistent on them not increasing it again the next time they do something king-ey.<br /> <br /> Maybe in actual play, really ambiguous cases like that don't come up often. Maybe I'll quickly start presenting nastier social rolls with fallback positions already in mind. I don't know. I hope so, because as I said, they're a cool idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't understand it to mean that the Hard Bargain has to be 'less bad' than the original influence; it just needs to be comparable. It's perfectly fair if the player decides to stick with the original influence rather than the alternative--that's the 'hard' part. <br /> <br /> I think your Intimacies and concept could be really helpful in determining what the bargain might be, but you can also work in future plot points. Let's say you want to have a local town turn against the Circle so that they are forced to go on a quest to win back trust. Your players have Virtues like Justice and Ambition which fit this story.<br /> <br /> So let's say the influence is to inspire the PC to rage against a person they care about and don't want to hurt. You could give the PC an easy option to just break something valuable instead (trickier with the sanctity of Merits, because shattering an Artifact weapon would be a good swap for hurting a beloved Intimacy, I feel; but perhaps smashing a local icon or holy site will do, as this feeds into your intended plot), or might allow the PC to take their anger out on an influential third person instead (say, the local magistrate, because she represents denial of the PC's freedom at a time when they feel they are being controlled by others and resent it), or might fall back on the tried and tested: combat (you rule that in fighting their new urges, the PC misses the Wyld Hunt which has now circled them and prepares for an ambush).<br /> <br /> I use Intimacies in my current Vampire game, as I love them so much, and for every Intimacy a character has, I try to plan at least 3-4 plot hooks which I can use whenever I need inspiration. I intentionally plan for NPCs to have opposing goals to create conflict and I update them to fit with the story I have sketched out ahead.<br /> <br /> I think you could do the same here. It's just a matter of thinking, 'How can I turn this person's Virtues or Intimacies into an opportunity to propel the story forward in a way that's interesting?' And when the thing that propels the story forward is a conflict, and one that challenges a PC's weaknesses, you have something ripe for a Hard Bargain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T00:10:07-07:00","id":1452123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452074#post1452074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence, please. I'm not too proud to beg. Please please please please just pick whether reflexive Charms create reflexive or &quot;real&quot; actions, and specify every exception. Alternately, specify every time. I really want to love this game, and to know whether I do, you need to tell me the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to Charms and the limitations on actions per turn, I think a lot of the ambiguity here comes from not having clear designation for cost, action type, duration, and so on for each Charm (especially action type). On top of that, it seems like most of the usage of Steps (given that Charms are Step 1 by default and you can only use 1 Charm per Step) is actually just to reinvent the Simple action type in a way that takes more words and that is slower to understand than just saying so.<br /> <br /> Imagine if the rule about the number of actions you can take was written this way:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each character can use a maximum of two Simple actions per round. Even if a character uses a Simple action generated by a Reflexive action (such as a counterattack Charm), that still counts against the limit. If you would use a Simple action but have already used two Simple actions this round, the action doesn't happen. </div> </div> </div>Now take that and clearly mark every Charm and every non-charm combat action as Simple/Dramatic/Reflexive, and have a generic Simple attack action (let's call it &quot;Strike&quot; for clarity) that Charms can also give you. Then you just need consistent templating for directly-used Simple actions and for generated Simple actions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Basic Action: Strike</b><br /> <b>Action</b> Simple<br /> <br /> You attack a target, using the resolution rules on page XX. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Glorious Exalted Bolt</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b> Ranged Combat 2 or Sagacity 2<br /> <b>Cost</b> 1m; <b>Action</b> Simple<br /> <br /> <i>The Exalt forms a blazing bolt of Essence aligned with their nature to strike their enemies.</i><br /> <br /> This Charm acts as a ranged Strike using either Sagacity or Ranged Combat, except that instead of using a wielded weapon, you generate an essence attack, which you treat as a heavy ranged weapon with short range and the Artifact and Ranged tags. You can add 1a to the Cost to increase the essence attack's range to medium. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Swift Counterattack</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b> Close Combat 3<br /> <b>Cost</b> 1m; <b>Action</b> Reflexive (Step 8)<br /> <br /> <i>Reading her enemy\u2019s movements, the Exalt unleashes a deadly counterattack.</i><br /> <br /> Make a melee Strike using Close Combat against one enemy who attacked you this round. This Strike suffers the flurry penalty as if it were part of a flurry. </div> </div> </div>(Note the difference between &quot;acts as&quot; and &quot;make&quot;; the latter invokes the Simple action limit, while the former avoids it since it's already been invoked by the Charm being Simple.)<br /> <br /> And, there you go, no more ambiguity.<br /> <br /> Pathfinder 2e uses a very similar structure to this for actions-that-create-other-actions. For example, Flurry of Blows is a 1-action ability (Simple action equivalent, basically) that lets you Strike twice, and each Strike resolves as a full action even though it's only costing you one of your actions for the round. That system doesn't use it for a hard cap on actions-per-round, but it does carry across an escalating penalty on multiple attacks per round, which works very nicely as a soft cap to prevent people from optimizing just for total number of attacks per round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","user":"Roadie","date":". 06-14-2021, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T01:01:35-07:00","id":1452128,"title":"","content":"Did they remove perfect defenses from the game in Exalted Essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T01:05:27-07:00","id":1452129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452128#post1452128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they remove perfect defenses from the game in Exalted Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they did. I haven't seen any for the moment in Universal Charms, but sore Exalt specific Charms might still exist. If you're referring to specifically the 2e Percect D\u00e9fenses yeah I believe they don't exist at all, and neither in 3e. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2168_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2168\" data-vbnamecard=\"2168\">Chejop Kejak</a> People on the Discord seems to think that most Charms that create actions (like GCG or the Abyssal Charm on Mongoose-and-Cobra Escape) counts toward your limit of 2 actions per round, but you don't need to &quot;flurry&quot; them or take any penalty for using on another action on your turn (contrary to some Multi-attacks Charm that specifically say so in their text for example)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T01:16:27-07:00","id":1452131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452001#post1452001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not super active on RPGnet or the discord, but I'm seeing a lot of mentions of versioning and things being in the &amp;quot;finished version&amp;quot; and it has me kinda concerned. Has it been clarified exactly how different things are? Will we have the actual current version when the KS ends? I really want to start diving into Essence and had assumed based on back KS that wouldn't be a problem with the KS manuscript but everything I'm hearing gives me pause. Any idea if the compiled version after the KS ends will have all these updates or are there potentially substantial changes we just won't even see until the backer PDF?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the current version. Backers will, months from now, get an updated version with changes and formatting and art. We will submit errata about typos and unclear elements in that pdf, and then they will send us a final pdf and send it to printers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T02:38:24-07:00","id":1452133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452129#post1452129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe they did. I haven't seen any for the moment in Universal Charms, but sore Exalt specific Charms might still exist. If you're referring to specifically the 2e Percect D\u00e9fenses yeah I believe they don't exist at all, and neither in 3e.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2168_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2168\" data-vbnamecard=\"2168\">Chejop Kejak</a> People on the Discord seems to think that most Charms that create actions (like GCG or the Abyssal Charm on Mongoose-and-Cobra Escape) counts toward your limit of 2 actions per round, but you don't need to &quot;flurry&quot; them or take any penalty for using on another action on your turn (contrary to some Multi-attacks Charm that specifically say so in their text for example)</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavenly Guardian Defense <i>exists</i> as a charm, but apparently the idea was &quot;it's mostly used to do these things anyway&quot; and given how costly it is to use in combat in core Ex3, I can see the reasoning even if I do not wholly agree with it. It's not a showstopper for me, though, given the other differences in the combat system (like Incap not actually taking you entirely out of a fight unless everyone is down).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T02:52:45-07:00","id":1452137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452133#post1452133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heavenly Guardian Defense <i>exists</i> as a charm, but apparently the idea was &quot;it's mostly used to do these things anyway&quot; and given how costly it is to use in combat in core Ex3, I can see the reasoning even if I do not wholly agree with it. It's not a showstopper for me, though, given the other differences in the combat system (like Incap not actually taking you entirely out of a fight unless everyone is down).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I wouldn't call it a &quot;Perfect Defense&quot; Charm, just a &quot;You can try to use this stat to defend against environmental damage&quot; stat. I get your point though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T06:43:10-07:00","id":1452157,"title":"","content":"&quot;Perfect Defenses&quot; in the 2E sense already only exist as a single Charm in 3E. If Seven Shadows Evasion is coming back, we won't know until we hit Solar Charms, late in the week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452129#post1452129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's true that the counter attack rule seems a bit specific for so few charms. I will ask on the discord if the charms which allows you to Build Power reflexively (like GCG or the abyssal mode of the dodgkng Charm to greate a phantom double) do count as your action for the turn or not<br /> ...<br /> People on the Discord seems to think that most Charms that create actions (like GCG or the Abyssal Charm on Mongoose-and-Cobra Escape) counts toward your limit of 2 actions per round, but you don't need to &quot;flurry&quot; them or take any penalty for using on another action on your turn (contrary to some Multi-attacks Charm that specifically say so in their text for example)</div> </div> </div> </div>That does seem to be the intention most of the time. However, GCG specifically creates a <i>reflexive</i> Build Power action, where Mongoose-And-Cobra Escape -&gt; Spectral Deception doesn't. If that doesn't mean GCG's Build Power bypasses the action limit (as reflexive actions do, unless they specify otherwise), then that word really needs to be cut.<br /> <br /> I agree that it probably shouldn't bypass the limit. Letting someone take two actions (generating a weapon or armor for each), Build Power twice, then do the same thing the next turn before uncommitting the motes, is clearly abusive. But, as has perhaps become obvious, I don't always agree with the writers about how things &quot;should&quot; work, which is why I'd prefer them to tell me what they mean than rely on us making the same guesses.<br /> <br /> Somewhat related to all of this, my current working hypothesis is that whenever the book talks about an unspecified &quot;action,&quot; it means a <i>simple</i> action, and it doesn't mean reflexive unless it says so. If someone finds statements or text which either support or refute that, please do let me know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452123#post1452123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to Charms and the limitations on actions per turn, I think a lot of the ambiguity here comes from not having clear designation for cost, action type, duration, and so on for each Charm (especially action type). On top of that, it seems like most of the usage of Steps (given that Charms are Step 1 by default and you can only use 1 Charm per Step) is actually just to reinvent the Simple action type in a way that takes more words and that is slower to understand than just saying so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it does look like that. I like Step-based resolution, but it only works when it's clearly defined, and here it isn't - it seems like every action has at least a Step 1, but the book won't tell us that, let alone what other Steps (if any) they've got.<br /> <br /> Here's a puzzle which occurred to me recently: &quot;During a fight scene, only one Charm may be used per step of combat... If a Charm has no listed Step, treat it as a Step 1.&quot; Read literally, this appears to mean that you cannot use an Excellency to enhance, say, Evidence-Discerning Method <i>in combat</i>. Outside of it, you can, because conflicting Step 1 Charms only matter &quot;during a fight scene.&quot; Was that deliberate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T10:29:20-07:00","id":1452180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452157#post1452157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a puzzle which occurred to me recently: &quot;During a fight scene, only one Charm may be used per step of combat... If a Charm has no listed Step, treat it as a Step 1.&quot; Read literally, this appears to mean that you cannot use an Excellency to enhance, say, Evidence-Discerning Method <i>in combat</i>. Outside of it, you can, because conflicting Step 1 Charms only matter &quot;during a fight scene.&quot; Was that deliberate?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to be, yes. It was certainly deliberate that using Charms on social influence behaves differently for social influence in combat - reflecting, I guess, that in combat you're in more of a hurry and don't have time to activate all your Charms.<br /> <br /> I think being able to apply the Integrity Excellency to boost Resolve out of combat but not in combat wasn't deliberate, but not sure on either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T10:40:35-07:00","id":1452181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452180#post1452180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think being able to apply the Integrity Excellency to boost Resolve out of combat but not in combat wasn't deliberate, but not sure on either.</div> </div> </div> </div> Incidentally, I don't get <i>how</i> to boost Resolve with an Excellency, since the text of the Charm doesn't say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-14-2021, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T12:06:15-07:00","id":1452196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452181#post1452181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Incidentally, I don't get <i>how</i> to boost Resolve with an Excellency, since the text of the Charm doesn't say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be in the systems chapter, but I know somewhere in the manuscript it brings up how 2 dice roughly equals 1 success and that &quot;exchange&quot; is used for boosting static values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T12:13:57-07:00","id":1452197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452196#post1452196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be in the systems chapter, but I know somewhere in the manuscript it brings up how 2 dice roughly equals 1 success and that &quot;exchange&quot; is used for boosting static values.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently so. It's not under Excellencies or the Dice Limit, which were the places I had thought to look, but turns out to be a general rule under Bonuses and Penalties.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that characters &quot;take half the number of dice and round up,&quot; rather than down as in 3E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T16:46:34-07:00","id":1452254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452131#post1452131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the current version. Backers will, months from now, get an updated version with changes and formatting and art. We will submit errata about typos and unclear elements in that pdf, and then they will send us a final pdf and send it to printers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope the Week 5 full Pdf includes the current version of Withering Attacks and Milestones. Without those, the game is sort of unplayable. And it surely wouldn't take long just to put those in. Other stuff isn't so vital for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T18:14:33-07:00","id":1452258,"title":"","content":"Well, how they are implementing Elemental Aura is a delight. No fuss and bother to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T20:58:32-07:00","id":1452273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452254#post1452254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope the Week 5 full Pdf includes the current version of Withering Attacks and Milestones. Without those, the game is sort of unplayable. And it surely wouldn't take long just to put those in. Other stuff isn't so vital for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be great!<br /> <br /> I don't know how likely it is, though, so I'm pinning my hopes on fans making a compilation of corrected rules based on stuff the devs say, then getting one of them to say &quot;close enough until the Back pdf&quot; about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452258#post1452258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, how they are implementing Elemental Aura is a delight. No fuss and bother to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does look really neat! The meditation idea gives it a cool feel, too, though I'm not sure how often it will actually be used in combat. A lot may depend on whether it can be flurried.<br /> <br /> My big question, however, is &quot;can you be in multiple auras at once?&quot; 3E doesn't allow that, obviously, but I'm not sure about Essence based on that preview. We'll see if it gets detailed further in the full writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T23:21:13-07:00","id":1452282,"title":"","content":"This is something that has probably been answered already, but I don't have the patience to search around.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Milestones, I understand how they're supposed to work in general, but there are two points that get me confused.<br /> <br /> On Personal Milestones, they say that's possible to 'buy' different Modes or repurchase Charms. The repurchase is pretty obvious, but I got the impression that you automatically get all the modes you qualify for immediately, and you cannot buy cross-Exalted Modes, so... it's referred to Exalt-specific Modes that are not presented in the 'Universal Charm' section or there is something I missed?<br /> <br /> And for the Exalted Milestones, the fact that you can only use them for 'Exalted Charms' refer to splat-specific charms, like, only Solar/Lunar/Dragonblooded Charms, or it works also for Universal Charms? Because if it doesn't work for Universal Charm they're of very limited use, so I'm almost certain you can use them to get Universal Charms, but I'd like to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T23:40:20-07:00","id":1452284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452196#post1452196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might be in the systems chapter, but I know somewhere in the manuscript it brings up how 2 dice roughly equals 1 success and that &quot;exchange&quot; is used for boosting static values.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure this helps boost resolve, since<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"> Resolve is not an Integrity roll or pool, its a static value set depending on your Integrity value</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T01:08:56-07:00","id":1452288,"title":"","content":"I'm uns ure this has been linked, but there is a dev clarification document assembled by the Discord :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oh6OYAJ060OS6exdFxVF3nGvw74qzenuzYfHqNPulLE/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oh6OYAJ060OS6exdFxVF3nGvw74qzenuzYfHqNPulLE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oh6OYAJ060OS6exdFxVF3nGvw74qzenuzYfHqNPulLE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oh6OYAJ060OS6exdFxVF3nGvw74qzenuzYfHqNPulLE/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T01:14:52-07:00","id":1452289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452282#post1452282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something that has probably been answered already, but I don't have the patience to search around.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Milestones, I understand how they're supposed to work in general, but there are two points that get me confused.<br /> <br /> On Personal Milestones, they say that's possible to 'buy' different Modes or repurchase Charms. The repurchase is pretty obvious, but I got the impression that you automatically get all the modes you qualify for immediately, and you cannot buy cross-Exalted Modes, so... it's referred to Exalt-specific Modes that are not presented in the 'Universal Charm' section or there is something I missed?<br /> <br /> And for the Exalted Milestones, the fact that you can only use them for 'Exalted Charms' refer to splat-specific charms, like, only Solar/Lunar/Dragonblooded Charms, or it works also for Universal Charms? Because if it doesn't work for Universal Charm they're of very limited use, so I'm almost certain you can use them to get Universal Charms, but I'd like to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have found one Universal Charm where you can buy more modes. I forget what. Buying it gave you 2 modes (it didn't have a base effect) and then you could buy more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T01:25:53-07:00","id":1452290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452288#post1452288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm uns ure this has been linked, but there is a dev clarification document assembled by the Discord :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oh6OYAJ060OS6exdFxVF3nGvw74qzenuzYfHqNPulLE/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oh6OYAJ060OS6exdFxVF3nGvw74qzenuzYfHqNPulLE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oh6OYAJ060OS6exdFxVF3nGvw74qzenuzYfHqNPulLE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oh6OYAJ060OS6exdFxVF3nGvw74qzenuzYfHqNPulLE/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's very useful. Although, once again, further clarification of Withering Attacks just confuses me. Overwhelming isn't a minimum at all, it's on top of what you roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T01:31:53-07:00","id":1452291,"title":"","content":"Just noticed something : The document specifies Teamwork has Base Difficulty 3, which seems normal because the game specifies rolls have Base Difficulty 3 when no Difficulty is specified.<br /> <br /> Until you notice Flickering Shadow Evasion (and I believe many other Charms ? Haven't check) have no Difficulty mentioned, so it should assume Base Difficulty 3. Which I don't think is the intent. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> I think Overwhelming is a minimum indeed, the phrasing is just a bit poor but should mean (if I'm not mistaken) : if you rolled lower damage than withering but still hit your attack, you still get Overwhelming Power (fuck yeah !)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T05:59:45-07:00","id":1452310,"title":"","content":"Minor quibble: EE seems to use the term Overwhelm, rather than OverwhelmING.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452289#post1452289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have found one Universal Charm where you can buy more modes. I forget what. Buying it gave you 2 modes (it didn't have a base effect) and then you could buy more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sharpshooter's Clever Tricks works that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452291#post1452291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just noticed something : The document specifies Teamwork has Base Difficulty 3, which seems normal because the game specifies rolls have Base Difficulty 3 when no Difficulty is specified.<br /> <br /> Until you notice Flickering Shadow Evasion (and I believe many other Charms ? Haven't check) have no Difficulty mentioned, so it should assume Base Difficulty 3. Which I don't think is the intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Also, even knowing the Difficulty 3 thing, I'm not totally clear how many dice Teamwork adds, because &quot;roll against Difficulty 3, then count 'any successes you achieve'&quot; isn't really defined. Supposing I attempt teamwork and roll 4 total successes - does my ally get:<br /> (A) 1 die (my extra successes after meeting the difficulty)<br /> (B) 2 dice (1 for meeting the difficulty, plus extra successes)<br /> (C) 4 dice (my total successes rolled - if I'd rolled 2 or fewer, they'd get nothing, but since I succeeded, they get all the successes I &quot;achieved&quot;)<br /> <br /> My best guess is B, because that's how Build Power works, but there doesn't seem to be a matching general rule, or even terminology for &quot;successes from a roll, as distinct from both total successes on that roll and extra successes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T06:07:06-07:00","id":1452314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452310#post1452310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor quibble: EE seems to use the term Overwhelm, rather than OverwhelmING.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sharpshooter's Clever Tricks works that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Indeed. Also, even knowing the Difficulty 3 thing, I'm not totally clear how many dice Teamwork adds, because &quot;roll against Difficulty 3, then count 'any successes you achieve'&quot; isn't really defined. Supposing I attempt teamwork and roll 4 total successes - does my ally get:<br /> (A) 1 die (my extra successes after meeting the difficulty)<br /> (B) 2 dice (1 for meeting the difficulty, plus extra successes)<br /> (C) 4 dice (my total successes rolled - if I'd rolled 2 or fewer, they'd get nothing, but since I succeeded, they get all the successes I &quot;achieved&quot;)<br /> <br /> My best guess is B, because that's how Build Power works, but there doesn't seem to be a matching general rule, or even terminology for &quot;successes from a roll, as distinct from both total successes on that roll and extra successes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goo remark. I'm assuming B as well, since Build Power and Withering Attacks work like that, but if I didn't know this I would assume it's A","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T06:13:58-07:00","id":1452315,"title":"","content":"Neall said at the ExEss playtest on Sunday that James was given the latest document at the start of the Kickstarter, and that's what he'll be releasing. They aren't going to try to update bits and pieces of it and send it to him. So, we'll see the rules as they stood at the beginning of the KS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T07:47:08-07:00","id":1452327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452315#post1452315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall said at the ExEss playtest on Sunday that James was given the latest document at the start of the Kickstarter, and that's what he'll be releasing. They aren't going to try to update bits and pieces of it and send it to him. So, we'll see the rules as they stood at the beginning of the KS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's what I figured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T07:56:51-07:00","id":1452328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452315#post1452315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall said at the ExEss playtest on Sunday that James was given the latest document at the start of the Kickstarter, and that's what he'll be releasing. They aren't going to try to update bits and pieces of it and send it to him. So, we'll see the rules as they stood at the beginning of the KS.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's... unfortunate. A fan-based Erratta document seems required as it stands to play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T08:10:24-07:00","id":1452332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452328#post1452328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's... unfortunate. A fan-based Erratta document seems required as it stands to play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, that's exactly what I was afraid of.<br /> Sure, all the past manuscripts have had things change, but ExEss seems to be taking it to an extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T08:19:12-07:00","id":1452333,"title":"","content":"Since I don't want to derail the Charms thread into another attempt at hashing out general rules (as well as trying to keep the community's efforts to understand this all in one place for future reference, here's my confusion about Flowing/Still modes for Getimians:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Essence</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getimians may activate either Mode of a Charm based on whether or not they are presently Flowing or Still. If the Getimian has a majority of one type of motes, they may access that Mode. A Charm, when used, is always either Flowing or Still; there is no neutral Mode.</div> </div> </div> </div> (1) We don't know what happens if the pools are equal, and there is explicitly no &quot;neutral&quot; version - several Charms either cannot be used or have no effect without modes.<br /> (2) We also don't know whether the game checks the pools before or after paying for the Charm. If I have 3 Flowing 2 Still, then spend 2 Flowing on Icon-Obliterating Passion, which version do I get? (This may be why the other two 2-Mote Charms are oddly lacking in Modes.)<br /> (3) Two Charms (Devil-Queen's Court and Throne Smashing Ambition) refer instead to whether the Getimian <i>used</i> Flowing or Still Motes on the Charm. Either that's from an old version of the rules, or the sidebar which starts the section is, or those two Charms are explicit exceptions to the general rule. I do not know which.<br /> <br /> My current guess is actually that the lack of neutrals means it's always meant to pick a mode based on which Motes you use. I have no textual support for that, it would just be the cleanest to use in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T08:23:40-07:00","id":1452334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452333#post1452333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I don't want to derail the Charms thread into another attempt at hashing out general rules (as well as trying to keep the community's efforts to understand this all in one place for future reference, here's my confusion about Flowing/Still modes for Getimians:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (1) We don't know what happens if the pools are equal, and there is explicitly no &amp;quot;neutral&amp;quot; version - several Charms either cannot be used or have no effect without modes.<br /> (2) We also don't know whether the game checks the pools before or after paying for the Charm. If I have 3 Flowing 2 Still, then spend 2 Flowing on Icon-Obliterating Passion, which version do I get? (This may be why the other two 2-Mote Charms are oddly lacking in Modes.)<br /> (3) Two Charms (Devil-Queen's Court and Throne Smashing Ambition) refer instead to whether the Getimian <i>used</i> Flowing or Still Motes on the Charm. Either that's from an old version of the rules, or the sidebar which starts the section is, or those two Charms are explicit exceptions to the general rule. I do not know which.<br /> <br /> My current guess is actually that the lack of neutrals means it's always meant to pick a mode based on which Motes you use. I have no textual support for that, it would just be the cleanest to use in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>From how I perceived it from the initial text for still and flow is that they can choose eighter mode regardless if one is higher or one lower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T09:18:23-07:00","id":1452338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452333#post1452333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I don't want to derail the Charms thread into another attempt at hashing out general rules (as well as trying to keep the community's efforts to understand this all in one place for future reference, here's my confusion about Flowing/Still modes for Getimians:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (1) We don't know what happens if the pools are equal, and there is explicitly no &quot;neutral&quot; version - several Charms either cannot be used or have no effect without modes.<br /> (2) We also don't know whether the game checks the pools before or after paying for the Charm. If I have 3 Flowing 2 Still, then spend 2 Flowing on Icon-Obliterating Passion, which version do I get? (This may be why the other two 2-Mote Charms are oddly lacking in Modes.)<br /> (3) Two Charms (Devil-Queen's Court and Throne Smashing Ambition) refer instead to whether the Getimian <i>used</i> Flowing or Still Motes on the Charm. Either that's from an old version of the rules, or the sidebar which starts the section is, or those two Charms are explicit exceptions to the general rule. I do not know which.<br /> <br /> My current guess is actually that the lack of neutrals means it's always meant to pick a mode based on which Motes you use. I have no textual support for that, it would just be the cleanest to use in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I presumed this was covered by Getimian Alchemy advantage where they effectively have 2 pools of motes, Flowing and Still, they divide their base mote pool into. So I'd assume it keys off of which of those pools is larger since they get benefits from that specifically and so it probably carries through into how their Still/Flowing charm modes are handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26892-queenofnevers","name":"queenofnevers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26892_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T09:43:47-07:00","id":1452343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>queenofnevers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452338#post1452338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I presumed this was covered by Getimian Alchemy advantage where they effectively have 2 pools of motes, Flowing and Still, they divide their base mote pool into. So I'd assume it keys off of which of those pools is larger since they get benefits from that specifically and so it probably carries through into how their Still/Flowing charm modes are handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only issue with this is that say you have Flowing 1 / Still 4 as your split at Essence 1. When I have all of my motes, I would be considered Still. That means that I could spend my Flowing mote first, always refill it last, and therefore I am always Still...? I'm coming around to the belief that you are in whatever mode of your last Essence expenditure. It just doesn't make sense to me that you can spend motes from one pool and be in the other mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T09:44:15-07:00","id":1452344,"title":"","content":"So, I know the conversation has moved on a bit to specific charms, but I just wanted to bring up Anima, in case I'm missing something or reading something wrong. As written, it seems like every single mote spent contributes to your Anima, compared with 3e where you needed to spend 5 peripheral motes in a single instant to bump your Anima up. This seems...way way faster and harder to avoid building Anima for characters that probably want to keep Anima down, and sets up a pretty strong incentive to not use charms in combat at all, especially if the combat's likely to last more than a few rounds. In base 3e, you have the personal pool to draw from, and you can keep your peripheral spend low, but the choice is always &quot;use less of my cool shit&quot; vs. &quot;use more of my cool shit&quot;. The way it's written in ExEss seems to be &quot;use none of my cool shit&quot; vs. &quot;use some of it&quot; and risk the Wyld Hunt. Charms are kinda the beating heart of Exalted, and so changing the incentive from &quot;be strategic vs. go nuts&quot; to &quot;don't use charms vs. use some&quot; doesn't feel great to me. Am I missing something that makes this less a problem than I think it is? Alternatively (and understanding we don't have the full ruleset), does the system break in any big ways if I just....double (or 1.5x or whatever) the anima threshold values?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4115-flumpet38","name":"flumpet38","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T10:02:10-07:00","id":1452347,"title":"","content":"well for one, Essence doesn't really does charm combos, at most you see one to two charms being used each turn. With the only time you are gonna be noticed is Anima 5+ with 10 being needed to been seen at miles gives you some leeway. At chargen you only get 5 charms so again you pool of possible powers is smaller. Your range of freedom is a lot larger basically","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T10:10:43-07:00","id":1452350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452343#post1452343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only issue with this is that say you have Flowing 1 / Still 4 as your split at Essence 1. When I have all of my motes, I would be considered Still. That means that I could spend my Flowing mote first, always refill it last, and therefore I am always Still...? I'm coming around to the belief that you are in whatever mode of your last Essence expenditure. It just doesn't make sense to me that you can spend motes from one pool and be in the other mode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's not really what I got from reading it? I feel like it's more like you have Flowing 1, Still 4. You are in Still mode. When you use Getimian charms, you get that mode benefit because even if you're at 0 of those 4 motes the higher max of your two pools is Still and thus that's the mode you're in until you reallocate them between sessions as it mentions doing in Getimian Alchemy. I think charms that let you get a benefit from committing specific motes probably breaks that - like Devil-Queen's Court. I'm just interring that from mechanical benefit of their Alchemy being based on which pool is larger and it seems like that doesn't change depending on how full the pool is only which pool is technically larger but I could just be reading into that in a way that seems like off a hassle to manage/track.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's just my interpretation and I could be way off. I do admit it could stand to be cleaned up in both sections on Getimian Alchemy as it isn't really clear what the intent is. Hopefully the devs will clarify somewhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26892-queenofnevers","name":"queenofnevers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26892_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T10:11:47-07:00","id":1452352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>flumpet38</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452344#post1452344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written, it seems like every single mote spent contributes to your Anima, compared with 3e where you needed to spend 5 peripheral motes in a single instant to bump your Anima up. This seems...way way faster and harder to avoid building Anima for characters that probably want to keep Anima down, and sets up a pretty strong incentive to not use charms in combat at all, especially if the combat's likely to last more than a few rounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically correct.<br /> <br /> I think that the desire to have more of a cushion before you flare out to the horizon is why there are now an otherwise-crazy eleven(!) levels of Anima to track. And remember that, so long as you don't go Above Glowing (up through Anima 4), &quot;Storyteller characters don\u2019t immediately notice unless they have a reason to.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, I think that it is deliberate that (other than the dedicated Stealth Castes), it's much harder to keep your Anima down during an intense fight than in 3E, where people are very rarely forced to flare against their wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively (and understanding we don't have the full ruleset), does the system break in any big ways if I just....double (or 1.5x or whatever) the anima threshold values? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure whether you mean &quot;it takes 2 motes at once to raise Anima&quot; (which would essentially make a number of builds never do that) or &quot;there are 20 levels of Anima&quot; (which is somewhat more doable, though you'd obviously have to recalculate anything using Anima as a cost), but either way, the most obvious fallout of this rule is that it becomes much harder for characters to access their anima abilities when they want to.<br /> <br /> My off-the-cuff idea for a hack would be to simply change what Anima values mean, maybe nothing visible at Anima 0-4, a forehead mark and faint glow (which people are mostly too distracted to notice mid-battle, and you can make rolls to hide outside of it) at 5-7, an unmistakable battle aura at 8-9, then the standard miles-high beacon at 10. That would allow most of the same gameplay, but much less visibility.<br /> <br /> You could also try giving out a free Charm modeled after Guarded Mind Meditation, something like:<br /> &quot;Commit 2 motes. The Exalt may hide her anima so long as she does not rise to Bonfire (7+) - or, if you really want to make hiding viable, you could only auto-break dimming at Iconic (10). An anima hidden this way never allows the Exalt the benefits of an Active anima banner.&quot;<br /> <br /> That version offers a tradeoff: if you want all your motes or all your superpowers, you need to &quot;go loud,&quot; but you can operate at slightly-reduced power for a good long time.<br /> <br /> With any of these rules, you may want to consider throwing some extra bonus to Night/Day/Nadir Castes, since everyone gets a lesser version of their most famous schtick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T14:17:14-07:00","id":1452375,"title":"","content":"I think the new Anima stuff is build with the idea to replace Willpower. I think Anima costs are here to replace the WP costs, and so Anima must not be too hard to level or you'll always be running behind in Charms activators.<br /> <br /> Also, if you want less visibility, doing Chejop Kejak suggestion to pass the discrete threshold more towards the 7 instead of 4-5 might be a simple solution","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T02:58:33-07:00","id":1452434,"title":"","content":"I was discussing this with other players, and it seems that Infected Fate is both pretty powerful and easy to abuse.<br /> <br /> Say your circle is fighting Mask of Winters, and you are an essence 3 Getimian. For a down cost of 1 mote each:<br /> - Infected Fate: You circle's Dawn is now your bodyguard. While fighting MoW, he gains what amounts to three dice (or a free excellency), each turn. And then he can place his free excellency over it!<br /> - Infected Fate: Now Mask of Winters is your bodyguard as well! Now he loses 1 success for each action where he acts against it (that is, all of them!). There is no way for him to get rid of it.<br /> <br /> There is no limitation on Infected Fate for being used on other Exalted, and no limitations on it to be used in involuntary targets. This is way too good!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T04:15:29-07:00","id":1452447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452352#post1452352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My off-the-cuff idea for a hack would be to simply change what Anima values mean, maybe nothing visible at Anima 0-4, a forehead mark and faint glow (which people are mostly too distracted to notice mid-battle, and you can make rolls to hide outside of it) at 5-7, an unmistakable battle aura at 8-9, then the standard miles-high beacon at 10. That would allow most of the same gameplay, but much less visibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually pretty sure this take i already how they do it. The manuscript says that you need 5+ Anima for people to actually fully notice your Anathema. Anything below you can pretty much hide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T05:17:58-07:00","id":1452449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452447#post1452447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually pretty sure this take i already how they do it. The manuscript says that you need 5+ Anima for people to actually fully notice your Anathema. Anything below you can pretty much hide.</div> </div> </div> </div>...which is why, in the variant I recommended, you can &quot;pretty much hide&quot; up through 7 Anima, while hiding is perfect and automatic (barring something like All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight) up through 4.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, can I just point out that it's incredibly strange to me that at Anima 1, your Caste Mark becomes visible, but your anima still doesn't count as &quot;active&quot;? Or, conversely, that active effects kick in at Anima 2, not 3? Mostly, I find it odd that there are these different &quot;tiers&quot; of anima, but then there's also this one division in the middle of one of them - if nothing else, it makes the player aid I'm brainstorming up less elegant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T05:20:52-07:00","id":1452450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452449#post1452449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...which is why, in the variant I recommended, you can &quot;pretty much hide&quot; up through 7 Anima, while hiding is perfect and automatic (barring something like All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight) up through 4.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, can I just point out that it's incredibly strange to me that at Anima 1, your Caste Mark becomes visible, but your anima still doesn't count as &quot;active&quot;? Or, conversely, that active effects kick in at Anima 2, not 3? Mostly, I find it odd that there are these different &quot;tiers&quot; of anima, but then there's also this one division in the middle of one of them - if nothing else, it makes the player aid I'm brainstorming up less elegant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I might probably decide to straight up change some of these things, memorizing 7 different tiers for Anima doesn't really interest me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T06:35:39-07:00","id":1452461,"title":"","content":"Maybe even eight!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Essence Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every two points of Anima increases the level of display from Dim to Iconic. At Dim (1-2) the character\u2019s Caste Mark becomes visible. At Glowing (3-4), the character is lit by a soft light. At Burning (5-6) the aura of their anima can light up a room. At Bonfire (7-9) it\u2019s visible from bowshots away. At Iconic (10), it\u2019s visible on the horizon, and it displays an image unique to the character and her personality. At the first three points, Storyteller characters don\u2019t immediately notice unless they have a reason to. Once a character reaches 5 Anima, they can no longer hide their divine nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read &quot;at the first three points&quot; as meaning Dim, Glowing, and the unnamed level of &quot;Anima 0&quot;. But it is possible that they mean &quot;at Anima 1-3, Storyteller characters don\u2019t immediately notice... At Anima 5, hiding it is impossible. <i>And by strong implication, at Anima 4, NPCs will notice it unless you successfully hide it.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> The latter was actually my initial read, since the text does otherwise say &quot;points&quot; when talking about the numerical values and &quot;levels&quot; for the descriptive ones (also, that paragraph doesn't mention &quot;Anima 0&quot; as anything). I currently favor the former - not because I think the text does, but because it's probably wise to resolve ambiguities in a way which seems cleaner in play, and splits fewer Anima levels in half.<br /> <br /> Of course, by that logic, my favored (definitely non-canon) version is probably more like:<br /> Anima 0-2: Dim. There are no visible signs, and characters only get passive anima powers.<br /> Anima 3-4: Glowing. The character is lit by a faint glow (which people will only notice if they're actively looking for it and succeed a somewhat tricky roll), active anima powers come online.<br /> Anima 5-9: Burning. The character's battle aura is impossible to disguise, and visible from range bands away. Their Caste Mark is clearly visible.<br /> Anima 10: Iconic, per usual.<br /> (Also, if you wanna strut, Celestials below Anima 5 can reflexively turn their Caste Mark on/off for free at any time.)<br /> <br /> Four tiers, like in past editions. Gameplay is only slightly affected - the biggest change is not getting active stuff until Anima 3, and if that bugs you, you could move Anima 2 up to Glowing (I kinda like that you need to get a little serious and use more than you recover per scene/round to get the benefit). Unlike the house rules I recommended for stealthy Celestials, this does preserve what I think is the game's intention regarding hiding anima banners, just without the inherent oddness that someone looking at your face could ever miss a glowing forehead sigil (maybe all PCs wear Naruto headbands?) and leaving the exact brightness of Burning more up to interpretation.<br /> <br /> My desire for symmetry does make me want Glowing at 3-5 and Burning at 6-9 (3/3/4 just sits better than 3/2/5), but that is a further change for reasons of aesthetics rather than simplicity, so I'm more conflicted there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T06:49:17-07:00","id":1452467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452449#post1452449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...which is why, in the variant I recommended, you can &amp;quot;pretty much hide&amp;quot; up through 7 Anima, while hiding is perfect and automatic (barring something like All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight) up through 4.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, can I just point out that it's incredibly strange to me that at Anima 1, your Caste Mark becomes visible, but your anima still doesn't count as &amp;quot;active&amp;quot;? Or, conversely, that active effects kick in at Anima 2, not 3? Mostly, I find it odd that there are these different &amp;quot;tiers&amp;quot; of anima, but then there's also this one division in the middle of one of them - if nothing else, it makes the player aid I'm brainstorming up less elegant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah now I get what you mean, yeah makes sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T07:54:47-07:00","id":1452473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452461#post1452461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe even eight!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I read &quot;at the first three points&quot; as meaning Dim, Glowing, and the unnamed level of &quot;Anima 0&quot;. But it is possible that they mean &quot;at Anima 1-3, Storyteller characters don\u2019t immediately notice... At Anima 5, hiding it is impossible. <i>And by strong implication, at Anima 4, NPCs will notice it unless you successfully hide it.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> The latter was actually my initial read, since the text does otherwise say &quot;points&quot; when talking about the numerical values and &quot;levels&quot; for the descriptive ones (also, that paragraph doesn't mention &quot;Anima 0&quot; as anything). I currently favor the former - not because I think the text does, but because it's probably wise to resolve ambiguities in a way which seems cleaner in play, and splits fewer Anima levels in half.<br /> <br /> Of course, by that logic, my favored (definitely non-canon) version is probably more like:<br /> Anima 0-2: Dim. There are no visible signs, and characters only get passive anima powers.<br /> Anima 3-4: Glowing. The character is lit by a faint glow (which people will only notice if they're actively looking for it and succeed a somewhat tricky roll), active anima powers come online.<br /> Anima 5-9: Burning. The character's battle aura is impossible to disguise, and visible from range bands away. Their Caste Mark is clearly visible.<br /> Anima 10: Iconic, per usual.<br /> (Also, if you wanna strut, Celestials below Anima 5 can reflexively turn their Caste Mark on/off for free at any time.)<br /> <br /> Four tiers, like in past editions. Gameplay is only slightly affected - the biggest change is not getting active stuff until Anima 3, and if that bugs you, you could move Anima 2 up to Glowing (I kinda like that you need to get a little serious and use more than you recover per scene/round to get the benefit). Unlike the house rules I recommended for stealthy Celestials, this does preserve what I think is the game's intention regarding hiding anima banners, just without the inherent oddness that someone looking at your face could ever miss a glowing forehead sigil (maybe all PCs wear Naruto headbands?) and leaving the exact brightness of Burning more up to interpretation.<br /> <br /> My desire for symmetry does make me want Glowing at 3-5 and Burning at 6-9 (3/3/4 just sits better than 3/2/5), but that is a further change for reasons of aesthetics rather than simplicity, so I'm more conflicted there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think of the first reading you made because I thought &quot;the first 3 anima levels&quot; could only refer to &quot;Anima 0-2&quot;, but now that you mention it it makes more sense mechanically and is more fluid","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T14:26:39-07:00","id":1452534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452434#post1452434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was discussing this with other players, and it seems that Infected Fate is both pretty powerful and easy to abuse.<br /> <br /> Say your circle is fighting Mask of Winters, and you are an essence 3 Getimian. For a down cost of 1 mote each:<br /> - Infected Fate: You circle's Dawn is now your bodyguard. While fighting MoW, he gains what amounts to three dice (or a free excellency), each turn. And then he can place his free excellency over it!<br /> - Infected Fate: Now Mask of Winters is your bodyguard as well! Now he loses 1 success for each action where he acts against it (that is, all of them!). There is no way for him to get rid of it.<br /> <br /> There is no limitation on Infected Fate for being used on other Exalted, and no limitations on it to be used in involuntary targets. This is way too good!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A couple of things. First, using this on an enemy should require a Unarmed Close Combat roll, similar to the Abyssal mode of Essence-Lending Method.<br /> Second, I think if someone tried to argue that making the Mask of Winters 'my bodyguard' would affect all rolls in combat would get just a laugh in response. If Mask of Winters attacked <i>you</i>, sure. But what about a bodyguard says that they have to play nice with your other bodyguards, say?<br /> <br /> Frankly, Infected Fate is the 'main' ability of the Getimian; I would be loath to nerf it. There are several ways to balance it if you think it's too powerful. Just for starters, require it to cost Essence equal to the target's Essence, or 1 if it's a mortal or extra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T14:30:01-07:00","id":1452535,"title":"","content":"So, new stretch goals have been shown off, and there's something there that worries me: The fact that one of the stretch goals is &quot;We'll pay the writers more.&quot;<br /> <br /> Literally, it's just that. Even if it words it as a bonus, the fact of the matter is is that we (or at least, I) assumed that the writers would automatically be payed more if the Kickstarter does well, makes sense, it's like air-breathing mermaids. Instead, their ability to earn more for their work is now locked behind a paywall, something that didn't need to happen. I'm aware that other Kickstarters do the same thing, but I'm still not a fan of that system for those either. I just don't think that an incentive for donating to the cause should be &quot;we won't pay our writers as much if you don't.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T15:17:44-07:00","id":1452546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452535#post1452535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, new stretch goals have been shown off, and there's something there that worries me: The fact that one of the stretch goals is &amp;quot;We'll pay the writers more.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Literally, it's just that. Even if it words it as a bonus, the fact of the matter is is that we (or at least, I) assumed that the writers would automatically be payed more if the Kickstarter does well, makes sense, it's like air-breathing mermaids. Instead, their ability to earn more for their work is now locked behind a paywall, something that didn't need to happen. I'm aware that other Kickstarters do the same thing, but I'm still not a fan of that system for those either. I just don't think that an incentive for donating to the cause should be &amp;quot;we won't pay our writers as much if you don't.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Writers are paid on a contract basis; they are contracted to write X words at Y cents* a word. As the Kickstarter does well, more stretch goals are unlocked, meaning more words need to be written, meaning more contracts need to go out. A successful Kickstarter gives the writers the chance to be paid more to do more work. <br /> <br /> This stretch goal is a bonus. Literally, a bonus. Additional payment, advice and beyond OPP\u2019s contractual obligations. Especially considering the writers have probably already been paid; the manuscript is late enough in the process that writer\u2019s work should done; it\u2019s an editor and developer game now. <br /> <br /> I suppose the disconnect here is a misunderstanding of how writers get paid. It may make intuitive sense to you, but it isn\u2019t how the industry works. Turns out mermaids have gills, I guess. <br /> <br /> *yes, it is cents. From what I remember, 10 cents a word is standard; some more technical writings can get up to 25 cents a word. I think Dave Brookshaw once got a dollar a word, for something that was due the next day. Writers don\u2019t get paid that much, sadly, but that\u2019s the industry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T15:41:50-07:00","id":1452549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452535#post1452535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, new stretch goals have been shown off, and there's something there that worries me: The fact that one of the stretch goals is &quot;We'll pay the writers more.&quot;<br /> <br /> Literally, it's just that. Even if it words it as a bonus, the fact of the matter is is that we (or at least, I) assumed that the writers would automatically be payed more if the Kickstarter does well, makes sense, it's like air-breathing mermaids. Instead, their ability to earn more for their work is now locked behind a paywall, something that didn't need to happen. I'm aware that other Kickstarters do the same thing, but I'm still not a fan of that system for those either. I just don't think that an incentive for donating to the cause should be &quot;we won't pay our writers as much if you don't.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As a above mentioned the writers are getting a bonus along with getting money from doing the extra work from the stretch goals as one writer puts it as eloquently as possible on a discord post:<br /> <br /> disclaimer we have been paid and we are happy with our pay but YOOO I AM VERY GAY AND I WOULD LIKE A FEW MORE DOLLARS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 06-16-2021, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T17:46:24-07:00","id":1452564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452534#post1452534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of things. First, using this on an enemy should require a Unarmed Close Combat roll, similar to the Abyssal mode of Essence-Lending Method.<br /> Second, I think if someone tried to argue that making the Mask of Winters 'my bodyguard' would affect all rolls in combat would get just a laugh in response. If Mask of Winters attacked <i>you</i>, sure. But what about a bodyguard says that they have to play nice with your other bodyguards, say?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was running that game, the Mask would enthusiastically become your bodyguard, which may not help achieve the goals of the PC. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T20:03:29-07:00","id":1452571,"title":"","content":"Is there an Essence Character Sheet yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T21:01:04-07:00","id":1452576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452571#post1452571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an Essence Character Sheet yet?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not mine but someone from the fan exalted discord channel made this pdf interactive one, there's also multiple character sheets in there one being a google docs chart as well <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/652577291318198316/854924993314160660/Essence_Sheet_New.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/652577291318198316/854924993314160660/Essence_Sheet_New.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/652577291318198316/854924993314160660/Essence_Sheet_New.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/652577291318198316/854924993314160660/Essence_Sheet_New.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T21:25:26-07:00","id":1452578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gareth3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452564#post1452564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was running that game, the Mask would enthusiastically become your bodyguard, which may not help achieve the goals of the PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not your bodyguard is acting against their role by trying to keep you from murdering them is one of those questions which Getimians are already becoming infamous for causing.<br /> <br /> The Chosen of Table Arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T01:40:36-07:00","id":1452593,"title":"","content":"It's kind of strange how the Lintha, of all things, are getting whole stretch goals dedicated to them.<br /> <br /> It's not <i>bad</i>, mind you, just weirdly specific compared to the other stretch goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T02:07:08-07:00","id":1452596,"title":"","content":"I don't even what Lintha is ? What's this ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T02:20:35-07:00","id":1452597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gareth3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452564#post1452564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was running that game, the Mask would enthusiastically become your bodyguard, which may not help achieve the goals of the PC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My objective is to defeat Mask Of Winters. But how would he know he is my bodyguard? The way it's described, the Getimian don't even have to tell him!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T02:49:17-07:00","id":1452601,"title":"","content":"I don't like Stunts (add dices for nothing, my players always forget them, have to track the banked dice), what do you think of : <br /> <br /> a) Removing them straight and simple and decreasing all Difficulties by 1 (with the small caveat that double 9s, 8s or 7 get a small penalty)<br /> <br /> b) Just replace it by standard Willpower points : Use for +1 success, regain one on night sleep or something<br /> <br /> c) Making them like DD5 inspiration or only on instant use, no banking","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T02:56:45-07:00","id":1452602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452596#post1452596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even what Lintha is ? What's this ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In very broad terms: Lintha is a pirate clan/crime family in the West, well biggest and most dangerous pirate clan in the West. Lintha often refers to the family and also people who sign up (usually by paying tribute) to enter the clan. The grandfathers and grandmothers are the family bosses essentially. A good amount of Lintha uses supernatural powers either inherited from breeding with demons like gills or sorcerous powers to control sea monsters, weather, and elementals. Just like the mafia, usually joining the Lintha means that you can't get out (relatively popular background for some exalted and an excuse to break away from the Lintha)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T03:50:12-07:00","id":1452606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452602#post1452602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In very broad terms: Lintha is a pirate clan/crime family in the West, well biggest and most dangerous pirate clan in the West. Lintha often refers to the family and also people who sign up (usually by paying tribute) to enter the clan. The grandfathers and grandmothers are the family bosses essentially. A good amount of Lintha uses supernatural powers either inherited from breeding with demons like gills or sorcerous powers to control sea monsters, weather, and elementals. Just like the mafia, usually joining the Lintha means that you can't get out (relatively popular background for some exalted and an excuse to break away from the Lintha)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks nice explanation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T04:18:07-07:00","id":1452607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452597#post1452597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My objective is to defeat Mask Of Winters. But how would he know he is my bodyguard? The way it's described, the Getimian don't even have to tell him!</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. The Sidereal equivalent has the same problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T04:26:14-07:00","id":1452608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452596#post1452596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even what Lintha is ? What's this ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 101 of the core introduces them in the Southwestern pirate city of <b>Bluehaven</b>. And of course there's more details in earlier editions, but... basically what Eltacolibre said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 06-17-2021, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T07:14:05-07:00","id":1452623,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Lintha thing is super strange. Any Lintha superfans out there who would rather have multiple Lintha-themed additions than one for the Forest Witches or some Third Circle Demon stats, or what have you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gareth3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452607#post1452607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point. The Sidereal equivalent has the same problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, because the Sidereal version doesn't impose any penalties. If you want your target to get the bonus, you'd tell them. If you're subtly manipulating an NPC by making it so they're more successful when they act in a specific role, so over time they do that more, then so be it.<br /> <br /> But the Getimian one is totally different. The conditioning thing it off the table, because it only lasts one scene. It can apply to every role, rather than just one in that scene. It has no text saying that other Fate stuff displaces it, so if all 64 Getimians are in the same room, they can each pile one onto the same person. Oddly, it doesn't require touch, which throws the total lack of resistance mechanics into sharper focus. And, of course, there's a penalty for acting against it, making this a nasty debuff as well as a way to help allies.<br /> <br /> I think the intention must be that 1m for -1 to most actions a target takes for a scene is an aggressive but fair rate for one of your splat's main schticks. There's no way the writers never thought of &quot;follower&quot; or &quot;slave&quot; or any other kind of &quot;do not defy me, and then I tell you not to act&quot; interaction. (This seems pretty strong to be irresistable from where I'm sitting, but they're the ones with playtest time.) It is probably not their intention to have a circle of Getimians each drop those labels onto the same person (-4 successes to everything is a lot of penalty) - I am reporting this, so hopefully Getimian loom stuff will remove other Getimian loom stuff (and maybe also Sidereal Destinies, but that's a more complex question).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T08:08:55-07:00","id":1452632,"title":"","content":"Alright, so the Liminal Charms are a pleasant surprise. They have a nice spread of powers within their themes, while generally managing to be distinct from the Abyssals' deathly shit.<br /> <br /> It's a little awkward that there are both Aspect Modes and Nature Modes named for the Aspects, but the actual execution kind of looks like DB Aura, but better (compared to 3e) and more relevant (compared to XS). The Nature Modes for Last Exhalation of Secrets are especially neat, though I'd like them more as Aspect Modes (so that you could buy them permanently).<br /> Blood Nature looks like it's a lot more accessible than the others, since its self-harm option is the only one that doesn't require any external circumstance to trigger.<br /> <br /> I'm a sucker for meaty unkillable characters, too, so all the options to heal, get extra health, and generally Have Meat are very tempting. If I'm ever playing XS, I'm playing a Liminal.<br /> <br /> More Universal Charm Modes would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-17-2021, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T08:24:36-07:00","id":1452634,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure of how Liminals work : For example, take Corporeal Reformation. If you buy it normally, you only have the Base Effect, and then for a minor milestone you can purchase the Mode of your &quot;Caste&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join 