Exalt can use some water and stone powers. That seems weirder than Frankenstein's monster using some bone powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T05:04:42-07:00","id":1452758,"title":"","content":"I'm really not talking about the thematical consistency but rather the mechanical clarity, where you have the mode of 1 but you must purchase the mode of the others, and it's not the same as the nature of another which you unlock by doing some weird shit and ia available to all, but they all wear almost the same names. I didn't understand at first how it went, but now that I got it it's more clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T06:36:11-07:00","id":1452767,"title":"","content":"That's a good point, I was a bit confused about which were just the normal Mode rules and which were things you switched between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T08:01:33-07:00","id":1452776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452623#post1452623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the intention must be that 1m for -1 to most actions a target takes for a scene is an aggressive but fair rate for one of your splat's main schticks. There's no way the writers never thought of &quot;follower&quot; or &quot;slave&quot; or any other kind of &quot;do not defy me, and then I tell you not to act&quot; interaction. (This seems pretty strong to be irresistable from where I'm sitting, but they're the ones with playtest time.) It is probably not their intention to have a circle of Getimians each drop those labels onto the same person (-4 successes to everything is a lot of penalty) - I am reporting this, so hopefully Getimian loom stuff will remove other Getimian loom stuff (and maybe also Sidereal Destinies, but that's a more complex question).</div> </div> </div> </div>I should think that it would be fair to say that 'Getimian loom stuff' should not stack, because by the very nature of Infected Fate, the Getimian is placing their target into <i>their </i>Origin, effectively replacing what Loom affects them. Since every Getimian's Loom is different, if another Getimian uses Infected Fate on the same target, the second Getimian would be replacing the first Getimian's Loom with his own, and therefore overriding the first effect.<br /> <br /> This would not be the same for the Sidereals, because they are all dealing with the same Loom (the 'real' one from the standpoint of most everyone in Creation except the Getimians). Now, you could easily rule that they don't stack either because the pattern spiders of the Loom can't make them work, but that is a weaker argument, IMO.<br /> <br /> Of course, all of this is a flavor justification, not a mechanical one. On the mechanical side, I would assume that their playtesters have never tried to play a full Circle of Getimians, given realistic limits on playtest time and the number of Exalt types they have to test. Thus, your stacking penalty issue would have been harder to see.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T08:33:15-07:00","id":1452784,"title":"","content":"Respectfully, I've never tried to play a full circle of Getimians, either. This was the very first thing that occurred to me when I read Infected Fate.<br /> <br /> As with most seeming balance concerns in EE, I am uncertain whether this was a simple oversight, or the writers actually think it's okay. They're explicitly not interested in taking balance questions - fair enough, since it's both more important and less subjective to find outright holes in the rules - so I probably won't know for a while, if ever. As an ST, I would certainly rule that Infected Fate doesn't stack.<br /> <br /> But part of learning a new system is talking with strangers about the places where it gives back strange results, so we can either point out fixes each other aren't seeing, or see holes we had previously missed, before someone falls into one during play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T16:19:15-07:00","id":1452830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452767#post1452767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point, I was a bit confused about which were just the normal Mode rules and which were things you switched between.</div> </div> </div> </div> Incidentally, the Liminal Aspect Modes are the only Modes that actually work as described in the Milestones section (that is, you need to purchase them). As a result, Liminals get more out of Personal Milestones than any other splat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452758#post1452758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really not talking about the thematical consistency but rather the mechanical clarity, where you have the mode of 1 but you must purchase the mode of the others, and it's not the same as the nature of another which you unlock by doing some weird shit and ia available to all, but they all wear almost the same names. I didn't understand at first how it went, but now that I got it it's more clear.</div> </div> </div> </div> For extra fun, <b>Life, Death, and Rebirth</b> has effects named for the Aspects that are neither Aspect Modes nor Nature Modes, but something else entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T23:28:48-07:00","id":1452929,"title":"","content":"Hey, quick question for anyone who followed Monica's assorted Actual Plays: can y'all recommend one of those with extensive use of the social system, ideally semi-recent (so the rules will have shifted as little as possible)?<br /> <br /> Looking at the social Charms, I've been forced to conclude that I just do not understand the real-life social contract which EE's influence system was built around, and I'd really appreciate a little context to help me out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T06:27:24-07:00","id":1452946,"title":"","content":"This latest manuscript really affirms my long-held belief that necromancy is vestigial and should be folded wholly into sorcery. Just look at the range of concepts and aesthetics XS sorcery offers you: elemental and demonic pacts, alchemical enlightenment, arcane mathematics, magitech implants, and geomancy; among the spells, we see purifying fire, living wood, dream powers, and cataclysmic demon energies.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, necromancy offers you: soulsteel, obsidian, ghosts, ghosts, mirrors, skeletons, and ghosts. Sorcery, of course, also gets some spooky skeleton energy with Unbreakable Bones of Stone (<i>&quot;her skin becomes ashen and cold&quot;</i> etc.).<br /> <br /> This is not to say that necromancy isn't <i>cool</i>, but that it is fundamentally limited in a way sorcery isn't, and that the gameline's continued insistence that that two disciplines are somehow mirrored and equivalent, like Solars and Abyssals, just isn't true. Never has been, and I'm not sure how it ever could be.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I'm going to just quietly merge them together, going forward. Nothing of value will be lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T07:12:34-07:00","id":1452951,"title":"","content":"I agree about sorcery/necromancy. My plan is to at least downplay the distinction and make necromancy basically a set of alternate shaping rituals and narrative initiations. Then have modes that use the shaping rituals, either broadly (rituals of creation vs rituals of the underworld, as per the universal spells in Essence), or more specifically by individual shaping ritual. There could be a flavorful variant of a spell for someone who Bargained with Mara vs. a Student of the Heptagram vs. a Disciple of the Void. Double down on modes, which is one of the great new sub-systems in Essence in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T07:42:56-07:00","id":1452955,"title":"","content":"So I thought that the Greater Sign of Mercury was<i> ridiculous</i> the first time I saw it but waited to see how Exalted Essence handled fast travel before expressing concerns, but its closest competitor is Barless Gate a Void Circle spell and it absolutely crushes it.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T08:03:54-07:00","id":1452957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452955#post1452955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I thought that the Greater Sign of Mercury was<i> ridiculous</i> the first time I saw it but waited to see how Exalted Essence handled fast travel before expressing concerns, but its closest competitor is Barless Gate a Void Circle spell and it absolutely crushes it.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be, because I still cannot tell whether the Sidereal actually <i>chooses</i> the location, of if they just say &quot;any safe location that I've been to before,&quot; and the ST does the rest.<br /> <br /> Sadly, the first read seems extremely good, and the second extremely niche (you'd only do it to escape a desperate situation, or because you're a jerk who ruins other PCs' plans for fun), so it's a bit of a quandary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T08:13:40-07:00","id":1452958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452957#post1452957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, the first read seems extremely good, and the second extremely niche (you'd only do it to escape a desperate situation, or because you're a jerk who ruins other PCs' plans for fun), so it's a bit of a quandary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Escaping a desparate situation doesn't seem extremely niche to me - we did it a ton with Travel Without Distance in our game. Being able to do it reliably lets you do a ton of sneaky / hit-and-run strategies you couldn't otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T08:24:15-07:00","id":1452959,"title":"","content":"Travel Without Distance is one thing. Being willing to deal with the logistical hurdle of making your way back from <i>any point in Creation or Yu-Shan</i> is quite another.<br /> <br /> (Okay, fine, anywhere that a Chosen of Journies has ever visited before. Probably a long list!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T09:44:57-07:00","id":1452968,"title":"","content":"Unless you use the Greater Sign again in the hopes of ending up somewhere more useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T09:51:59-07:00","id":1452971,"title":"","content":"&quot;Teleport to any random place in multiple worlds in the hopes that it's useful&quot; is the definition of an effect precisely as good as the ST wants it to be, so I don't see that as a concern.<br /> <br /> It's nothing like teleporting your group any <i>specific</i> place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T11:19:18-07:00","id":1452974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1452971#post1452971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Teleport to any random place in multiple worlds in the hopes that it's useful&quot; is the definition of an effect precisely as good as the ST wants it to be, so I don't see that as a concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree to disagree. The problem I've frequently seen with powers that &quot;GM's choice&quot; or &quot;ST veto&quot; as a balancing factor is that they tend to have a predisposition towards a particular outcome rather than sometimes useful but sometimes not.<br /> <br /> Obviously, assuming that is the intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T11:54:07-07:00","id":1452977,"title":"","content":"That's fair. Either way, I'd like to know for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T08:48:11-07:00","id":1453169,"title":"","content":"Alright, looking at the panoply section, I'm seeing one-issue so far.<br /> <br /> One-handed (and to a much lesser extent, paired) are included in amongst the weapon tags. That's fine on its own, but we're told that mundane weapons can have up to two tags, and then the examples seem to include (or mysteriously exclude) these tags in addition to the others. A knife, for instance, is listed as having the concealable and thrown tags, but then also sometimes the paired tag. Mysteriously absent is the one-handed tag, something I'd definitely expect a knife to have.<br /> <br /> It really seems like it ought to be 3 tags for most weapons, or 2 if you really want to differentiate things. I like the general idea of a tag system and a &quot;build your own weapon, here are some examples&quot; approach, but this seems to be applied inconsistently from the sentence at the beginning of the section. If the intention is that the &quot;sometimes (tag)&quot; is a suggestion that might replace one of the others, that isn't super clear in this draft.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Looking at it more thoroughly, it seems like every weapon should have either melee or ranged. Then every melee weapon ought to have one of one-handed or two handed, and then two additional tags on top of that. Honestly, I'm not sure I like that. I think it would be far more elegant to simply remove the two handed tag and only include a one-handed tag. It might seem odd at first, but it then allows one-handed to simply be the bought advantage of getting to use an off-handed weapon/have a hand free. Two handed weapons then naturally have the advantage of getting to have more tags because they aren't &quot;taxed&quot; by taking one-handed. I like the basic idea of this system a lot, but it seems messy right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","user":"Whiskey Jack","date":". 06-22-2021, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T11:44:41-07:00","id":1453189,"title":"","content":"Was there supposed to be a template for Terrestrial Gods? The section for Celestial Gods notes a page number, so logically something SHOULD be there unless it's just referring to the dictionary section at the beginning. Otherwise, I'm going to have to convert the Elemental section over into a Terrestrial God template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T12:03:01-07:00","id":1453192,"title":"","content":"i think that's an error, already noted it down","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T13:15:26-07:00","id":1453202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whiskey Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1453169#post1453169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, looking at the panoply section, I'm seeing one-issue so far...</div> </div> </div> </div>The One-Handed tag reads &quot;A <b>ranged</b> weapon that can be wielded in one hand, leaving the user\u2019s other hand free,&quot; emphasis mine. The intention appears to be that melee weapons default to one hand, and ranged weapons default to two. This isn't totally consistent - axes are apparently always One-Handed, but only sometimes Thrown - but since One-Handed does literally nothing on melee weapons, it's an easy enough tag to ignore.<br /> <br /> The tags still don't quite seem to add up, however. Consider the sai: ignoring Melee, it's got Disarming, Piercing, and &quot;sometimes Paired.&quot; Those tags all have some actual weight, so how can I read this? Do some sais break the tag limit? Do Paired sais lose either Disarming or Piercing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T13:46:17-07:00","id":1453204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1453202#post1453202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The One-Handed tag reads &quot;A <b>ranged</b> weapon that can be wielded in one hand, leaving the user\u2019s other hand free,&quot; emphasis mine. The intention appears to be that melee weapons default to one hand, and ranged weapons default to two. This isn't totally consistent - axes are apparently always One-Handed, but only sometimes Thrown - but since One-Handed does literally nothing on melee weapons, it's an easy enough tag to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof, Thanks. I'm glad I'd missed something there, because I was starting to think that was just silly. I actually like the idea that one-handed is the default, and two-handed is added as a &quot;this is a heavy weapon and does more damage&quot; tag.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1453202#post1453202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tags still don't quite seem to add up, however. Consider the sai: ignoring Melee, it's got Disarming, Piercing, and &quot;sometimes Paired.&quot; Those tags all have some actual weight, so how can I read this? Do some sais break the tag limit? Do Paired sais lose either Disarming or Piercing?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that was what I was noticing in there as well. I think the implication is that some varieties of the weapon might swap out one of the other tags for that less common one, but it's not exactly spelled out in the text. Or perhaps it depends on how you're fighting with the weapon. The game is encouraging you to build your own weapons and to have whatever equipment makes sense for your character at the time. There's no mechanical difference between a twin sai fighter taking an action to switch from an aggressive, paired fighting stance to a more careful disarming stance and the same fighter simply switching from one set of weapons with the piercing and paired tags to a set with disarming and piercing.<br /> <br /> Like a lot of what I've seen in the draft, I really like the ideas here, but it seems like some edge cases need to be cleaned up and clarified. Not a sin during development as long as we see them getting addressed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T14:29:21-07:00","id":1453208,"title":"","content":"So, er, do you buy Evocations, or..?<br /> <br /> The chargen section implies they're free, and they aren't listed among the things you can buy with Milestones, but there isn't actually a... section on Evocations.<br /> <br /> Okay, actually, the hearthstones section says outright that you auto-learn any Evocation you meet the prereqs for. I wish that was clearer, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whiskey Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1453169#post1453169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mysteriously absent is the one-handed tag, something I'd definitely expect a knife to have.</div> </div> </div> </div> Checking the One-Handed tag itself, it's only meant for non-thrown ranged weapons, which default to being two-handed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-22-2021, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T16:26:21-07:00","id":1453213,"title":"","content":"The concept of universal charms is interesting, and I find it kinda funny how quite a few appear to be originally Solar charms. The whole concept does make sense, instead of having each Exalt type just tediously remake basic stuff, they all get a shared set of stuff to do. It's a big shake-up though, so I dunno how others feel about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T16:44:49-07:00","id":1453214,"title":"","content":"I got around to reading a bit of the previews and just skimmed a few of the charms, the sorcery system and the antagonist section.<br /> <br /> I can't agree with most people claiming that the base system got somehow significantly simpler. That may change when I playtest it at some point after the official release, but my first impression was that in most parts the options increased thus adding depth. I like this, but this does not make the game simpler in any form.<br /> <br /> How the split between power and initiative plays out I can't say, but my prediction is that combat isn't significant faster or easier. I may be biased in that case since the proposed rule of &quot;everyone decides when they act&quot; for initiative is a no-go at my table. They will talk endlessly about the most optimal course of action instead of doing stuff dragging a single action over an hour or more. Having one side act and then the other I as a GM dislike heavily. So I'd go with regular initiative, which is just an additional value to keep track of compared to vanilla Ex3 combat, since Power/Initiative aren't the same value anymore.<br /> I like a lot of the changes, I'm interested in the new way hardness/soak are applied, gambits look way better, rush and aim are actually usable and very good and I will try it out expecting it to be a fun system to play with. But -again- I fail to see how it is easier. I suspect that the soak/hardness together with the powercap of 10 makes balancing for the ST a lot easier. So that would be a very big plus for me.<br /> <br /> Ability/Attribute reductions are not simplifications in my book. I never had a player that complained that there are too many or that they are somehow bad for the game. This is a solid &quot;meh&quot; from me. Doesn't make transitioning from one version to the other easier when everything on a base level is different.<br /> <br /> What I really like and appreaciate is the project/venture system. That may change ingame but one uniform system for crafting, travel, bureacracy, etc. is good stuff. There are a lot of examples in the book so comming up with new stuff/complications will be easy enough. I don't know how good the system will be in the end, but I believe it will be a big improvement. And I think I will test it out in my regular Ex3 game.<br /> <br /> Charms are drastically reduced in number and the design is also simplified, reducing complexity. This is where Essence really shines. Everything is a lot more accessible. Concerning balance I can't really speak with authority as I haven't played it and only read a few charms, but the power level seems to be all over the place. I believe the very unclear written Step based attack resolution is also part of that. There is a lot of weird interactions or applications that are not clear or borderline broken, which may or may not be fine. Some charms are just written in a very confusing way. Some charms are just useless.<br /> <br /> I despise the &quot;rest&quot; like DnD mechanics for recovery and will rip them out as soon as I got a grip on the system.<br /> <br /> The social system is a big question mark for me right now. I honestly don't really understand it, but from what I could gather is that I will probably ignore it and do it the Ex3 core way. I dislike virtues. That they can also add to social influence in addition to intimacies makes things more complex, no? The way to &quot;succeed&quot; at a social action is confusing, why would I need to persuade someone with additional successes if my original goal of persuading someone has been met with the difficulty in step 1? This feels like a bad adaption from the Scion 2nd Edition Stunt system.<br /> Also, isn't this the only part of Essence where this mechanic is used? Wasn't the goal to reduce the amount of sub systems instead of increasing them?<br /> Most of the dynamic of 3e Core social influence will still be there I guess (reading and then influencing the opposition) but everything is done in a confusing manner.<br /> As I said I don't really understand it (weird for a simplified system...) so everything above is even more subjective than everything else.<br /> <br /> Can't say anything about naval combat.<br /> <br /> From what I've seen I love the antagonist section. I love the qualities. Very good stuff. Exalted needs more like this.<br /> <br /> What really bothers me. And I mean it bothers me A LOT. Even more than the &quot;rest&quot; mechanics is the new difficulty scale. 3-10 seems absolutely absurd to me. I really hope that somewhere in the preview will be advice for Ex3 Core STs to convert difficulties from the 1-5 scale to the new one. On mechanical level this is a major nerf to everybody. A 5+5 mortal was really worth mentioning, being able to do almost inhumane stuff with a good chance. Now the almost impossible stuff is really almost impossible even for the best of the best and not achievable without the use of divine power.<br /> This is probably the most impactful thing in the whole book.<br /> <br /> I talked about it with my players and we pretty easily agreed that the focus of narration shifted with that change. Before we treated Exalted as a game where failure was the exception. The fun stuff is dealing with the consequences of being successful in almost everything. This changes completely in Essence. Failure becomes a lot more real and common. Especially if my concerns that the boosted dice pools and the frequency in which those can be rolled or be completely ignored through auto-success charms by the players without completely alarming everything in their direction of their presence are a lot less compared to the core become true.<br /> <br /> Our group just had a moment where an Ess4 Solar (280xp or something) failed a Stamina+Resistance check against Arrow Frog Venom causing a chain reaction into crippling injury (death) against a few hundred mortals. Then I think about the new scale, think back and realize that everyone would have been crippled more than once or twice with all the stunts they have pulled. The charms I have yet to read need to do a lot to make an Essence character even comparable capable to an Ex3 Core character. Even more so since Exellencies are now purchases.<br /> <br /> With all that in mind I think Essence is really a whole different game. It makes regular stuff a lot more challenging and I think the designers had a completely different vision of what Exalted should be compared to the authors of the core.<br /> <br /> I'll probably do a little 2-3 session one-shot in the essence 3 area. I'm not convinced yet that more will be fun. For me it sounds less like walking gods trying to save and restore the world from certain destruction or doom it and every other world alltogether and more like &quot;Storyteller DnD but always 2 CR less for the enemy encounter&quot;.<br /> <br /> The base system seems more complex with more fun options, the ST probably needs to put in a lot less work which is really nice, that the whole cast can be played is awesome, charms seem weird on first glance but are a lot easier for players and most of those that I read had really good effects and seemed fun.<br /> But I don't think that the kind of players that really like Essence will like the Core.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T17:30:42-07:00","id":1453216,"title":"","content":"For the 325k stretch goal the companion will include Dragon-Kings, spread the word","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T20:53:26-07:00","id":1453235,"title":"","content":"Quick question--if you're at the pledge level where you get the PDF core essence, does that include the companion PDF as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T21:12:21-07:00","id":1453237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1453235#post1453235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question--if you're at the pledge level where you get the PDF core essence, does that include the companion PDF as well?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;At $70,000 in Funding \u2013 Companion: Pillars of Creation \u2013 A Companion book with more Universal Charms, Evocations, Hearthstones, and warstriders will be created and released in a supplemental PDF, which will be added to the rewards list of all backers receiving the Exalted: Essence PDF.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> (In other words, yes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T23:46:33-07:00","id":1453248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1453189#post1453189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there supposed to be a template for Terrestrial Gods? The section for Celestial Gods notes a page number, so logically something SHOULD be there unless it's just referring to the dictionary section at the beginning. Otherwise, I'm going to have to convert the Elemental section over into a Terrestrial God template.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to tell, it could easily be referring to an earlier chapter. Chapter 1 Welcome to Creation, the Yu-Shan section briefly talks about Terrestrial gods.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T00:57:39-07:00","id":1453251,"title":"","content":"I... thought this was a simplified version. Why is the 8 point combat resolution table here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","name":"Black Paper Moon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar937_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T01:13:25-07:00","id":1453253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Paper Moon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1453251#post1453251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... thought this was a simplified version. Why is the 8 point combat resolution table here?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically the same resolution as in the 3e corebook, just explicated a bit and there's a standardized Coutnerattack step instead of it being unique to every counterattack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T01:28:19-07:00","id":1453255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1453253#post1453253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's basically the same resolution as in the 3e corebook, just explicated a bit and there's a standardized Coutnerattack step instead of it being unique to every counterattack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. That's unfortunate. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","name":"Black Paper Moon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar937_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T03:44:50-07:00","id":1453256,"title":"","content":"I think I can understand the disappointment for a simplified version.<br /> <br /> As a ST I find the new tools much more easy to prep games. I could go 10 NPC's in less than 2 hours using their tools, and I feel they all are unique and tell a different story. That's really what I missed for 3e. <br /> <br /> However, I wished some information was not spread everywhere and back in the book. Trying to make Battlegroups is annoying because you have to jump between the Battlegroup section and the Battlegroup Qualities for example","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T14:09:40-07:00","id":1453309,"title":"","content":"Stretch goal- Dragon Kings and Ochilike<br /> <br /> Am I the only one who doesn't know what an Ochilike is? Are they something new or are they something I just forgot that was in previous editions?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T14:14:18-07:00","id":1453310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1449352-essence-ks-27th-may-21?p=1453309#post1453309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who doesn't know what an Ochilike is? Are they something new or are they something I just forgot that was in previous editions?</div> </div> </div> </div> IRC, they were Dragon Kings who permitted gods to possess them symbiotically, becoming something distantly similar to Exalted for the duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"k